h rules and regulations. Collect and review SBCs, Certificates, SPDs, 5500s, and Wrap Docs.3. Meeting Preparation & Logistics: Create, design, facilitate, and present materials for all client meetings. Including, but not limited to, open enrollment PowerPoints, core meeting deck prep Xplore websites, iPad loading, and printing logistics. Collaborate with clients on AccelerateGo communication strategies as well as assisting clients with other MB value-added resources. Depending on their assigned team. Benefit Specialists may be called upon to independently conduct a full open enrollment presentation.4. Vendor Management: Manage relationships with insurance carriers, third-party administrators, and other benefit providers to ensure seamless service delivery.5. Benefits Administration: Oversee benefit enrollment, changes, and terminations, maintaining accurate records and addressing employee inquiries.6. Technology Utilization: Stay informed on benefits technology platforms clients may utilize to streamline administration and enhance employee and client experiences. Additionally, take full advantage of the Microsoft Office Suite, including Excel, Publisher, and PowerPoint. Follow MB’s renewal workflow in Salesforce8. Quoting Management: Assist Account Managers with the quoting process by preparing presentations and documents, gathering census information, and guiding the client through the market review process.9. Policy Implementation: Manage the implementation of new benefit policies by acting as the liaison between the carrier and the client; assist the client with installation paperwork, terminate any prior policies, and request a deductible credit report and certificate of coverage for the new policy. Qualifications:Bachelor’s degree preferred. Self-starter who will take initiative in meeting client’s needs.Exceptional communication (both oral and written) and interpersonal skills.Client-centric mindset.Detail-oriented with excellent organizational and project management abilities.Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite.Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team.Comfortable presenting in front of groups (once knowledge base is acquired). Thu, 6 Aug 2026 15:36:53 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11279702/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11352324 Auditor Trainee (TAX) or Auditor 1 (TAX) (CID) – Queens County (ID222269) (Full Time - On Site Position in Kew Gardens, NY) at NYS Department of Taxation and Finance Employer: NYS Department of Taxation and Finance \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Auditor 1 (Tax) Duties Description Conduct audits and examinations of taxpayer’s books and records to determine compliance with the various articles of the NYS Tax Law;Develop and maintain working knowledge of the Tax Law, Criminal Tax and Penal Law as well as Department and Criminal Investigations Division (CID) procedures and policies, including the Code of Conduct, Ethics practices and security and confidentiality rules;Communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing, with supervisors and other Department staff, taxpayers and/or their representatives, and prosecutor offices;Develop and maintain skills in computer technology including operation of laptop computers, PCs, and various software and job-related applications;Travel frequently, including both local and overnight within and outside New York State and to locations not accessible by public transportation; and be able to perform field works in non-business hours if necessary;Carry computer equipment and case materials to various field audit sites, training classes, BCMS conferences, etc.Prepare cases for prosecution and assist prosecuting authority;Represent CID and advocate disputed cases at BCMS conferences and Small ClaimsHearings; may participate at hearings as a witness for the Department to assist attorneys from the Department’s Office of Counsel in the resolution of disagreed cases; testify in Grand Jury and Trial in criminal courts;Conduct interviews of witnesses, taxpayers, or subjects under investigation with an investigative team;Perform various special assignments and miscellaneous tasks as requested; andAdhere to the Department's time and attendance rules and regulations. Notes Having a valid NYS license may be a condition of employment in this title, based on geographic location.Work hours, travel, and telecommuting options to be discussed during the interview.Appointment to each level of the traineeship will depend on which minimum qualifications are met. Minimum Qualifications Title: Auditor Trainee 1 (CID)Location: Kew Gardens, NYSchedule: Monday-FridayWork hours: 8:30am-4:30pmSalary: $53,764–$68,630Apply by: 09/05/2026 Title: Auditor Trainee 2 (CID)Location: Kew Gardens, NYSchedule: Monday-FridayWork hours: 8:30am-4:30pmSalary: $59,994–$76,359Apply by: 09/05/2026 Title:  Auditor 1 (CID)Location: Kew Gardens, NYSchedule: Monday-FridayWork hours: 8:30am-4:30pmSalary: $66,951–$85,138Apply by: 09/05/2026 For the Trainee 1 (TAX): You must meet one of the following: Bachelor’s degree including 24 credits in accounting, auditing, or taxation; or Bachelor’s degree including 18 credit hours in accounting, auditing, or taxation and 6 credits in finance, money and banking, economics, or business. For the Trainee 2 (TAX): You must meet one of the following: Bachelor’s degree including 24 credits in accounting, auditing, or taxation and one year experience; or Bachelor’s degree including 18 credit hours in accounting, auditing, or taxation and 6 credits in finance, money and banking, economics, or business and one year of experience; or Bachelor’s degree including 24 credits in accounting, auditing, or taxation and Master’s degree including 15 credit hours in accounting, auditing or taxation; or Bachelor’s degree including 18 credit hours in accounting, auditing, or taxation and 6 credits in finance, money and banking, economics, or business and Master’s degree including 15 credit hours in accounting, auditing or taxation. For the Auditor 1 (TAX): You must meet one of the following: Bachelor’s degree including 24 credits in accounting, auditing, or taxation and two years of experience; or Bachelor’s degree including 18 credit hours in accounting, auditing, or taxation and 6 credits in finance, money and banking, economics, or business and two years of experience; or Bachelor’s degree including 24 credits in accounting, auditing, or taxation and a CPA license in New York State; or Bachelor’s degree including 18 credit hours in accounting, auditing, or taxation and 6 credits in finance, money and banking, economics, or business and a CPA license in New York State; or Bachelor’s degree including 24 credits in accounting, auditing, or taxation and Master’s degree including 15 credit hours in accounting, auditing, or taxation and one-year experience; or Bachelor’s degree including 18 credit hours in accounting, auditing, or taxation and 6 credits in finance, money and banking, economics, or business and Master’s degree including 15 credit hours in accounting, auditing or taxation and one-year experience. How To Apply For more information on the position, view the job announcement (https://statejobs.ny.gov/public/vacancyDetailsView.cfm?id=222269) for Vacancy ID 222269 Apply now using our Web Application (https://www7b.tax.ny.gov/HELP/gateway/HELP.home) Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:14:57 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11352324/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11352385 Auditor Trainee (TAX) or Auditor 1 (TAX) (CID) – Schenectady County (ID222263) (Full Time - On Site Position in Schenectady, NY) at NYS Department of Taxation and Finance Employer: NYS Department of Taxation and Finance \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Auditor 1 (Tax) Duties Description Conduct audits and examinations of taxpayer’s books and records to determine compliance with the various articles of the NYS Tax Law;Develop and maintain working knowledge of the Tax Law, Criminal Tax and Penal Law as well as Department and Criminal Investigations Division (CID) procedures and policies, including the Code of Conduct, Ethics practices and security and confidentiality rules;Communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing, with supervisors and other Department staff, taxpayers and/or their representatives, and prosecutor offices;Develop and maintain skills in computer technology including operation of laptop computers, PCs, and various software and job-related applications;Travel frequently, including both local and overnight within and outside New York State and to locations not accessible by public transportation; and be able to perform field works in non-business hours if necessary;Carry computer equipment and case materials to various field audit sites, training classes, BCMS conferences, etc.Prepare cases for prosecution and assist prosecuting authority;Represent CID and advocate disputed cases at BCMS conferences and Small ClaimsHearings; may participate at hearings as a witness for the Department to assist attorneys from the Department’s Office of Counsel in the resolution of disagreed cases; testify in Grand Jury and Trial in criminal courts;Conduct interviews of witnesses, taxpayers, or subjects under investigation with an investigative team;Perform various special assignments and miscellaneous tasks as requested; andAdhere to the Department's time and attendance rules and regulations. Notes Having a valid NYS license may be a condition of employment in this title, based on geographic location.Work hours, travel, and telecommuting options to be discussed during the interview.Appointment to each level of the traineeship will depend on which minimum qualifications are met. Minimum Qualifications Title: Auditor Trainee 1 (CID)Location: Schenectady, NYSchedule: Monday-FridayWork hours: 8:30am-4:30pmSalary: $53,764–$68,630Apply by: 09/05/2026 Title: Auditor Trainee 2 (CID)Location: Schenectady, NYSchedule: Monday-FridayWork hours: 8:30am-4:30pmSalary: $59,994–$76,359Apply by: 09/05/2026 Title:  Auditor 1 (CID)Location: Schenectady, NYSchedule: Monday-FridayWork hours: 8:30am-4:30pmSalary: $66,951–$85,138Apply by: 09/05/2026 For the Trainee 1 (TAX): You must meet one of the following: Bachelor’s degree including 24 credits in accounting, auditing, or taxation; or Bachelor’s degree including 18 credit hours in accounting, auditing, or taxation and 6 credits in finance, money and banking, economics, or business. For the Trainee 2 (TAX): You must meet one of the following: Bachelor’s degree including 24 credits in accounting, auditing, or taxation and one year experience; or Bachelor’s degree including 18 credit hours in accounting, auditing, or taxation and 6 credits in finance, money and banking, economics, or business and one year of experience; or Bachelor’s degree including 24 credits in accounting, auditing, or taxation and Master’s degree including 15 credit hours in accounting, auditing or taxation; or Bachelor’s degree including 18 credit hours in accounting, auditing, or taxation and 6 credits in finance, money and banking, economics, or business and Master’s degree including 15 credit hours in accounting, auditing or taxation. For the Auditor 1 (TAX): You must meet one of the following: Bachelor’s degree including 24 credits in accounting, auditing, or taxation and two years of experience; or Bachelor’s degree including 18 credit hours in accounting, auditing, or taxation and 6 credits in finance, money and banking, economics, or business and two years of experience; or Bachelor’s degree including 24 credits in accounting, auditing, or taxation and a CPA license in New York State; or Bachelor’s degree including 18 credit hours in accounting, auditing, or taxation and 6 credits in finance, money and banking, economics, or business and a CPA license in New York State; or Bachelor’s degree including 24 credits in accounting, auditing, or taxation and Master’s degree including 15 credit hours in accounting, auditing, or taxation and one-year experience; or Bachelor’s degree including 18 credit hours in accounting, auditing, or taxation and 6 credits in finance, money and banking, economics, or business and Master’s degree including 15 credit hours in accounting, auditing or taxation and one-year experience. How To Apply For more information on the position, view the job announcement (https://statejobs.ny.gov/public/vacancyDetailsView.cfm?id=222263) for Vacancy ID 222263 Apply now using our Web Application (https://www7b.tax.ny.gov/HELP/gateway/HELP.home) Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:22:03 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11352385/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11184291 Firefighter/Paramedic at Fairfax County Fire and Rescue Department (FCFRD) Employer: Fairfax County Fire and Rescue Department (FCFRD) \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Fairfax County Fire and Rescue Department (FCFRD) is the largest Fire Department in the State of Virginia with roughly 1,400 highly trained uniformed personnel. Here at FCFRD, field personnel work one of three 24-hour rotating shifts, including weekends and holidays. The FCFRD staffs 39 fire stations with ALS Engines, ALS Ladder Trucks, ALS Rescue Squads, Tankers, Hazardous Materials unit, Hazardous Materials support unit, and 42 transport units.  Several other types of apparatus, such as Brush Trucks, Boats, and support vehicles supplement the needs of the FCFRD.   At FCFRD we provide training for our Firefighter/Emergency Medical Technician position (EMT). No experience is required, and all training is paid. At the training academy, recruits learn Firefighting and Emergency Medical Services, participate in community risk reduction activities, operate apparatus and equipment, participate in physical fitness training, attend drills and training, maintain, and inspect equipment, and perform other related duties. Additionally, the FCFRD is home to VATF-1/USA-1 (Team 1), part of the Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) response system and one of two internationally deployable Urban Search and Rescue (USAR) Teams in the United States. Starting Salary:  $78,143k for the Firefighter/Paramedic with ALS Certification plus $10k signing bonus! Employee Benefits:  -Paid Entry Level Training 25 Year Retirement + Pension Benefits at 2.5% Final Average Salary  -Diverse Workplace / Above National Average Number of Women -Paid Continuous Training, including Paramedic Program and Other Specialties  -Plus, Many More!  For Advanced Life Support (ALS) Providers:  - 10k SIGNING BONUS!  - Annual ALS Incentive Pay ($7,087) - Hourly ALS Riding Pay $2/$3hr  - Continuing Education Credits Earned while On-Duty Shift   Schedule: - 24hrs ON - 24hrs OFF - 24hrs ON - 24hrs OFF - 24hrs ON - 4 Days OFF   Minimum Requirements: 18 years of age or older Completion of High School Diploma or GED Valid Driver’s License Drug-free for the Last 12 Months No More than Two Moving Infraction in the Last 12 Months Tue, 7 Jul 2026 13:10:05 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11184291/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11279496 Work for NCDOJ, Forensic Scientist, Admin Specialist, Paralegal, Attorney, Etc. at North Carolina Department of Justice┃State Crime Laboratory┃Justice Academy Employer: North Carolina Department of Justice┃State Crime Laboratory┃Justice Academy \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n North Carolina recognizes the value of directly related work experience and does not want the lack of a degree to be a barrier to starting or advancing a state career.  Some state job postings say you can qualify by an “equivalent combination of education and experience.” If that language appears in the job posting, then you may qualify through EITHER years of education OR years of directly related experience, OR a combination of both. See http://www.oshr.nc.gov/experience-guide for details. https://ncdoj.gov/employment/https://ncdoj.gov/crime-lab/crime-laboratory-careers/Apply via Workday Thu, 6 Aug 2026 15:08:15 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11279496/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11281515 Construction Laborer at Civil Site Services Employer: Civil Site Services \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Job Title: Construction LaborerDepartment: Field OperationsReports To: Foreman / SuperintendentPosition SummaryCivil Site Services is seeking a dependable and hardworking Construction Laborer to assist with all phases of heavy civil construction projects. This position supports crews by performing physical labor, operating hand and power tools, maintaining job site safety, and assisting with site preparation, grading, utility installation, concrete work, erosion control, and other construction activities. The ideal candidate has a strong work ethic, values teamwork, and is committed to working safely in a fast-paced outdoor environment.Essential Duties & ResponsibilitiesPerform general labor tasks on heavy civil construction projects.Assist with excavation, grading, trenching, and backfilling operations.Install underground utilities including water, sewer, and storm drainage systems.Prepare job sites by clearing debris, setting up equipment, and organizing materials.Load, unload, and transport construction materials and equipment.Operate hand tools, power tools, compactors, and other construction equipment as directed.Assist with concrete forming, pouring, finishing, and curing.Install erosion and sediment control measures.Direct traffic around work zones when required.Perform site cleanup and maintain a safe, organized work environment.Follow all company safety policies and OSHA regulations.Work effectively with supervisors, equipment operators, and fellow crew members.Perform other duties as assigned.QualificationsHigh school diploma or GED preferred.Previous construction or heavy civil experience preferred but not required.Ability to perform physically demanding work in various weather conditions.Ability to lift and carry up to 75 pounds regularly.Must be dependable, punctual, and willing to learn.Ability to follow verbal and written instructions.Valid driver's license preferred.Reliable transportation to and from job sites.Knowledge, Skills & AbilitiesBasic understanding of construction tools and equipment.Strong work ethic and positive attitude.Ability to work independently and as part of a team.Good communication skills.Strong attention to safety and quality.Ability to work overtime and occasional weekends as project schedules require.Physical RequirementsFrequently lift, carry, push, and pull materials weighing up to 75 pounds.Stand, walk, bend, kneel, crouch, climb, and perform repetitive motions throughout the workday.Work outdoors in varying temperatures and weather conditions.Ability to work around heavy equipment and moving machinery.Work EnvironmentOutdoor construction sites.Exposure to dust, mud, noise, vibration, and changing weather conditions.Use of required personal protective equipment (PPE), including hard hats, safety glasses, gloves, reflective vests, and steel-toed boots.BenefitsCompetitive payHealth, dental, and vision insurancePaid time off and holidaysRetirement savings plan (if applicable)Opportunities for training, advancement, and career growthCivil Site Services is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to providing a safe, productive, and inclusive workplace for all employees. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 19:32:10 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11281515/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11279769 Manager, Enterprise Human Resources at North American Properties Employer: North American Properties \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Position OverviewNorth American is seeking a Manager, Enterprise Human Resources to lead day-to-day HR operations and support the people needs of North American and its affiliated companies.Reporting to the Director, Business Operations, this individual will oversee core HR processes, including onboarding, offboarding, benefits and retirement plan administration, associate relations, performance support, compliance, and associate records. The Manager will work closely with company leaders and external partners to ensure HR practices are consistent, responsive, and aligned with business needs.This position is well suited for an HR professional who combines strong judgment, discretion, organization, and a service-oriented approach with the ability to operate independently in a complex, multi-entity environment. Contributions You Will Make to the TeamHuman Resources Operationso Oversee day-to-day HR operations, processes, documentation, and associate records.o Manage onboarding, employment changes, leaves of absence, and offboarding.o Maintain consistent, efficient, and compliant HR practices across the organization.o Develop and improve HR procedures, templates, communications, and administrative processes.o Partner with EMS and the Director, Business Operations on HR strategy, workforce needs, and organizational priorities.o Advise managers on performance management, associate relations, policy interpretation, documentation, and workplace matters.o Support organizational changes, workforce planning, and other business-driven HR initiatives.Benefits and Retirement Plan Administrationo Oversee 401(k) administration, compliance documentation, associate communications, and coordination with plan partners.o Support benefits administration, enrollment, eligibility, qualifying life events, and associate inquiries.o Coordinate annual activities, including open enrollment, audits, compliance testing, required notices, and plan reporting.o Partner with payroll, benefits, retirement plan, legal, and advisory partners to resolve issues and ensure accurate administration.Associate Relations and Complianceo Provide guidance to associates and managers on policies, performance expectations, workplace practices, and employment matters.o Support performance discussions, coaching, corrective action, and appropriate documentation.o Help ensure compliance with applicable employment laws, company policies, and record-retention requirements.Associate Experience and Special Projectso Support initiatives that strengthen associate engagement, communication, retention, and development.o Assist with performance-management programs, training, recognition, and organizational communications.o Lead or support HR projects involving process improvement, systems, compliance, integrations, or organizational change.o Partner across finance, payroll, IT, operations, and leadership to coordinate HR-related initiatives.o All other responsibilities as assigned. Qualifications & Requirements - What You'll Need to be Successfulo Bachelor’s degree in human resources, business administration, or a related field.o 3-5 years of HR experience, including HR operations, benefits, associate relations, or administration.o Working knowledge of employment laws, HR compliance, benefits administration, and sound employment practices.o Experience advising Supervisors and handling sensitive associate matters with discretion and sound judgment.o Strong organizational, communication, project-management, and problem-solving skills.o Ability to manage multiple priorities, operate independently, and recognize when matters require escalation.o Demonstrated commitment to accuracy, confidentiality, responsiveness, and follow-through.o Proficiency in Microsoft Office and familiarity with HR, payroll, benefits, or applicant-tracking systems.Preferred Qualifications:o PHR, SPHR, SHRM-CP, SHRM-SCP, or comparable professional certification.o Experience working with a professional employer organization or other outsourced HR partners.o Experience supporting multiple businesses, locations, or affiliated companies. BenefitsAt North American, we live our values of Relationships, Ownership, Agility, Strength and Stability, Courage and Creativity, Empowerment, and Integrity. North American and its portfolio companies invest first in people, recognizing that our associates are our greatest assets.Full-time associates receive a competitive compensation package based on experience, a best-in-class benefits package, and opportunities for continued professional development. About North American PropertiesNorth American Properties and its portfolio companies believe that it all comes down to connections—people to each other; cities to their souls; partners to opportunities; and individuals to experiences that move them. We believe that by fulfilling people’s desire for connectedness, we’re creating happier places and experiences that in turn become more successful environments, more vibrant communities and ultimately, a better world. Since 1954, we’ve balanced a well-capitalized approach and a keen focus on successful execution with a willingness to question conventional wisdom, reimagining and expanding the possibilities for more than $7 billion of assets across the US. Whether developing multifamily, mixed-use, office, student housing, hotel or retail environments, we’re driven to deliver more valuable, meaningful real estate and ventures that transform, inspire, delight and succeed by connecting us all with what matters most. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 15:44:13 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11279769/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11281840 Estimator Project Coordinator at Jefferies Kidd Design Build Employer: Jefferies Kidd Design Build \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Company OverviewAt Jefferies & Kidd Design Build, we specialize in creating exceptional custom homes and commercial spaces throughout Coastal North Carolina. We pride ourselves on a seamless, high-end design-build experience. From initial concept to the final walk-through, our team delivers superior craftsmanship, transparent communication, and meticulous project management.Job SummaryWe are seeking a highly organized, proactive Estimator / Project Coordinator to join our team. In this role, you will act as the operational bridge between our design phase and field execution, working directly alongside our Project Managers (PMs). You will be responsible for translating design plans into accurate, competitive cost estimates while simultaneously coordinating the critical behind-the-scenes logistics—such as bidding, subcontractor scheduling, and material procurement—that keep our projects moving smoothly.If you are a detail-oriented professional who loves construction logistics, thrives on keeping projects on schedule, and wants to work with a premier coastal builder, we want to hear from you.Key Responsibilities1. Estimating & Bidding (Pre-Construction)Perform Takeoffs: Conduct detailed material and labor takeoffs from architectural and structural drawings.Manage the Subcontractor Bidding Process: Package and distribute bid invitations to our trusted subcontractor network, utilizing Buildertrend to coordinate submissions, clarify scopes of work, and ensure full coverage.Bid Leveling & Analysis: Analyze and compare incoming subcontractor proposals to ensure accurate pricing, identify gaps, and eliminate hidden costs.Budget Development: Collaborate with the leadership team to compile comprehensive, highly accurate project budgets and cost-plus estimates.2. Project Coordination (Supporting the PMs)PM Partnership: Work hand-in-hand with field Project Managers to ensure a seamless handoff from the estimating phase to active construction.Subcontractor & Vendor Scheduling: Assist PMs in coordinating trade schedules, ensuring subcontractors are locked in and ready to roll per the master Buildertrend schedule.Purchase Orders & Agreements: Generate and track subcontracts, purchase orders (POs), and change orders, ensuring all compliance documents (insurance, licenses) are active.Material Procurement: Source, price, and coordinate the timely delivery of specialized, long-lead materials (such as custom windows, specialized trim packages, and structural components) to prevent job site delays.3. Document & Database ManagementBuildertrend Administration: Serve as a key internal administrator for Buildertrend—maintaining clean project files, updating selection sheets, and tracking bid packages.RFI Tracking: Manage the Request for Information (RFI) process, coordinating between designers, engineers, PMs, and subcontractors to resolve plan discrepancies quickly.Cost Database Updates: Track real-time material pricing fluctuations and historical cost data to keep our pricing models and standard specifications accurate.Required QualificationsEducation: Bachelor’s degree (4-year degree) in Construction Management, Civil Engineering, Business Administration, or a related field.Experience: 2–4 years of experience in residential custom home or light commercial construction, with a focus on estimating, bidding, or project coordination.Technical Skills:Strong proficiency with construction management software—specifically Buildertrend or Procore.Proficiency with digital takeoff software (e.g., On-Screen Takeoff, Bluebeam, PlanSwift).Excellent skills in Microsoft Excel and the Google Workspace suite.Location: Ability to work out of our office and make occasional site visits to active projects in the local coastal area.Key Competencies for SuccessHighly Collaborative: You thrive in a team-first environment and understand how to communicate effectively with field superintendents, subcontractors, designers, and clients alike.Meticulous Organization: You don't let small details slip through the cracks, whether you're reviewing a trim package or organizing a complex bid sheet.Proactive Problem Solver: You anticipate potential scheduling or material supply chain bottlenecks before they impact the job site.Local Coastal Knowledge: Familiarity with coastal building practices, local subcontractor networks, and wind-borne debris/coastal building requirements is a significant plus.What We OfferCompetitive salary based on experience.Paid Time Off (PTO) and paid holidays.A supportive, professional office environment with room for career advancement into Project Management or Lead Estimating.Benefits: Dental insuranceHealth insurancePaid time offProfessional development assistance Work Location: In person Thu, 6 Aug 2026 20:19:26 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11281840/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11007411 Environmental Inspector at LCS, Inc. Employer: LCS, Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n LCS, INC. EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITYGeologist, Environmental Scientist, Environmental AnalystLender Consulting Services, Inc. (LCS) is a risk management consulting firm that provides environmental, construction, and appraisal due diligence consulting services to our clients. While LCS was founded 28 years ago in Buffalo, New York, we currently have offices nationwide, including New York, Pennsylvania, Connecticut, Maryland, Washington DC, Virginia, Tennessee, North Carolina, Florida, Texas, Colorado, and California.As an employee-owned firm, LCS has established a culture of superior customer service and believes in the power of collaboration, expertise, and innovation to elevate services. As we continue to expand our reach and take on new and exciting projects, we are looking for a talented individual who shares our vision and is eager to contribute their skills.Phase II Assessor, Geologist, Environmental Scientist, Environmental Analyst, construction inspector. Our firm has an open position for an experienced environmental and construction inspector to conduct inspections primarily in the Baltimore and Mid-Atlantic area. However, travel outside the Mid-Atlantic area will be required. This position’s primary purpose is to conduct Phase I/II Environmental Site Assessments. This position's secondary purpose is to train to conduct Construction Draw Monitoring and Property Condition Assessments. Please note that this is not an engineering position.LCS’ team of professional and qualified construction monitors, environmental professionals, appraisers, and real estate staff members will provide training. This full-time position may lead to advancement in our growing firm.Skills and Requirements:● BS/BA degree in a related field and excellent organizational, project management, communication, and writing skills.● Team player with the ability to work alone and interact well with property owners, contractors, and the like.● Attention to detail, creative problem solving, and critical thinking.● Ability to analyze regulatory, analytical, historical, and site-specific documentation.● A valid driver’s license and dependable transportation with the ability and willingness to travel outside the immediate NYC area, as requested.● Applicants with applicable experience, a Professional Geologist License, OSHA Construction Training Certificates, OSHA 40-hour HAZWOPER Training, an EPA AHERA Asbestos Inspector Certification, and/or other State Licenses are highly desired, but all are encouraged to apply.This position is a full-time position with salary pay and benefits. Salary is commensurate with experience. Benefits include:● Healthcare coverage with options for dental and vision coverage● Life and disability insurance options● Paid vacation, quarterly personal days, and yearly sick time● “Ownership” under an IRS-qualified Employee Stock Ownership Plan (ESOP)Qualified and interested applicants looking to join LCS’ expanding team are welcome to submit a current resume along with current references to be considered for this opportunity.Job Type: Full-timeBenefits: Dental insuranceFlexible scheduleHealth insurancePaid time offRetirement planVision insurance Education: Bachelor's (Required) Experience: Construction or Environmental Inspection: 2 years (Required) Language: English (Required) License/Certification: Driver's License (Required) Willingness to travel: 50% (Preferred) Work Location: On the road/home office Thu, 30 Apr 2026 18:10:51 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11007411/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11176552 Paralegal - Bucks County at Voce Employer: Voce \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Add Your Voice - Work For UsWe use our voice, and empower you to use yours, to create positive, lasting change in people’s lives. We use our voice because we believe every person should belong and be empowered to thrive.Who We AreOur agency began in 1999 by pioneering a model that is nationally recognized. We believe every child deserves a safe, nurturing permanent home - with a caring and supportive family that makes it possible to grow and thrive.A pioneer in new approaches to achieving permanency for children in foster care, we employ specialized knowledge and a continuum of services to help agencies expedite adoptions and keep families together.To learn more, please visit https://vocetogether.org/expertise/adoption-permanency.htmlAdditionally, with our partner Diakon, we co-administer the Statewide Adoption and Permanency Network (SWAN) program for the Pennsylvania Department of Human Services.To learn more about LSI, SWAN or Diakon, please visit www.diakon-swan.orgSWAN Legal Services Initiative ParalegalsVoce employs paralegals to perform work for the SWAN Legal Services Initiative (LSI), a program that was created to address barriers within the legal process that delay permanency for a child in the child welfare system. LSI paralegals work out of every county's children and youth office. LSI paralegals assist counties with all aspects of the legal process which ensures children are in safe and permanent homes.What You Will ContributeDraft legal documents for solicitor review, including petitions, orders, motions and stipulationsParticipate in county court hearings and pre-hearing conferencesAssist with all aspects of lay and expert witness preparation for testimonyFacilitate and/or train on approved LSI training topicsSupport county best practicesConduct diligent searches to locate parents, relatives or other potential permanency resources or connections for children who are receiving services from, or are in the custody of the county and collaborate with caseworkers regarding all search resultsWhat It Will Take To SucceedGeneral knowledge/work experience in legal or in child welfare and an Associate's degree, Bachelor's degree or paralegal certificate is preferred. A minimum of 5 years of related experience will be considered in lieu of degree and/or certification. We strive to hire motivated professionals with strong organizational and time management skills who will thrive in a dynamic and collaborative work environment.Why Voce - We Invest In YouWe offer a competitive total rewards package that includes:Health insurance with medical spending accounts (employer contribution to the HSA if electing HDHP)Dental, vision, long term disability and accident insuranceThree employer-paid benefits: short term disability insurance, life insurance and Employee Assistance ProgramEmployer contribution equivalent to 6% of your salary to your 401(k)13 paid holidays (including three floating holidays)18 days of PTO in first year of employmentQualified employer participating in Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)Please submit your cover letter and resume to be considered.EOE Thu, 2 Jul 2026 14:27:50 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11176552/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11279417 Kennel Attendant at The Suite Life Employer: The Suite Life \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n The Suite Life is a premier dog daycare and boarding facility where pups enjoy safe, fun, and comfortable stays while their families are away. With 35 spacious suites, five structured playgroups, and personalized care for every dog, we take pride in creating a clean, stress-free environment for our four-legged guests.Our team is dedicated to more than just the basics — we focus on providing enrichment, love, and attention to every dog in our care. From supervised group play to one-on-one cuddle time, we make sure each pup feels like part of our family.Working at The Suite Life means being part of a team that values reliability, responsibility, and a genuine love for dogs. Kennel attendants play an essential role in keeping our facility clean, safe, and fun — ensuring every dog has the best stay possible. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 14:49:12 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11279417/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11281474 Network Administrator - Palo Alto & Juniper at Smart Start Employer: Smart Start \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Network Administrator________________________________________________________DEPARTMENT: Information TechnologyREPORTS TO: IT DirectorFLSA: Full-time, Exempt (Salary) Schedule: Monday-Friday, 8am-5pm (Hybrid) Why You Should Join Us!A comprehensive health plan that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage to ensure you and your family have access to the care you needA 401(k)-retirement plan with a generous company match to help you save for your future and achieve your financial goalsOther fringe benefits including Birthday & Anniversary bonus, company-wide discounts, life insurance, Telemedicine access, short & long-term disability, and more!Positive work environments that offer work/life balance and professional growthMission-driven work making a global impact with local rootsThe opportunity to have hands on work experience with industry leading, innovative technology Position Summary Smart Start is seeking a strong Network Engineer to support and improve our enterprise network infrastructure. This role is responsible for Juniper switching and routing, Palo Alto firewalls, VPN connectivity, site-to-site networking, datacenter connectivity, monitoring, troubleshooting, and production support.This is a hands-on network role. We need someone who can troubleshoot real production issues, work through firewall and routing problems, support critical infrastructure, and help strengthen network reliability and security. Although the primary focus is network engineering, this role may also assist with adjacent systems administration tasks across Windows Server, Active Directory, DNS, DHCP, Hyper-V, and other core infrastructure services in support of production operations Essential Duties and ResponsibilitiesManage and troubleshoot Juniper switching and routing infrastructure.Manage and troubleshoot Palo Alto firewalls, including policies, NAT, VPNs, traffic logs, and HA configurations.Support LAN, WAN, datacenter, remote-site, and third-party connectivity.Troubleshoot production connectivity issues involving firewalls, switches, routers, VPNs, DNS, DHCP, servers, and applications.Use firewall logs, packet captures, routing tables, interface counters, and monitoring tools to diagnose issues.Monitor network availability, circuit health, firewall performance, VPN tunnels, and site connectivity.Plan and complete network changes using maintenance windows, validation steps, and rollback plans.Support firewall rule reviews, network segmentation, vulnerability remediation, and security improvements.Work with vendors and carriers on circuit issues, hardware replacements, firewall support cases, and escalations.Maintain network diagrams, IP addressing, firewall rules, VPN documentation, circuit records, and support procedures.Participate in production support, after-hours maintenance, and on-call rotation.Perform other duties as assigned by the IT Director. Qualifications7+ years of hands-on enterprise network experience required.Strong experience with Juniper networking equipment requiredStrong experience with Palo Alto firewalls requiredExperience with routing, switching, firewalling, VPNs, NAT, segmentation, and high-availability network design required.Experience troubleshooting complex network issues in production environments required.Experience supporting multi-site LAN/WAN environments, datacenter connectivity, remote offices, and redundant circuits required.Experience with packet captures, firewall logs, switch logs, routing tables, and network monitoring tools required.Experience working with vendors, carriers, and technical support providers required.Ability to participate in after-hours maintenance and on-call rotation required.Working systems administration knowledge in Windows Server, Active Directory, DNS, DHCP, or Hyper-V are preferred.Experience with Hyper-V or other virtualization platforms preferred.Experience supporting production application environments preferred.Experience with SolarWinds, FortiMonitor, PRTG, or similar monitoring tools preferred.Familiarity with backups, disaster recovery, vulnerability management, SOC2, ISO, or NIST preferred.PowerShell, scripting, or automation experience preferred.JNCIA, JNCIS, PCNSA, PCNSE, Network+, Security+, or similar certifications preferred. Physical Demands & Work EnvironmentThe physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the functions.While performing the duties of this position, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee frequently is required to use hands or fingers to handle, or feel objects, tools or controls. The employee is occasionally required to stand; walk; sit; reach with hands and arms; climb or balance; and stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl. The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 25 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this position include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, and the ability to adjust focus. The noise level in the work environment is usually moderate.This job description in no way states or implies that these are the only duties to be performed by the employee(s) incumbent in this position. Employees will be required to follow any other job-related instructions and to perform any other job-related duties requested by any person authorized to give instructions or assignments.All duties and responsibilities are essential functions and requirements and are subject to possible modification to reasonably accommodate individuals with disabilities. To perform this job successfully, the incumbents will possess the skills aptitudes and abilities to perform each duty proficiently. Some requirements may exclude individuals who pose a direct threat or significant risk to the health or safety of themselves or others.The requirements listed in this document are the minimum levels of knowledge, skills or abilities. This document does not create an employment contract, implied or otherwise, other than an “at will” relationship.#LI-Hybrid Thu, 6 Aug 2026 19:21:50 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11281474/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11279072 Deputy, Sheriff (Lateral Entry) at Douglas County Employer: Douglas County \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Please download the Personal History Statement (CLICK HERE) in addition to completing your online application. Personal History Statements must be completed and sent to the Douglas County Sheriff's Office prior to interviews being conducted. Deputy Sheriffs perform field and office law enforcement duties. As uniformed or non-uniformed officers, they patrol assigned areas; transport mentally ill persons to appropriate institutions; serve Court Orders; investigate violations of law; apprehend violators; gather and preserve evidence; appear as court witnesses; under Court Order, replevin property; carry out eviction procedures; collect delinquent taxes; conduct Sheriff's sales required by law; investigate accidents and render aid to the public; make reports; book, guard and transport prisoners as required by law and by the Sheriff; provide Court security and supervise civilian employees of the Sheriff's Office when necessary.The work involves responsibility for the protection of life and property; for the prevention, detection and investigation of crime; and for maintaining law and order. The work involves an element of personal danger and may be performed either in plain clothes or in uniform. Specific assignments are received from superior officers and are carried out in accordance with established rules and procedures found in the Standard Operating Procedures of the Sheriff's Office.Deputies must be able to act with good judgment without direct supervision in meeting emergencies. Work is reviewed through reports, inspections and observations of results obtained.Education and Work Experience and Other Requirements:Education:Candidate must have graduated from high school or must possess a certificate that certifies an educational development of at least a high school graduation level (G.E.D).Experience:Applicant must be employed as a sworn law enforcement officer working 100 hours or more per year in this capacity, and maintain an active law enforcement certification. Applicants from a jurisdiction other than the State of Nebraska must complete the Nebraska Law Enforcement Training Center (NLETC) Reciprocity Course within one (1) calendar year of hiring.Applicants who have qualifying Military Police experience will also be considered if they can provide supporting documentation for the reciprocity process.Character:Must be of good character and must not have demonstrated a disregard of the law to such an extent that usefulness, as an employee would be impaired.If adverse information relative to a potential employee's character and/or background is developed during the course of the routine background investigation, the Sheriff will explore this during the verbal interview and make the decision relative to hiring.  Such decision must be consistent with Article V, Section G of the Merit Commission Rules.Physical Demands:Vision of 20/20 uncorrected to 20/20 corrected; normal depth perception; no permanent or ocular abnormality including color blindness.Any indication of organic, active or irreversible disease of the ear shall result in disqualification.  Hearing must be such that the applicant can understandably receive frequencies of normal voice range.Completion of a physical examination by a physician designated by the Commission.Age:Must have attained the age of 21 years at the time of certification from the NLETC.License:Possession of a valid Motor Vehicle Operator's License at the time of application, time of hire, and throughout employment.Douglas County is an EOE - Disability/Veterans Thu, 6 Aug 2026 14:02:58 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11279072/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11280801 Business Growth and Risk Specialist - Raleigh at Insurance Group of America Employer: Insurance Group of America \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Business Growth and Risk SpecialistInsurance Group of America (IGA)Full-Time | Salary | Growth Track | BenefitsFLSA Classification: Exempt About the OpportunityCommercial insurance is one of the most stable, high-earning, and recession-proof sectors in the country. Every business needs it, it’s required by law, and it renews annually. IGA operates in a unique niche within this industry, working directly with contractors to help them secure the bonding capacity and risk structure they need to grow their companies.This role is ideal for candidates interested in business, finance, risk management, and long-term client relationships. It combines analytical work, business development, and strategic advising within a career path that offers significant long-term financial upside. What You’ll DoAs a Business Growth and Risk Specialist, you’ll support contractors as they grow — helping them understand their financial position, expand their bidding capacity, and structure their risk programs effectively.Your responsibilities include:Developing a pipeline of contractor relationships through proactive outreachIntroducing IGA’s specialized services to prospective clientsLearning how to evaluate contractor financials and creditworthinessHelping clients secure payment and performance bondsAdvising clients on growth strategies, bidding opportunities, and risk structureCoordinating with underwriting partners on behalf of clientsBuilding and managing a long-term book of businessBecoming a trusted advisor as clients scale their operationsBusiness development is a normal part of the early career. Over time, the role becomes increasingly advisory, relationship-driven, and strategic. Why This Role MattersContractors cannot bid or win major public projects without the bonding capacity you help them secure. Because IGA solves the hardest problem contractors face, our team maintains a close ratio above 90 percent — far above industry standards.You will directly impact the growth, stability, and long-term success of contractor businesses. What You Can ExpectComprehensive training in commercial risk, financial analysis, and bondingWeekly mentorship from industry experts and senior leadershipA clear progression path toward owning your own client portfolioA performance-based compensation model with strong long-term upsideA career with compounding income, year over yearThis is a long-term career path, not a short-term position. Who Thrives HereThe people who excel in this role:Are internally motivated and competitiveThink like business ownersCommunicate clearly and build trust quicklyEnjoy solving business and financial challengesWant both autonomy and long-term earning potentialAre interested in business development and relationship-buildingBusiness, finance, economics, and entrepreneurship backgrounds tend to perform extremely well, but the degree is not mandatory. RequirementsBachelor’s degree preferred but not requiredStrong communication and analytical skillsAbility to work independently and manage your own goalsInterest in business development and long-term client relationshipsPhysical Requirements:· Remaining in a stationary position, often standing or sitting for prolonged periods. (Constantly)· Communication with others to exchange information. (Constantly)· Repeating motions that may include the wrists, hands, and/or fingers. (Constantly)· Speech and hearing are sufficient for in-person and telephone communications. (Constantly)· Vision sufficient for the use of a computer monitor. (Constantly)· Assessing the accuracy, neatness and thoroughness of the work assigned. (Constantly)· Sedentary work that primarily involves sitting/standing. (Constantly)· Light work that includes moving objects up to 20 pounds. (Occasionally) Next Steps:Complete a short Grit Assessment used to determine long-term success indicators.How to ApplySubmit your resume through Handshake.Qualified candidates will be contacted to schedule the initial phone call. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 17:53:39 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11280801/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11282418 Registered Professional Land Surveyor at Goodwin - Lasiter - Strong Employer: Goodwin - Lasiter - Strong \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n GLS offers a competitive salary and a comprehensive benefits package including medical/dental/vision insurance, continuing education assistance, 401K and year-end bonus potential. We are committed to providing our team with the tools, resources and support they need to succeed. If you are ready to take your career to the next level and join a dynamic team of professionals, we invite you to apply for the Senior Project Manager, Registered Professional Land Surveyor position at any one of the following locations: Bryan/College Station, Lufkin, Groesbeck or Waco.ResponsibilitiesManage survey department staff and schedules, ensuring that all survey deliverables meet quality standards.Oversee business development activities, including proposal preparation and project management.Interact with clients and staff on technical matters related to surveying.Conduct property boundary surveys and provide legal descriptions for use in deeds, leases, or other legal documents.Collaborate with project team members, including architects, engineers, and other RPLS.Coordinate activities of field crews, including providing job assignments, information, direction, and daily checking of work product.Review and process the results of field surveys, including the shape, contour, location, elevation, and dimensions of land features and structures. Verify the accuracy of field data, including measurements and calculations conducted at survey sites.QualificationsCurrent Texas RPLS.2+ years of relevant land survey experience, including field staff management experience.Working knowledge of field instrumentation Trimble, GPS, and robotic total stations.Intermediate knowledge of relevant technical software, including Civil 3D and MicroSurvey.Proficient in Microsoft Products.Must be able to maintain a budget and relationships with clients.Excellent cooperative skills in working efficiently with a team, assisting with the training of survey personnel, coordination of field work, and leading others in accomplishing work activities. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 22:03:19 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11282418/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11280108 Physical Damage Appraiser at Texas Farm Bureau Employer: Texas Farm Bureau \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n This position is responsible for inspecting and appraising vehicles in order to properly assess the damages and complete a thorough, accurate, and competitive estimate or total loss inspection in a timely manner consistent with department goals. MAJOR RESPONSIBILITIES AND AUTHORITY Complete all daily and monthly assignments in a timely manner. Maintain all forms and equipment assigned, including but not limited to, company car, calculator, camera, automated estimating systems, computer, printer, company cell phone.Submit completed appraisal report and supporting documentation to the appropriate Claims Representative within the department cycle time goal.Complete the repair estimate in the field when at all possible, and review it with the repair facility and/or owner.Inspect vehicles and complete supplements as required.Update the Claims Representatives, peers, and Physical Damage Manager on any changes or updates in the auto repair industry, or in your local area of responsibility, as appropriate.Maintain relations with all other professions in the auto repair and insurance industries, as well as maintain a high standard of ethical behavior in all professional relationships.Report any Underwriting matters or evidence of external fraud to the Physical Damage Manager.Evaluate and document the Actual Cash Value (ACV) of any vehicle determined to be a total loss according to company procedure.Demonstrate willingness to assist with or participate in pilot programs at the direction of Physical Damage Manager.Assist in the training of newly hired Claim Representatives and Physical Damage Appraisers. Willingness to mentor newly hired adjusters and appraisers.Assist in the development and presentation of training courses and modules for team, district, regional and statewide meetings as directed by Physical Damage managers and/or State Physical Damage Manager.Attend all team, region and statewide training as directed by the respective Physical Damage Manager or State Physical Damage Manager.Comply with the Certified Fleet Operator requirements of the Company Driving and Safety Policy.Properly care for and maintain company properly including car, cell phone, computer, etc.Other duties as assigned. MINIMUM POSITION QUALIFICATIONS High school diploma or equivalent.3-5 years’ experience in physical damage appraising for an insurance company or as a body shop appraiser or manager.All Lines Adjuster license from the Texas Department of Insurance, maintained according to the licensing requirements set forth by the state of Texas; or have the ability to obtain such license in a reasonable period.Ability to develop high competence level and utilization of computer-based estimatics platform.Ability to develop strong knowledge of company computer applications, including the internet.Effective interpersonal verbal skills, both face-to-face and over the phone.Effective typing/keyboarding skills.Effective organizational skills.Ability to plan, organize, and complete detailed work independently or in a team environment.Willing to travel as required. Valid Texas driver’s license and driving record at the time of hire which would not place the employee on probation, or disqualify the employee from Certified Fleet Operator status under the Company Driving and Safety Policy. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Use of PC, telephone, copy machine, fax, and other office equipment over six (6) hours per day. Extended periods of sitting and concentration.Occasional bending, twisting, crouching, pulling, pushing, lifting, and moving items weighing up to 30 lbs. WORKING CONDITIONS Occasional long, irregular hours.Travel, including overnight travel, as required.Work to be conducted in office environment owned or leased by the company; or from a secure residential office. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 16:33:06 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11280108/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11279962 Staff Accountant at B.O.T.H. Solutions Houston Employer: B.O.T.H. Solutions Houston \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Staff Accountant (Entry Level)Location: Houston, TXPosition: Full-Time, On-Site (Not Remote)Start Your Accounting Career With UsWe're looking for a motivated Staff Accountant to join our growing team. Whether you're a recent accounting graduate or have up to two years of experience, this is an opportunity to build a strong accounting foundation while working with a diverse portfolio of hospitality clients.You'll receive hands-on training, mentorship, and increasing responsibility as your skills develop.This is a full-time, on-site position in Houston.Responsibilities• Perform bank and credit card reconciliations • Prepare and post journal entries • Assist with month-end and year-end close • Maintain accurate accounting records • Assist with financial reporting and account analysis • Support accounts payable and accounts receivable as needed • Work with multiple restaurant and hospitality clients • Assist with special projects and process improvements  Qualifications• Bachelor's degree in Accounting (or graduating within the next few months) • 0–2 years of accounting experience • Strong attention to detail and organizational skills • Proficiency in Microsoft Excel • QuickBooks experience is a plus, but not required • Strong communication and interpersonal skills • Eagerness to learn and grow professionally  Why Join Us?Instead of working with just one company, you'll gain experience supporting a variety of restaurants and hospitality businesses. This provides exposure to different operating models, accounting challenges, and financial reporting needs while building a well-rounded skill set. This position is ideal for someone who wants to build a long-term career in accounting and is looking for an environment where they can continue learning, develop professionally, and take on more responsibility over time. Benefits• Competitive salary • Employer-paid medical and dental insurance • 401(k) retirement plan • Paid time off • Ongoing mentorship and training • Opportunities for professional growth and advancement Thu, 6 Aug 2026 16:21:30 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11279962/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11280078 Field Customer Care Representative Trainee at Texas Farm Bureau Employer: Texas Farm Bureau \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n This position provides prompt, courteous, and knowledgeable service to earn members’ and policyholders' trust and satisfaction, while supporting County Farm Bureau operations. MAJOR RESPONSIBILIITES AND AUTHORITY Provide prompt, professional, and courteous service to members and insureds in person, by phone, and through electronic channels. Ensure every interaction reflects the organization’s commitment to excellence in customer care.Assist in promoting and executing the core County Farm Bureau purpose activities. Place high priority on assisting the CFB President and Board members with duties related to the promotion of agriculture, including Board activities and general office and clerical support as directed.Dedicate available time to understanding and mastering material for the General Lines Property and Casualty license exam. Collaborate with team members and cross-train in various roles to ensure the seamless completion of daily tasks, especially in the absence of colleagues.Assist the applicant with the membership application.Observe the preparation of daily deposits in accordance with established guidelines and procedures. Review the Delinquent Membership report daily and contact members to assist with membership renewal, updates to membership data, and payment.Exercise good judgment and maintain confidentiality when handling critical and sensitive information, records, and reports regarding the county, members, and insureds. Discuss with the CAAP Supervisor and, when needed, the Agency Manager, issues, problems, or needs within the county offices.Comply with the Certified Fleet operator requirements of the Driving and Safety Policy.Other duties as may be assigned. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS High School Diploma or GED.Obtain and maintain General Lines Property and Casualty license pursuant to Texas law. Must be acquired within 45 days of employment.Ability to type a minimum of 45 WPM with a maximum of 5% errors.Basic knowledge and experience with Microsoft Office software, including Word, Outlook, PowerPoint, and Excel.Excellent communication skills, both written and oral.Effective interpersonal verbal skills, in person and via telephone.Ability to plan, organize, and complete detailed work independently or in a team environment.Strong organizational skills with the ability to coordinate several tasks at the same time.Willing and able to learn new skills and refine existing skills as needed.Valid Texas driver’s license and driving record at the time of hire which would not disqualify the employee from driving for business purposes. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Use of computer, telephone, copy machine, fax machine, scanner, and other office equipment over six (6) hours daily.Extended periods of sitting and concentration.Occasional bending, twisting, crouching, pulling, pushing, lifting, and reaching in an office environment.Occasional lifting and moving items weighing up to 30 lbs. Occasional travel by auto or other public transportation. WORKING CONDITIONS Occasional long, irregular work hours.Work to be conducted in office environment owned or leased by company. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 16:30:12 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11280078/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11282508 Heavy Civil Estimator and Project Controls Specialist at Miller Construction Company, Inc. Employer: Miller Construction Company, Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n About the RoleAre you ready to take your technical construction skills to the next level? We are a well-established and growing heavy civil construction firm based in East Texas, specializing in large-scale utilities and dirt work projects.We are seeking a driven, detail-oriented Estimator & Project Controls Specialist to join our team. This role bridges the gap between preconstruction strategy and real-world project execution. Working closely with executive leadership and project managers, you will be heavily involved in winning bids and tracking project performance from start to finish.What You Will DoCore Estimating: Perform detailed physical and digital take-offs from civil plans and blueprints. Build bottom-up estimates and prepare comprehensive bid packages.Preconstruction Planning: Assist in analyzing project risk, evaluating site conditions, and coordinating with engineers and vendors before boots hit the ground.Project Controls & Tracking: Monitor project budgets, analyze variances between estimated costs and actual field costs, and implement controls to keep projects profitable.Scheduling: Develop and maintain detailed project schedules (CPM/Bar Charts) to ensure tight deadlines and milestones are met.Required QualificationsThe Right Foundation: A degree in Construction Management, Civil Engineering, or significant hands-on field experience with an aptitude for numbers.Estimating Strength: Must demonstrate strong structural/mathematical thinking, blue-print reading skills, and familiarity with estimating software (HCSS, B2W, Excel, etc.).Operational Mindset: An understanding of project scheduling, cost-tracking, and how project controls impact the field.Core Skills: Excellent attention to detail, strong communication skills, and the ability to work collaboratively within a fast-paced team environment.Why Join Us?Direct Mentorship: Work directly with company executives and veteran project managers—no corporate red tape.Competitive Compensation: Pay is highly competitive and commensurate with your experience level.Benefits: 401(k) retirement plan, health insurance, and Paid Time Off (PTO).The East Texas Advantage: Enjoy a high quality of life with a low cost of living in East Texas—no state income tax and affordable housing.Relocation Support: We look for top talent across the country and provide relocation assistance to help you transition to the Longview area. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 22:28:55 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11282508/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11280747 Business Growth and Risk Specialist - Atlanta at Insurance Group of America Employer: Insurance Group of America \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Business Growth and Risk SpecialistInsurance Group of America (IGA)Full-Time | Salary | Growth Track | BenefitsFLSA Classification: Exempt About the OpportunityCommercial insurance is one of the most stable, high-earning, and recession-proof sectors in the country. Every business needs it, it’s required by law, and it renews annually. IGA operates in a unique niche within this industry, working directly with contractors to h