nesty and integrity in every aspect of our business. We are open with our employees, transparent with our customers, and loyal to the communities in which we serve. While Lamar is a large company, each office has its own culture and family atmosphere, making employees feel connected both locally and nationally.We are committed to sustainable and environmentally friendly business practices and use a number of innovative strategies to reduce our environmental impact. Please click here to learn more about Lamar's green initiatives. Lamar is an EEO/AA employer including Individuals with Disabilities, Protected Veterans, and any other State or Federally protected characteristic.Please note: Lamar Advertising does not sponsor or take over sponsorship of a work visa. Only candidates with U.S. work authorization not requiring sponsorship will be considered for employment.SMS and Email Communications: By providing your contact information and submitting this form, you agree to receive email and SMS communications from Lamar Advertising Company regarding job opportunities, hiring events, and career-related updates. Message and data rates may apply. You can opt out at any time by emailing recruiting@lamar.com or replying 'STOP' to text messages. Your information will be processed in accordance with our privacy policy.Disability Self-Identification: When applying for a job with Lamar, you will be asked to voluntarily self-identify whether you have a disability. Please take a moment to watch this video for clarification on why we're asking for this information!California Residents - Lamar collects personal information in the ordinary course of considering job applicants. This information may include, for example, name, address, phone number and other contact information, employment history and reference contact information, and any other information provided by an applicant to Lamar.  By submitting an application, you consent to the use or sharing of this personal information solely for the purpose of consideration for employment by Lamar.  Lamar will not sell this information.#PrioritySales #EarlyTalent Wed, 5 Aug 2026 14:12:58 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11274877/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11279012 CNC Machine Operator at Horizon Machine Inc. Employer: Horizon Machine Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n CNC MACHINISTHorizon Machine, Inc. provides manufacturing for leading companies in the defense, shooting, and hunting communities as well as manufacturing our own separate line of products including bolt actions and suppressors. We employ individuals with backgrounds in machining, gunsmithing, mechanical design, accounting, business management, and those who have a willingness to learn. Everyday we are designing and manufacturing new parts and products to advance the industry.We are always looking for driven and talented CNC Machinists. Applicants with basic or advanced understanding of machining will be reviewed.We are looking for:-Technical degrees in machining/manufacturing or equivalent work experience-Work experience with Okuma, Doosan, DMG Mori, and Haas machines-CNC Programming skills-Able to read and edit code (G and M Code)-Adequate measuring skills (micrometer, dial caliper)-Basic machine maintenance and setup-Understand basic geometry and trigonometry-Calculate metric and imperial measurements-Ability to read prints / technical drawings-Attention to detail-Not afraid to ask questions!Benefits:-Paid Holidays, Paid vacation, Paid sick leave-Group Health-Simple IRA Matching Contribution Mon, 10 Aug 2026 19:56:27 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11279012/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11280761 Nuclear Medicine Technologist at Saint Alphonsus Health System Employer: Saint Alphonsus Health System \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n 💼 About the RoleSaint Alphonsus Health System is seeking a skilled and compassionate Nuclear Medicine Technologist to join our team in Boise, Idaho, Nampa, Idaho and Ontario, Oregon. In this role, you will operate nuclear scintillation equipment to produce diagnostic images, administer radiopharmaceuticals, and ensure patient safety and comfort throughout the imaging process. 📋 QualificationsCompletion of an accredited Nuclear Medicine Technologist program.  Certification by NMTCB or ARRT in Nuclear Medicine. 🌟 Why Join Us?Benefits start Day One: Medical, Dental, Vision, PTO, Life Insurance, Disability.Retirement savings plan with employer match.Tuition reimbursement and career development opportunities.Work within one of the largest Catholic healthcare systems.Supportive team environment and referral bonus program. 📨 Apply TodayIf you're passionate about patient care and nuclear medicine, we’d love to hear from you! Thu, 6 Aug 2026 17:32:41 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11280761/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11281411 G1-G2 Math Teacher at Think Academy US - TAL Education Group Employer: Think Academy US - TAL Education Group \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Start: August 2026Job Type: Full-Time (30–40 hours/week, W2)Compensation: $35-40/hour for teaching + $16–20/hour for non-teaching/admin timeJoin Think Academy as a full-time G1-G2 Math Teacher. Teach with a structured, high-quality curriculum, receive paid training, and grow into long-term teaching and curriculum roles. We're especially looking for candidates with the potential to grow into a Grade Leader role, taking on teacher mentorship and grade-level management responsibilities as they develop. This is a long-term teaching opportunity — not a short-term tutoring role.About Think AcademyThink Academy US, a wholly owned subsidiary of TAL Education Group (NYSE: TAL), is a leading education company dedicated to helping K–12 students build strong academic foundations, confidence in math, and long-term learning ability through high-quality teaching and thoughtfully designed curriculum.Why This Role Is DifferentMost teaching roles expect you to build everything yourself. Here, you teach within a structured instructional system — curriculum, lesson materials, training, and team support are already in place, so you can focus on teaching quality and student growth instead of building materials from scratch.Stronger Teaching Support — high-quality curriculum and lesson materials, structured onboarding, ongoing training, and a team to collaborate with instead of teaching in isolationA Path to Grade Leader — this role is designed as a talent pipeline for our G1-G2 team. Strong performers may be considered for Grade Leader responsibilities within their first several months, taking on teacher coaching, standard-setting, and grade-level coordinationCompetitive, Growing Earnings — paid for both teaching and non-teaching work, with performance-based raises up to 3 times a year, and an end-of-semester commissionWhat You'll DoTeach G1-G2 math in a clear, engaging, kids-friendly way, using our curriculum, lesson materials, and instructional guidance.Lead virtual classes with strong classroom energy, patience, and the ability to hold young students' attention and engagement. Create a warm, positive, high-expectation learning environment suited to early learnersGrade homework, give timely feedback, and communicate proactively and professionally with parents about progress, classroom behavior, and learning habits.Deeply understand each lesson's teaching goals and common student sticking points, rather than simply following slidesParticipate in training, lesson prep, and ongoing professional development; take feedback well and continuously refine your teaching and service habitsSchedule & CommitmentOnboarding starts August 2026; teaching begins September 2026~3-6 classes/week (6-12 teaching hours), plus admin hours (grading, prep, parent comms) — total 30-40 hrs/weekClass windows (Pacific Time): Wed-Fri, 4pm-8pm and Sat-Sun, 9am-8pmOnce classes are assigned, your schedule stays consistent week to week (except federal holidays)Commit to at least one year (till May 2027)Relocation potential: for candidates on the Grade Leader track, we'd like you to be able to relocate to our Bay Area office between November and January, contingent on strong performance in your first few monthsCompensation & BenefitsTeaching Hours: $35-40/hourNon-Teaching/Admin Hours: $16-20/hour (grading, class prep, parent communication)Performance-based pay increases up to 3 times per year, plus end-of-semester commission targeted at 15-30% of total teaching compensationBenefits: 401(k), health/dental/vision insurance (based on eligibility)Visa sponsorship may be considered for long-term, high-performing teachersWho We're Looking ForBachelor's degree or higher from an accredited college or universityStrong math foundation, comfortable with U.S. Elementary School math content or above; Education, Child Development, Math Education, Psychology, or related majors preferredFluent, confident English instruction skills, plus the ability to communicate clearly and professionally with parents and internal team members in Chinese or bilinguallyMeaningful prior experience with young learners (tutoring, camp teaching, after-school programs, classroom teaching, mentoring). Bonus points for prior online teaching experienceStrong service mindset: proactive, comfortable initiating communication with parents, students, and the team, not just delivering lessonsOpen to feedback, self-reflective, and able to quickly adjust your teaching and service approachGenuinely interested in a long-term teaching career and growth at Think AcademyAvailable during the class windows above; available on at least one weekend dayCandidates based in or open to relocating to the Bay Area preferredBonus points for candidates with experience as a team lead, mentor, or TA lead; math competition background; curriculum design or teacher training experience  Think Academy is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, or protected veteran status, and will not be discriminated against on the basis of disability. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 19:22:04 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11281411/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11282618 Stay Housed LA Intake Supervisor – Client Intake Workgroup at Legal Aid Foundation of Los Angeles Employer: Legal Aid Foundation of Los Angeles \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n POSITION: Stay Housed LA Intake Supervisor – Client Intake WorkgroupLOCATION: TBD* (see note)SALARY: $70,500k - $90,000k/annually DOE, with excellent benefitsAVAILABILITY: ImmediatelyAPPLICATION DEADLINE: Continuous until position is filled. Are you interested in joining an organization dedicated to increasing access to justice while addressing systemic inequities among the most vulnerable members of the Greater Los Angeles area? If yes, LAFLA is the place for you! The Organization: LAFLA is a nonprofit law firm that protects and advances the rights of the most underserved—leveling the playing field and ensuring that everyone can have access to the justice system. Celebrating 95 years of service to Los Angeles communities, LAFLA is the first and most experienced legal aid organization in Greater Los Angeles. LAFLA has more than 200 employees, including more than 100 attorneys, who provide free services and resources on a broad range of civil legal issues that impact healthy, safety, and self-sufficiency. Every year, LAFLA helps more than 100,000 people find their voice, regain control of their lives, and build a brighter future. Our unique combination of neighborhood offices, self-help centers at courthouses, and domestic violence clinics puts LAFLA on the frontlines in communities at the forefront of change. LAFLA also engages in impact litigation to help enact long-term systemic change—actively collaborating with a network of public and private partners to expand access to justice, identify needs in the communities we serve, and change laws and policies that adversely affect the underserved. For more information, please visit www.lafla.org. The Coalition: Stay Housed LA is a multi-organizational coalition that brings much-needed tenants’ rights resources to renters in Los Angeles County communities and may be the first step towards a “Right to Counsel” for tenants facing evictions. LAFLA’s Client Intake Workgroup handles housing intake for the coalition. LAFLA is currently accepting applications for the position of Intake Supervisor. NOTE – This position may be based out of one of the following community office locations based on successful candidate’s preference: East LA, South LA, Long Beach, Santa Monica. QUALIFICATIONS:• Minimum three (3) years of management experience required with the ability to motivate and inspire teams remotely and in person.• Experience performing intake and triage, particularly within a legal setting, is strongly preferred.• Demonstrated passion for Housing Justice work, and an understanding of tenants’ rights is preferred.• Extremely strong interpersonal skills and the demonstrated ability to maintain an empathetic and resourceful attitude with persons in crisis and/or experiencing high-stress levels.• Ability to meet deadlines and perform multiple tasks while maintaining extreme attention to detail in a fast-paced work environment.• Willingness to work beyond a minimum 7.0-hour workday, including evening and weekend meetings and events, and workweeks over 35 hours when obligations so necessitate.• Ability to travel to LAFLA’s five community offices required.• Bilingual in English and Spanish strongly preferred. EXAMPLES OF DUTIES:• Supervise a team of seven (7) Stay Housed LA receptionists who engage with potential clients and perform housing intake triage over the telephone and in person.• Oversee Stay Housed LA receptionist housing intake triage to ensure efficient, client-centered, and trauma-informed assistance. Responsibilities include ongoing coaching and training in eligibility screening; ensuring timely and accurate data entry; reviewing applications and appointments for substantive quality and administrative compliance; responding appropriately to supervisor requests from staff and potential clients; and managing schedules to guarantee adequate coverage.• In conjunction with LAFLA’s Intake and Call Center Supervisor, administering a high-volume telephone-based Contact Center—the Contact Center (hotline) is the primary way that tenants connect with Stay Housed LA to apply for legal help. Responsibilities include managing and monitoring Contact Center queues to ensure timely and responsive handling; and tracking and analyzing Stay Housed LA Contact Center metrics to identify areas for improvement and enhance the overall potential client experience.• Manage and mentor staff to ensure meaningful professional development and compliance with Stay Housed LA’s priorities, policies, and procedures. Responsibilities include hiring and onboarding staff; performing regular 1:1 check-ins inside each of LAFLA’s community offices; completing annual evaluations and professional development plans; reviewing staff timekeeping and leave requests. The Stay Housed LA Intake Supervisor will also collaborate with LAFLA’s Housing Justice teams to provide continuing education on tenants’ rights.• Partner with LAFLA and Stay Housed LA management, including its Director of Client Services and Compliance, Intake and Call Center Supervisor, Data and Innovation Manager, etc. to develop and implement innovative tools to improve intake processes.• Cultivate effective relationships with a broad team that includes management, LAFLA’s Intake and Call Center Supervisor, attorneys, paralegals, support staff, volunteers, and students.• Other duties as assigned. HOW TO APPLY - Please submit a cover letter, resume, and office location preference (East LA, South LA, Long Beach, Santa Moncia) online to ciwgjobs@lafla.org Include “SHLA Intake Supervisor – Client Intake” in the subject line. PROBATIONARY PERIOD - A one year probationary period will be required. AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER – Selection will be based solely on merit and will be without discrimination because of race, color, national origin, ancestry, ethnicity, citizenship, creed, sex, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, transgender status, age, religion, genetic information, physical or mental disability, medical condition, military or veteran status, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical condition, marital or registered domestic partners status, or any other legally protected status.The organization is committed to equal employment opportunity and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified candidates and employees pursuant to applicable law. We value and encourage diversity and solicit applications from all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, gender, sex, age, religion, creed, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, sexual orientation, physical or mental disability, medical condition, military and veteran status, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. If you require reasonable accommodation as part of the application process or expect to require an accommodation if hired, please contact humanresources@lafla.org. BENEFITS AND COMPENSATION – LAFLA offers a diverse environment with competitive compensation based on comparable public interest salaries. We also offer a generous benefits package for full-time employees including medical, dental, and vision for employees and dependents, life insurance, long-term disability and long-term care insurance, and 403(b) retirement plan. Employees may also qualify for bilingual supplements, law student loan reimbursements, and a cell phone stipend. COMMITMENT TO EMPLOYEE WELLNESS - Due to the mission driven nature of the organization, LAFLA is committed to a healthy work-life balance for all staff. In addition to a hybrid work schedule and robust benefits package, LAFLA staff enjoy wellness related benefits and employee assistance programs through our offered medical plans, as well as Wellness Friday video sessions, a wellness content library, 15 LAFLA observed holidays, and generous time off benefits. SUSTAINABLE HYBRID WORK SCHEDULE – LAFLA has recently adopted a sustainable schedule whereby employees get several Fridays off during the year. Depending on job classifications, some LAFLA staff are working on a manager approved hybrid work schedule, with the ability to work remotely up to half the week, if preferred, after the probationary period. The successful candidate must be local and willing to work from the assigned LAFLA location. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 23:11:06 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11282618/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11282736 Graduate Operating Engineer at NAES Corporation Employer: NAES Corporation \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n NAES Staffing Services has an immediate need for Graduate Operating Engineers to work in Rialto, CA for Anaergia / Rialto Bioenergy Services. This facility operates 24 hours a day; must be flexible and open to rotating shifts. Candidates work 12hr shifts. Pay rate is $28 - $32/hr. This is a temp to hire position.Please read the below job description and apply today if you meet the qualifications. About Us:Anaergia (TSX: ANRG) is a global leader in offering sustainable solutions to produce clean energy and the conversion of waste streams to resources. Through a proven portfolio of proprietary technological solutions, Anaergia maximizes the generation of renewable energy, diversion of waste from landfills, and reduction of greenhouse gases for customers across the municipal, industrial, commercial, and agricultural sectors. Headquartered in Burlington, ON, and through its multiple subsidiaries across North America, Europe, Africa, and Asia, Anaergia is trusted at more than 1,600 installations globally Job Description:Reporting to the Operations & Maintenance Lead, operate and maintain the receiving area equipment as needed to ensure the plant maximizes uptime and receives all material from haulers without delays. Job Responsibilities:Follow PM schedule, routine field inspection of all equipment, complete daily site walk to ensure equipment visual health, and filling completed preventive maintenance work requisition/ Job Order completion on CMMS.Monitor and operate plant process equipment in accordance with SOP’s and safe industry practices.Collect production data and adjust plant operating conditions from SCADA and in the field to achieve plant production plans and goals.  Examples of production data would include but not be limited to lab analysis, plant SCADA historian data, and field logs. Provide lab analysis for feedstock and digester material in the SNRC facility lab. Provide lab report to engineering for analysis.  Training will be provided for lab work. Implement all site safety procedures and ensure contractors and coworkers are following safe work procedures and protocols. Identify Spare parts, and consumables procurement needs and prepare requisition for approval.Support in stacking up of all spares, tools, and consumables (Oil, Grease, Seals, Bearings etc.) maintaining records, and availability of spares on time.Develop and maintain skills such as using forklifts, hoists, cranes, and hand and power tools, and examining the form and texture of parts.Inspecting and collecting information on parts/pipes and other equipment utilizing rulers, calipers, and other measuring instruments.Follow all safety SOPs and support in the fabrication of temp lines, pipes, patchwork, weld/grinding, or cutting work on site.Providing cleaning of equipment as necessaryEnsure all calibration records for all required equipment are up to date and kept in records.Inspects and tests eye wash stations, fire extinguishers, and other life safety systems including PPE.Maintains a safe and clean working environment by complying with procedures, rules, and regulations. Works in a clean manner.Contributes to team effort by accomplishing related results as needed.Flexibility in working longer hours/overtime or weekend work will be needed.Any additional tasks requested by O & M Lead to effectively operate and maintain the facility in a safe, reliable, and efficient manner.Job Requirements:Graduation from high school or GED equivalent.BS with technical focus or trade school certification Fri, 7 Aug 2026 00:56:53 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11282736/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11282486 Senior Water Resource Control Engineer (JC-527607) at State Water Resources Control Board Employer: State Water Resources Control Board \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n To be considered for this position, you must apply at CalCareers.ca.gov. To apply, you must first create a CalCareers account. Once your account is created, you can search for job code 527607 to locate the job posting and apply. Link: CalCareersNote: This position will no longer be available on CalCareers once the job closes on 8/17/2026. No applications will be accepted after the job closing date. Job Description and DutiesPlease note, the Water Boards do not participate in E-Verify.Are you looking for an exciting and fulfilling opportunity to help California’s small and disadvantaged communities address critical water quality and drinking water issues? Do you enjoy a fast-paced environment with opportunities to innovate and lead positive change? If so, then apply today and join our dedicated and driven team. The State Water Resources Control Board’s Division of Financial Assistance has an opening for a Senior Water Resource Control Engineer in the Office of Sustainable Water Solutions. The position is located at 1001 I Street, 16th Floor, Sacramento, CA 95814 right in the heart of Downtown next to light rail stations and other public transportation. Duties: Under the direction of a Supervising Water Resource Control Engineer and consistent with good customer service practices and the goals of the State and Regional Board’s Strategic Plan, the Senior Water Resource Control Engineer is responsible for directly supervising technical staff engaged in the administration of the Safe and Affordable Drinking Water Fund, Drinking Water and Clean Water State Revolving Fund’s grant/principal forgiveness funding, state bond funding and other infrastructure appropriations.  Additional information:Candidates must possess essential personal qualifications including integrity, initiative, dependability, good judgment, the ability to work cooperatively with others, and the ability to perform the assigned duties of the class.If the position requires driving, you must possess a current and valid Driver’s License. Please do not include full social security number, method of eligibility, and LEAP information in your application package. Please let us know how you heard about this position by taking this brief survey: Recruitment Survey.You will find additional information about the job in the Duty Statement.  Working ConditionsPlease note, the Water Boards do not participate in E-Verify.Positions at the Water Boards may be eligible for telework with in-person attendance based on the operational needs of the position and might be expected to comply with Executive Order (EO) 22-25 after July 1, 2026.Salary Information - CalHR salary rules allow appointment at the entrance rate (Cal. Code Regs., tit. 2, § 599.673) of a classification. For classes with alternate ranges, placement is based on education/experience. Employees appointed to the Attorney or Water Resource Control Engineer classification will receive Recruitment Higher Above Minimum (HAM) rate in accordance with the approved Civil Service Pay Scales.In addition, note: Effective July 1, 2025, the State of California implemented the Personal Leave Program 2025 (PLP 2025) which reduces an employee’s monthly salary in exchange for leave credits. Employees appointed to this classification will have their monthly salary reduced and will accrue hours of PLP 2025 on the first day of each pay period in accordance with the applicable bargaining contract. The salary range(s) included on this job posting do not reflect the reduction in pay.  Job type: Full-Time$11,437.00 - $14,315.00 per MonthThe Water Resources Control Board is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSFL) Qualified Employer. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 22:18:55 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11282486/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11186932 Account Executive at Konica Minolta Business Solutions, U.S.A., Inc. Employer: Konica Minolta Business Solutions, U.S.A., Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Overview Start your sales career with a global brand that invests in you. At Konica Minolta, you’ll build new business and grow existing accounts, all while getting out in the field and meeting customers face-to-face. This is a hands-on, hybrid sales role where you’ll learn fast, own real opportunities, and develop the skills to close deals. If you’re motivated, people-first, and ready to grow, this is your launchpad.  What You’ll Do: Learn and sell our full suite of print and tech solutions Build your pipeline through prospecting, networking, and referrals Spend the majority of your time in the field meeting customers at their locations Balance hunting (new business) + farming (growing accounts) Run consultative conversations and deliver solution-focused presentations Collaborate with your team to win deals and refine strategy Manage your pipeline, track activity, and hit your goals Participate in training, team events, and ongoing development  Why You’ll Love It:Real-world sales experience from day one Supportive, team-first culture Clear growth path + skill development A chance to earn, learn, and win early in your career  What You Bring: Bachelor’s degree preferred, or equivalent experience 6 months - 3 years’ experience in a customer-facing role (sales development, account support, customer success support, renewals support, or similar) highly desirable Ability to customarily and regularly travel within the assigned territory to conduct in-person customer/prospect meetings and field-based selling Valid driver’s license and reliable transportation for daily field travel within assigned territory Alignment to our corporate values of Open & Honest, Customer-Centric, Innovative, Passionate, Inclusive & Collaborative, Accountable Familiarity with Salesforce a plus If you’re ready to build confidence, make an impact, and grow fast, this is your move. Tue, 7 Jul 2026 20:08:20 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11186932/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11282804 Insurance and Financial Services Position at State Farm Insurance - Allan Cheng Agency Employer: State Farm Insurance - Allan Cheng Agency \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Successful State Farm Agent is seeking a qualified professional to join their winning team for the role of Insurance and Financial Services Position - State Farm Agent Team Member. We seek an energetic professional interested in helping our business grow through value-based conversations and remarkable customer experience. If you are a motivated self starter who thrives in a fast-paced environment, then this is your opportunity for a rewarding career with excellent income and growth potential.RequirementsExcellent communication skills - written, verbal and listeningEnthusiastic about the role insurance and financial products play in helping people manage the risks of everyday life, recover from the unexpected, and realize their dreamsOrganizational skillsSelf-motivatedDedicated to customer serviceAbility to multi-taskAbility to effectively relate to a customerBilingual - Spanish or Mandarin preferredProperty and Casualty license (must be able to obtain)Life and Health license (must be able to obtain) Fri, 7 Aug 2026 02:22:19 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11282804/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11282272 Documentation Specialist - US Citizen (On-Site) at ProDIGIQ Inc. Employer: ProDIGIQ Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Please apply on career.prodigiq.com to be considered. About UsProDIGIQ is an AI company that delivers enterprise software for the aerospace and defense industries. We provide innovative products and services, including operations management, safety management, lease management, maintenance management, flight operations, flight scheduling, and gate management. We utilize typical web technologies, but the software we build for our clients are anything but typical. We empower our aviation clients, such as Frontier Airlines, Boeing, and Dallas-Fort Worth International Airport (DFW), to name a few, with powerful, scalable and intuitive software solutions that improve the safety, quality and efficiency of their operations.Job DescriptionProDIGIQ is looking for an exceptional Documentation Specialist who can help produce high-quality technical content that contributes to the overall success of our growing and fast-paced company. The Documentation Specialist will work closely with the Business Development and Engineering Departments as well as with our Executive Team. We are looking for a team-oriented candidate who has a strong work ethic to be able to get things done in a highly collaborative environment.ResponsibilitiesResearch, outline, write, and edit contentProduce and maintain high-quality documentation/content including but not limited to Request for Proposals (RFP) responses, product manuals, user guides, company blog posts, press releases, newsletter and website contentReview, analyze, and interpret technical requirements to gain a thorough understanding of the objectives of each solicitationMaintain and update a repository of technical contentDevelop comprehensive documentation for a variety of company initiatives that meet organizational standardsObtain a deep understanding of ProDIGIQ’s products and services and translate complex product information into simple and polished contentWrite easy-to-understand content that meets applicable standards and is appropriate for its intended audienceExplore new business opportunitiesKey QualificationsBA degree with 3.6 GPA or higher (English Major Preferred)2 years of experience (Preferred)Proven writing experienceExcellent writing skillsAbility to quickly grasp new concepts and develop product knowledgeAbility to effectively synthesize and communicate product features and benefitsAbility to manage deadlines efficientlyExtremely detail oriented and highly organizedMust be reliable, flexible, and willing to take on new challengesProDIGIQ fosters an inclusive work environment that encourages creativity, initiative, and professional growth. We offer competitive salaries and benefits. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 21:27:35 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11282272/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11282137 Deputy Sheriff Trainee at Orange County Sheriff's Department Employer: Orange County Sheriff's Department \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n A Deputy Sheriff Trainee will be required to attend and satisfactorily complete the 28-week P.O.S.T. Certified Orange County Sheriff's Regional Training Academy. Upon successful completion of the academy, the Deputy Sheriff Trainee will be promoted to the position of Deputy Sheriff I. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 20:56:50 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11282137/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11282557 Attorney (CBEST) - Economic Stability Workgroup at Legal Aid Foundation of Los Angeles Employer: Legal Aid Foundation of Los Angeles \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n POSITION: Attorney (CBEST) - Economic Stability WorkgroupLOCATION: East Los Angeles Community Office*SALARY: $88,400k - $103,415.50k/ annually DOE, with excellent benefitsAVAILABILITY: ImmediatelyAPPLICATION DEADLINE: Continuous until position is filled. Are you interested in joining an organization dedicated to increasing access to justice while addressing systemic inequities among the most vulnerable members of the Greater Los Angeles area? If yes, LAFLA is the place for you! The Organization: LAFLA is a nonprofit law firm that protects and advances the rights of the most underserved—leveling the playing field and ensuring that everyone can have access to the justice system. Celebrating 95 years of service to Los Angeles communities, LAFLA is the first and most experienced legal aid organization in Greater Los Angeles. LAFLA has more than 200 employees, including more than 100 attorneys, who provide free services and resources on a broad range of civil legal issues that impact healthy, safety, and self-sufficiency. Every year, LAFLA helps more than 100,000 people find their voice, regain control of their lives, and build a brighter future. Our unique combination of neighborhood offices, self-help centers at courthouses, and domestic violence clinics puts LAFLA on the frontlines in communities at the forefront of change. LAFLA also engages in impact litigation to help enact long-term systemic change—actively collaborating with a network of public and private partners to expand access to justice, identify needs in the communities we serve, and change laws and policies that adversely affect the underserved. For more information, please visit www.lafla.org. The Workgroup: The Economic Stability Workgroup (ESWG) helps people obtain benefits to fulfill basic needs (food, shelter, medical care, and services to attain self-sufficiency); fights wage theft and denial of unemployment insurance benefits; and advises on wrongful terminations and discriminatory employment practices. ESWG also helps people who cannot afford to repay their student loans due to disability or who have attended for-profit colleges that engaged in predatory, deceptive, or illegal practices. In addition to direct service, ESWG engages in policy advocacy and impact litigation to address systemic problems. The Position: This position includes a mix of general government benefits advocacy and representing clients in permanent disability appeals before the Social Security Administration (SSI and SSDI cases) or the State Hearings Division (CAPI cases). LAFLA is currently accepting applications for the position of Attorney. NOTE – This position is part of a special program created using designated funds. There is no assurance of ongoing funding or employment beyond 12 months. QUALIFICATIONS:• Active membership in the California State Bar with one to five years experience;• Demonstrated commitment to serving the needs of low-income people;• Litigation experience, including case evaluation, legal research and writing, discovery, negotiations, and administrative hearing or trial experience preferred;• Familiarity with government benefits programs such as General Relief, Supplemental Security Income, Social Security• Disability Insurance, Cash Assistance Program for Immigrants (CAPI) and other cash aid programs;• Previous public interest experience preferred; and• Willingness to work beyond a minimum 7.5 hour workday, including evening and weekend meetings and events, and• workweeks in excess of 35 hours when caseload or other obligations so necessitate. EXAMPLES OF DUTIES:• Conduct extensive interviews with potential or retained clients;• Review medical records and Social Security and Department of Public Social Services (DPSS) notices;• Assess merit for representation based on extensive review of medical records and other documents; and• Assist disabled and low-income clients with obtaining or maintaining Social Security Disability Insurance,• Supplemental Security Income or CAPI benefits through negotiation with the Social Security Administration and the Disability Determination Services agency, representation at administrative appeals or litigation in federal court. HOW TO APPLY - Please submit a cover letter and resume online to eswgjobs@lafla.org. Include “Attorney (CBEST) - Economic Stability” in the subject line. PROBATIONARY PERIOD – A one-year probationary period will be required. AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER – Selection will be based solely on merit and will be without discrimination because of race, color, national origin, ancestry, ethnicity, citizenship, creed, sex, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, transgender status, age, religion, genetic information, physical or mental disability, medical condition, military or veteran status, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical condition, marital or registered domestic partners status, or any other legally protected status.The organization is committed to equal employment opportunity and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified candidates and employees pursuant to applicable law. We value and encourage diversity and solicit applications from all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, gender, sex, age, religion, creed, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, sexual orientation, physical or mental disability, medical condition, military and veteran status, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. If you require reasonable accommodation as part of the application process or expect to require an accommodation if hired, please contact humanresources@lafla.org. BENEFITS AND COMPENSATION – LAFLA offers a diverse environment with competitive compensation based on comparable public interest salaries. We also offer a generous benefits package for full-time employees including medical, dental, and vision for employees and dependents, life insurance, long-term disability and long-term care insurance, and 403(b) retirement plan. Employees may also qualify for bilingual supplements, law student loan reimbursements, and a cell phone stipend. COMMITMENT TO EMPLOYEE WELLNESS – Due to the mission driven nature of the organization, LAFLA is committed to a healthy work-life balance for all staff. In addition to a hybrid work schedule and robust benefits package, LAFLA staff enjoy wellness related benefits and employee assistance programs through our offered medical plans, as well as Wellness Friday video sessions, a wellness content library, 15 LAFLA observed holidays, and generous time off benefits. SUSTAINABLE HYBRID WORK SCHEDULE – LAFLA has recently adopted a sustainable schedule whereby employees get several Fridays off during the year. Depending on job classifications, some LAFLA staff are working on a manager approved hybrid work schedule, with the ability to work remotely up to half the week, if preferred, after the probationary period. The successful candidate must be local and willing to work from the assigned LAFLA location. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 22:45:13 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11282557/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11282578 Senior Attorney - Housing and Communities Workgroup at Legal Aid Foundation of Los Angeles Employer: Legal Aid Foundation of Los Angeles \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n POSITION: Senior Attorney - Housing and Communities WorkgroupLOCATION: South Los Angeles Community OfficeSALARY: $125,836.55k - $133,500k / annually DOE, with excellent benefitsAVAILABILITY: ImmediatelyAPPLICATION DEADLINE: Continuous until position is filled.Are you interested in joining an organization dedicated to increasing access to justice while addressing systemic inequities among the most vulnerable members of the Greater Los Angeles area? If yes, LAFLA is the place for you!The Organization: LAFLA is a nonprofit law firm that protects and advances the rights of the most underserved—leveling the playing field and ensuring that everyone can have access to the justice system. Celebrating 95 years of service to Los Angeles communities, LAFLA is the first and most experienced legal aid organization in Greater Los Angeles. LAFLA has more than 200 employees, including more than 100 attorneys, who provide free services and resources on a broad range of civil legal issues that impact healthy, safety, and self-sufficiency. Every year, LAFLA helps more than 100,000 people find their voice, regain control of their lives, and build a brighter future. Our unique combination of neighborhood offices, self-help centers at courthouses, and domestic violence clinics puts LAFLA on the frontlines in communities at the forefront of change. LAFLA also engages in impact litigation to help enact long-term systemic change—actively collaborating with a network of public and private partners to expand access to justice, identify needs in the communities we serve, and change laws and policies that adversely affect the underserved. For more information, please visit www.lafla.org.The Housing and Communities Workgroup consists of community advocates who prevent unfair displacement, protects and expands affordable housing, works towards more equitable tenant policies in coalition with tenant organizers and provides legal support to community-based organizations seeking to build healthy, economically vibrant communities. LAFLA is currently accepting applications for the position of Senior Attorney. QUALIFICATIONS:• Active membership in the California State Bar;• At least ten years State or Local Policy Advocacy and/or litigation experience in Superior and Federal Court;• Community Lawyering Experience;• Demonstrated knowledge of housing law;• Excellent written and verbal communication;• Experience with diverse client population and a commitment to promoting anti-racism; and• Willingness to work beyond a minimum 7.5 hour workday, including evening and weekend meetings and events, and workweeks in excess of 37 hours when caseload or other obligations so necessitate. EXAMPLES OF DUTIES:• Serve as lead counsel on cases that include complex advocacy and direct services, commensurate with experience Actively participate in community groups and coalitions on issues, such as systemic racism, impacting service-eligible populations;• Develop case strategies and work plans for matters assigned;• Provide advice and technical assistance to community-based organizations engaged in policy advocacy to support low-income communities;• Draft pleadings, legal documents, trial memoranda, appellate briefs and community education materials;• Investigate, develop and litigate high-impact cases at the trial and appellate level in federal and state courts; and• Work on public policy issues impacting low income individuals and communities including issues of systemic racism.HOW TO APPLY - Please submit a cover letter and resume online to hocojobs@lafla.org. Include “Senior Attorney - Housing and Communities” in the subject line.PROBATIONARY PERIOD - A one-year probationary period will be required.AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER – Selection will be based solely on merit and will be without discrimination because of race, color, national origin, ancestry, ethnicity, citizenship, creed, sex, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, transgender status, age, religion, genetic information, physical or mental disability, medical condition, military or veteran status, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical condition, marital or registered domestic partners status, or any other legally protected status.The organization is committed to equal employment opportunity and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified candidates and employees pursuant to applicable law. We value and encourage diversity and solicit applications from all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, gender, sex, age, religion, creed, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, marital status, sexual orientation, physical or mental disability, medical condition, military and veteran status, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. If you require reasonable accommodation as part of the application process or expect to require an accommodation if hired, please contact humanresources@lafla.orgBENEFITS AND COMPENSATION – LAFLA offers a diverse environment with competitive compensation based on comparable public interest salaries. We also offer a generous benefits package for full-time employees including medical, dental, and vision for employees and dependents, life insurance, long-term disability and long-term care insurance, and 403(b) retirement plan. Employees may also qualify for bilingual supplements, law student loan reimbursements, and a cell phone stipend.COMMITMENT TO EMPLOYEE WELLNESS – Due to the mission driven nature of the organization, LAFLA is committed to a healthy work-life balance for all staff. In addition to a hybrid work schedule and robust benefits package, LAFLA staff enjoy wellness related benefits and employee assistance programs through our offered medical plans, as well as Wellness Friday video sessions, a wellness content library, 15 LAFLA observed holidays, and generous time off benefits.SUSTAINABLE HYBRID WORK SCHEDULE – LAFLA has recently adopted a sustainable schedule whereby employees get several Fridays off during the year. Depending on job classifications, some LAFLA staff are working on a manager approved hybrid work schedule, with the ability to work remotely up to half the week, if preferred, after the probationary period. The successful candidate must be local and willing to work from the assigned LAFLA location. Thu, 6 Aug 2026 22:55:32 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11282578/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11283677 Client Support Representative at Legacy Marketing Employer: Legacy Marketing \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n We're seeking a Client Support Representative in Richmond. This role focuses on supporting the AT&T mobile campaign, assisting customers with service setup, and troubleshooting mobile device issues.As a Client Support Representative, you will command the front line of AT&T's mobile connectivity, delivering swift and definitive resolutions for device issues, plan guidance, and account management to ensure every customer remains powerfully connected. The Client Support Representative’s expertise will be the critical link that transforms complex mobile technology into seamless, everyday reliability.Who We AreWe are Legacy Marketing: Virginia-born, results-driven. As a sales and business consulting firm, our mission is to aggressively expand AT&T's mobile footprint, providing the strategic horsepower that fuels connectivity for businesses and families across the region.What We Are AboutWe believe reliable service is a right, not a privilege. Our team is the enforcer of that right, delivering support with the authority and precision that makes customer uncertainty a thing of the past.What Will I Be Doing as a Client Support Representative?Provide digital-first client support by resolving mobile service and device issues through digital channels and a CRM system.Guide client onboarding by assisting customers with mobile plan selection, service activation, and account setup.Manage client accounts by tracking statuses, support tickets, and service milestones in CRM systems to ensure timely follow-up.Collaborate across teams to resolve complex client issues such as provisioning delays, billing problems, and device compatibility concerns.Educate clients on product features and account tools to enhance their satisfaction and increase self-service usage.Identify and recommend service enhancements based on a client's specific needs and usage patterns to drive account growth.What Do I Need to Bring to the Table as a Client Support Representative?High school diploma or GED required; coursework in communications, business, or technology preferred to support service workflows and customer engagement.Experience in service coordination, mobile device support, or account onboarding—ideally within telecom or subscription-based platforms.Strong communication and resolution skills; able to guide customers through service processes and troubleshoot device or account-related issues.CRM proficient; maintains clean, actionable data to support account tracking, service milestones, and performance reporting.Detail-oriented and proactive; capable of managing multiple support workflows with precision, professionalism, and a focus on customer satisfaction. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 13:28:52 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11283677/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11187697 Dental Sales Representative (Open to International Students Sponsorship) at Dentco Employer: Dentco \n\n Expires: 09/06/2026 \n\n Job DescriptionConduct market analysis on your territory to assess competitive positioning, pricing trends, and growth opportunitiesIdentify, prospect, and qualify new business opportunities through field outreach and relationship-buildingEngage directly with dental professionals to assess clinical and operational needs, and present tailored solutionsManage and nurture client relationships to drive repeat business and increase account productionEnsure a high standard of customer service through timely communication and proactive support QualificationsMust have a car and be willing to drive extensively to meet with clientsPrior sales experience is a plus, but not a mustBachelor’s degree required; an MBA degree is a plusDemonstrated initiative, strong work ethic, and a results-oriented mindsetExcellent interpersonal and communication skillsResilience in handling objections Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced setting Compensations40-100k with a performance-driven commission structure Travel reimbursement for field activitiesStructured onboarding and ongoing professional sales trainingOpen to international candidates (including OPT) Fri, 10 Jul 2026 20:55:17 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11187697/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11283441 Test Prep Faculty at Foley Prep, Inc. Employer: Foley Prep, Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n Job Title: Educational Consultant & Test Prep FacultyCompany OverviewFoley Prep is New Jersey’s premier tutoring and test preparation company. We are experiencing exciting growth and are looking to expand our elite faculty of 25 full-time professionals. With seven state-of-the-art office locations across New Jersey, we are committed to making a lasting, positive impact on the academic trajectories and lives of the young people we serve.Position OverviewWe are seeking a highly motivated, articulate, and dedicated Full-Time Test Prep Faculty member to join our dynamic team. In this in-office role, you will be instrumental in guiding students through their academic and test preparation journeys, helping them unlock their highest potential.While prior tutoring experience is a plus, we are primarily looking for driven college graduates—particularly those with a STEM background—who possess an exceptional work ethic and a genuine passion for mentorship. If you are a clear communicator looking to build a rewarding career alongside a collaborative team of professional educators, this is the role for you. Key ResponsibilitiesInstruction & Mentorship: Deliver engaging, high-quality test preparation instruction to students in an in-office setting across our New Jersey locations. Student Impact: Serve as an academic role model, fostering a supportive and motivating environment that encourages young people to succeed and build confidence.Clear Communication: Effectively communicate student progress, areas for improvement, and actionable strategies to both students and their parents. Team Collaboration: Work alongside our established faculty of 25 full-time professionals, sharing best practices and contributing to the continued growth and reputation of Foley Prep. Professional Excellence: Maintain a rigorous work ethic, high standard of professionalism, and dedication to the educational outcomes of our clients. Qualifications & RequirementsEducation: Bachelor’s (or near-degree) degree required. A degree in a STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering, or Mathematics) field is highly preferred. Experience: Prior tutoring or teaching experience is preferred, but not required. We are willing to train the right candidate who demonstrates the necessary drive and aptitude. Communication Skills: Exceptional verbal and written communication abilities, with a talent for breaking down complex concepts into accessible, digestible lessons. Work Ethic: A demonstrated strong work ethic with a readiness to thrive in a growing, fast-paced educational environment. Logistics: Must be able and willing to work full-time, in-person across Foley Prep's 7 New Jersey office locations. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 12:00:51 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11283441/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11285834 Pharmacist - Full-time Floater - Enterprise, AL at Publix Super Markets Employer: Publix Super Markets \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n As a Publix Pharmacy Associate, you’ll see how very satisfying it is to work for a company that is passionately devoted to its customers, to its associates, and to the wellness of the communities it serves. What sets our pharmacy departments apart is a genuine patient-centric environment with clinical services such as immunizations, MTM (medication therapy management), and much more!Publix is continually recognized as one of the best places in America to work; see why Publix should be part of your list of top places to work in Pharmacy. And, with growth potential of up to 50 new pharmacies per year, our promote from within culture allows for a rewarding career path into any one of the following areas: retail management, specialty pharmacy, out-patient hospital pharmacy, corporate or centralized pharmacy operations.Your passion for health and wellness, combined with our reputation and commitment to excellence, are what sets Publix apart from the crowd. We know you want to make a career out of caring. We want your career to be with Publix Pharmacy. Join the team that pharmacists and patients feel good about.In addition to the shared basic responsibilities of all Publix associates, a Floating Pharmacist’s responsibilities include, but are not limited to, the following. As a Floating Pharmacist, you will:provide dedication to each pharmacies success, by executing strategy, motivating and inspiring staff as the pharmacist-on-dutyset priorities to maximize contribution, executing daily tasks, supporting the team and building rapport with both customers and associatesprovide best-in-class pharmacy service to patients, empower your staff in providing value and service through counseling, building personalized relationships, promoting customer loyalty, offering pharmacist led clinical services to improve health and wellness and preventative care through services available at Publixinspire each team you work with to do the right thing, gaining buy in, and empowering the team to be accountableprovide enthusiasm for all new pharmacy initiatives at your assigned locationmanage team performance, such as prescription promised time, by assigning tasks to ensure complex operational activities are met in a timely and efficient manner in the absence of the pharmacist-in-chargeuse best practices to make sound business decisions while covering as the pharmacist-on-dutybe regarded as an expert on the pharmacy technology system and how it is used for both routine and complex prescription processingmentor others on Publix pharmacy best practices to maximize sales, minimize shrink while meeting customers’ needs, using programs such as auto refill and Sync Your Refillsproactively advance pharmacy clinical initiatives including Medication Therapy Management (MTM) and immunizationsmaintain a flexible work-week schedule in order to meet the needs of our customers, andassist in all other duties as assigned.The minimum qualifications for the position of Floating Pharmacist are:must be at least 18 years of agemust be a graduate of a school of pharmacymust have and maintain an unrestricted, state pharmacist licensemust not have active suspensions, sanctions, or other restrictions related to participation in a private, federal, or state health insurance program upon hire and thereafter andmust not have received an unacceptable result on a company-sponsored drug test within the last three yearsOther qualifications for the position of Floating Pharmacist include:be an immunizing pharmacist meeting the requirements as established by the state (or be scheduled to become an immunizer in the next set of training classes)effective communication and interpersonal skillsability to interpret and understand instructions and solve problemsnumerical and financial aptitude andknowledge of retail merchandising and inventory control. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 19:36:24 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11285834/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11285855 Pharmacist - Full-time Floater - Foley, AL at Publix Super Markets Employer: Publix Super Markets \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n As a Publix Pharmacy Associate, you’ll see how very satisfying it is to work for a company that is passionately devoted to its customers, to its associates, and to the wellness of the communities it serves. What sets our pharmacy departments apart is a genuine patient-centric environment with clinical services such as immunizations, MTM (medication therapy management), and much more!Publix is continually recognized as one of the best places in America to work; see why Publix should be part of your list of top places to work in Pharmacy. And, with growth potential of up to 50 new pharmacies per year, our promote from within culture allows for a rewarding career path into any one of the following areas: retail management, specialty pharmacy, out-patient hospital pharmacy, corporate or centralized pharmacy operations.Your passion for health and wellness, combined with our rep