ces available at Publixmentor, train and develop a high functioning pharmacy team, providing developmental opportunities and challenging assignments to all staff, to grow and develop, tailoring to meet each one’s needsinspire your team to do the right thing, gaining buy in, and empowering the team to be accountable for the goals of the pharmacy departmentserve as a champion for executing programs and processes, creating enthusiasm for innovation in your locationmanage performance including scheduling and assigning tasks to ensure complex operational activities are met in a timely and efficient mannerensure continuous improvement and maintain a competitive advantage by understanding metrics as they relate to sales and service in your pharmacy, using best practices and making sound business decisions as the pharmacist-in-chargebe regarded as an expert on the pharmacy technology system and how it is used for both routine and complex prescription processingexcel in managing medication on-hand inventory and regarded as an expert in pharmacy inventory operationsmentor others on best practices to maximize sales, minimize shrink while meeting customers’ needs while using programs such as auto refill and Sync Your Refillsproactively advance pharmacy clinical initiatives including Medication Therapy Management (MTM)and immunizationsparticipate locally as a community pharmacist in events that will meet the unique health and preventative care needs within the local area, such as health screenings and immunizationsmaintain a flexible work-week schedule in order to meet the needs of our customers, andassist in all other duties as assigned.Required Qualifications :The minimum qualifications for the position of Pharmacy Manager are:must be at least 18 years of agemust be a graduate of a school of pharmacymust have and maintain an unrestricted state pharmacist licensemust not have active suspensions, sanctions, or other restrictions related to participation in a private, federal, or state health insurance program upon hire and thereafter andmust not have received an unacceptable result on a company-sponsored drug test within the last three yearsPreferred Qualifications :Other qualifications for the position of Pharmacy Manager include:be an immunizing pharmacist meeting the requirements as established by the state (or be scheduled to become an immunizer in the next set of training classes)ability to understand profit and loss statementseffective communication and interpersonal skillsability to define problems, plan work, utilize logic, and draw conclusionsnumerical and financial aptitude andknowledge of retail merchandising and inventory control. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 19:16:55 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11285711/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11285570 Maintenance Technician at Pero Family Farms Employer: Pero Family Farms \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n DescriptionTitle: Maintenance TechnicianReports To: Maintenance ManagerLocation: Delray Beach, FLType: Full-Time | Onsite | Non-Exempt COMPANY SUMMARYFor more than a century, Pero Family Farms has built its reputation on dedication, commitment, and integrity. Operating since 1908, Pero is a fully integrated farming organization specializing in organic farming, logistics, global supply chain management, national sales, food processing, and strategic marketing. With more than 35,000 acres spanning Florida to New York and operations across several states, we continue to grow—and we are investing in the people who will shape our future.For new graduates, that future can begin in Palm Beach County, where career opportunity meets an exceptional South Florida lifestyle. Enjoy year-round sunshine, beautiful beaches, outdoor adventures, vibrant communities, great restaurants, and endless opportunities to explore. At Pero, we are not simply filling positions—we are building careers, developing talent, and creating opportunities for the next generation of professionals and leaders. JOB PURPOSEThe Maintenance Technician’s main responsibilities will include but are not limited to assisting the maintenance supervisor with fabrication/installation and preventative maintenance of equipment throughout the facilities. This position will report directly to the Maintenance Supervisor.RequirementsPRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIESFabrication of needed parts or materialsRepair machinery and facilitiesPerform preventative maintenance on equipmentInstall and test new equipmentResponsible for keeping the production machinery running with minimum downtimeResponsible for maintaining repairs to the facilitiesComplete paperwork in a timely and legible mannerFollow safety policies/procedures including wearing necessary PPEFollow attendance policy and other policies  EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCEPossess verbal and written communication skillsExperience in fresh food or production environment2+ year of maintenance experienceHigh School Diploma or GED preferredMust have own transportationMust have a working knowledge of English languageBasic Mathematical abilitiesAbility to interact across departments   WORKING CONDITIONSExposure to product fumes (e.g., onions, peppers, and other produce)Exposure to cold environments (temperatures of 45°F or below)Exposure to cleaning and sanitation chemicals (e.g., chlorine)Work performed in a fresh food production and warehouse environmentRequired to work overtime as neededUse of tools and equipment, including occasional use of cutting utensils (e.g., knives, peelers)Fast-paced production setting with a focus on minimizing downtimeCompliance with safety policies and use of required personal protective equipment (PPE) PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTSAbility to stand, walk, and sit for extended periods of timeFrequent use of hands for grasping, handling tools, and writingOccasional bending, stooping, reaching, and climbingAbility to lift and carry items ranging from 5 to 50 poundsManual dexterity to perform maintenance, repairs, and fabrication tasks COMPANY BENEFITS/PERKS401(k)Health, Dental, Vision Insurance and morePaid Time Off (PTO)The company (Pero) reserves the right to alter, amend, expand or contract these duties and responsibilities as the company's needs evolve. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 18:51:16 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11285570/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11284665 Home Sales Advisors & Realtors at Forward March Management LLC Employer: Forward March Management LLC - Home Base Advisors \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n UNIQUE REALTOR OPPORTUNITY & PLATFORMAre you ready to join a unique and fast-growing residential realtor and manufactured / modular home dealer company located in Jacksonville, NC (next to Camp LeJeune) offering the opportunity, training, and resources to earn a high six figure income? HOME BASE is seeking two hires - a junior salesperson and a seasoned real estate agent.Realty by Home Base is a licensed realtor and its affiliate, Home Base Advisors (HBA) a licensed manufactured/modular home dealer.By combining the traditional realtor business with that of a manufactured/modular home dealership, HOME BASE Advisors/Agents have two distinct ways to earn commissions and close a high volume of home sales transactions. Additionally, HOME BASE has the financial backing of a regional private real estate investor that will either buy land from you and have you re-list once a spec home or rental is move in ready OR buy the land and hold it until your client’s funding and manufactured home purchase are ready for a turn-key closing. Either way our agents make two commissions for one transaction.TRUST IS EARNEDAs our senior team each has 30 years of experience in real estate development, investing and customer service, our clients appreciate the expertise and guidance to overcome the many challenges associated with sourcing land and building their dream home. It’s this level of knowledge and expertise that will help you win the trust of more clients. HOME BASE is seeking real estate professionals that want to contribute to and grow with a highly knowledgeable team.As you can focus on either residential realty sales or manufactured home sales but the more well rounded Advisors will seek to wear both hats. In our hybrid model, salespersons will not only service their clients and their real estate needs, but also receive favorable splits and a high volume of leads and appointments set on your behalf to assist buyers interested in purchasing land and/or a factory-built home. Again, giving you two primary paths to earn commissions.MANUFACTURED HOMES - ON TRENDThe manufactured home sector has grown tremendously the past decade. Since covid, home prices and rents have skyrocketed, thus pricing many buyers out of the market. However, manufactured homes are becoming an increasingly favored solution to home ownership.QUALIFIED CANDIDATESThe ideal candidate should be a good communicator, listener, and advisor yet politely persistent. However the person needs to be able to manage a sales process and be highly detail oriented. HOME BASE is seeking candidates that are willing to bet on themselves to succeed.This offers a great opportunity to help people own their own homes and generate a strong commission income at the same time. Tremendous growth opportunity for the right candidate looking to take the next step in his/her real estate sales and professional career.  Real estate experience is preferred, but not required. Additional consideration will be given to highly accomplished military and/or school teachers (thank you both for your service) looking to transition into real estate. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 16:19:04 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11284665/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11284696 IT Specialist at Charm City Medical Center, Inc. Employer: Charm City Medical Center, Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n Charm City Medical Center Overview:Charm City Medical Center is an integrated opioid treatment, behavioral health, and mental health treatment facility in Baltimore, MD. We offer Methadone, Suboxone, IOP, OP, DWI/DUI treatment programs. We are a start-up, and ask candidates to expect a fast-paced, dynamic workplace environment. Stellar patient care is our #1 goal. We use state-of-the-art technology to deliver our services, and we need team members who are well-versed in modern technology and systems.  Why join Charm City Medical Center?Be a Founding Team MemberOpportunity to shape and grow a first-of-its-kind integrated behavioral health program from the ground up.Client-Service-Driven CareRooted in social justice and inspired by H. Jack Geiger’s revolutionary model of addressing healthcare through poverty eradication and community investment.Truly Integrated ServicesWork in a facility that combines an OMHC, IOP, OTP, and eventually primary care, pharmacy & community medicine (RN-driven case management).Career and Financial UpsidePotential involvement in future projects with the possibility for equity.Community-Centered LocationLocated in 21217, a historically underserved area, ideal for professionals who want to make a real, visible impact in their own or nearby communities.Service-disabled veteran and board-certified physician-led practice.Put simply, we know our stuff. Job Overview:The IT Specialist at Charm City Medical Center is responsible for supporting the day-to-day technology needs of the clinic, including network management, hardware/software support, data security, and troubleshooting. This role will be instrumental in maintaining clinical and administrative technology infrastructure to ensure seamless patient care and regulatory compliance. Key Responsibilities: Technical Support & MaintenanceProvide onsite and remote support to staff for hardware, software, and connectivity issues.Set up, configure, and troubleshoot desktop and mobile devices, printers, scanners, and tablets.Network & Systems AdministrationMaintain local and cloud-based systems, including internet, Wi-Fi, and internal servers.Monitor system performance, ensure regular data backups, and assist in disaster recovery planning.EMR/EHR & Practice Management SystemsSupport the implementation and optimization of electronic medical records (EMR) and practice management platforms.Train staff and troubleshoot system issues related to patient data and scheduling.Cybersecurity & ComplianceEnsure HIPAA compliance and data protection standards are met across all platforms.Manage user accounts, permissions, and access control for sensitive patient information.Vendor & Equipment ManagementServe as the point of contact for external IT vendors and service providers.Track IT inventory, order necessary equipment, and manage warranties/licenses.Innovation & DevelopmentRecommend technology upgrades and process improvements.Assist with special projects including new site development, telehealth integration, and compliance audits.Skills & Qualifications:Proficiency in Windows and Mac OS environments, Google Workspace, and EMR/EHR platforms.Strong problem-solving and communication skills.Understanding of HIPAA regulations, network security, and data privacy standards.Experience with VPNs, firewalls, antivirus systems, and device management tools.Ability to multitask, prioritize tickets, and support staff at various technical skill levels. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 16:19:49 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11284696/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11285973 Pharmacist - Full-time Floater - Panama City, FL at Publix Super Markets Employer: Publix Super Markets \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n As a Publix Pharmacy Associate, you’ll see how very satisfying it is to work for a company that is passionately devoted to its customers, to its associates, and to the wellness of the communities it serves. What sets our pharmacy departments apart is a genuine patient-centric environment with clinical services such as immunizations, MTM (medication therapy management), and much more!Publix is continually recognized as one of the b