hnology system and how it is used for both routine and complex prescription processingmentor others on Publix pharmacy best practices to maximize sales, minimize shrink while meeting customers’ needs, using programs such as auto refill and Sync Your Refillsproactively advance pharmacy clinical initiatives including Medication Therapy Management (MTM) and immunizationsmaintain a flexible work-week schedule in order to meet the needs of our customers, andassist in all other duties as assigned.The minimum qualifications for the position of Floating Pharmacist are:must be at least 18 years of agemust be a graduate of a school of pharmacymust have and maintain an unrestricted, state pharmacist licensemust not have active suspensions, sanctions, or other restrictions related to participation in a private, federal, or state health insurance program upon hire and thereafter andmust not have received an unacceptable result on a company-sponsored drug test within the last three yearsOther qualifications for the position of Floating Pharmacist include:be an immunizing pharmacist meeting the requirements as established by the state (or be scheduled to become an immunizer in the next set of training classes)effective communication and interpersonal skillsability to interpret and understand instructions and solve problemsnumerical and financial aptitude andknowledge of retail merchandising and inventory control. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 20:01:01 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11285973/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11284084 Senior Controls Engineer at Mohawk Technology, LLC Employer: Mohawk Technology, LLC \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n We are seeking a Senior Controls Engineer to join our team at our Delano or Menahga, MN office. We are open to making the Mohawk, MI location work for the right candidate. The Senior Controls Engineer will lead controls-related projects from start to finish. In this role, you'll be responsible for design, parts ordering, and making sure projects are on schedule and successful. You'll work with other engineers and customers and occasionally travel with the sales team for proposals.Role and ResponsibilitiesMentoring other controls engineersLeading controls-related projects ranging from 40 to 2,000+ hoursDesigning electrical and network systems and reviewing electrical drawing packagesPLC and HMI programmingWorking with the panel shop on control panelsCollaborating with various groups of engineers and customersMust satisfactorily comply with alcohol and controlled substance company policiesAdhere to all safety protocols and proceduresTraveling estimated at 20-30%Other duties as assignedPhysical RequirementsDriving a vehicle and flying to client and/or Mohawk Technology locationsMoving around large facilities on a frequent basis with multiple floors and roomsWorking long hours, typically 12+, in stressful, on-site environmentsWalking, standing, going up and down stairs, sitting, kneeling, crouching, and bending for extended periodsAbility to lift and carry up to 25 pounds on a regular basis and heavier weights on an infrequent basisAbility to work in varying temperatures and environments (e.g., construction sites, manufacturing floors)Wearing PPE that complies with customer and company safety standards, including safety-toed boots, hard hat, safety glasses, ear plugs, hair nets, smocks, and on occasion, arc flash PPEWorking HoursTypical office hours:8 am – 5 pmOccasional nights and weekendsOn-Site Hours:Hours may vary, but are typically 12+Occasional nights and weekendsPreferred Knowledge and SkillsMinimum 5 years of experience designing and programming control systemsMinimum 5 years managing controls-related projectsExperience with control system programming with PID loopsExperience with Rockwell Software (Studio 5000, FactoryTalk, etc.) and Rockwell/Allen Bradley hardware (PowerFlex, Kinetix, ControlLogix, CompactLogix, etc.)Network/communication design experienceAbility to specify electrical componen