fit offerings vary per agency* This job posting is for an opportunity at a Goosehead Insurance agency independently owned and operated by a local franchised Agency Owner. If you choose to apply for this position, you understand and acknowledge that your application and any information included with it will be submitted to the Agency Owner. If you are hired for this position, you also understand and acknowledge that the Agency Owner’s franchised business will be your employer, not Goosehead Insurance Agency, LLC, and that the Agency Owner is solely responsible for all decisions related to your employment, including hiring, firing, discipline, compensation, scheduling, and supervision. To learn more about our job opportunities, apply here. We look forward to speaking with you! Fri, 7 Aug 2026 16:25:43 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11284741/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11285566 Community Support Specialist (Adult & Youth) at Burrell Behavioral Health Employer: Burrell Behavioral Health \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n Job Description:Job Title: Community Support SpecialistLocation: Independence, MODepartment: Adult Community Services & Youth Community ServicesEmployment Type: Full-time Job Summary:Join our compassionate and collaborative team as a Community Support Specialist, where you will make a meaningful difference in the lives of individuals in your community. In this role, you will empower clients and their families to build strong foundations for long-term wellbeing and independence. You will utilize evidence-based techniques to create personalized plans that address specific needs, fostering growth, stability, and resilience. We are looking for individuals who are self-motivated, possess strong communication skills, and are dedicated to helping others. As a Community Support Specialist, you will provide community-based mental health services to children, adolescents, and adults. Your responsibilities will include assessment, diagnosis, treatment planning, and the implementation of interventions. You will collaborate with clients, families, and other stakeholders to develop and implement individualized treatment plans that address the client's specific needs and goals. This position offers…Employee Assistance Program – 24/7 counseling services, legal assistance, & financial consultation for you and your household at no costMileage Reimbursement – Company paid for work functions requiring travelEmployee Discounts – Hotels, Theme Parks & Attractions, College TuitionWorkplace Culture - An environment cultivating employee wellbeing, valuing each individual's humanity, and actively promoting a healthy, joyful workforce Key Responsibilities:Provide community-based mental health services, including assessment, diagnosis, treatment planning, and intervention implementation.Collaborate with clients, families, and stakeholders to develop and implement individualized treatment plans.Utilize a strengths-based approach that emphasizes empowerment, skill-building, and resilience.Provide behavioral interventions, including motivational interviewing and cognitive processing.Coordinate care with other service providers, including primary care physicians and community organizations.Maintain accurate and timely records of client interactions and progress.Participate in staff development activities to enhance knowledge and skills.Contribute to the organization's quality improvement initiatives.Develop and maintain relationships with key stakeholders involved in the client's care.Prepare for and facilitate PSR group sessions as pertinent to client treatment plan goals. Education, Experience, and/or Credential Qualifications:Bachelor’s degree in Psychology, Social Work, or other human services specialized field; orBachelor’s degree in an unrelated field with two years of related work experience; orAny four-year combination of higher education and two years of related work experience; orAssociate’s of Applied Science in Behavioral Health Support; orFour years of qualifying experience in delivering services to individuals with mental health disorders, substance use disorders, or developmental disabilities. Additional Qualifications:High school diploma with at least one year of experience in social services is required.A mental health professional as defined in the IL Administrative Code is strongly preferred.Adequate written skills to accurately complete required documentation within prescribed time frames.Skilled in case management and community support interventions. Physical Requirements:Sedentary work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently to lift, carry, push, or pull objects.Repetitive movements of hands, fingers, and arms for typing and/or writing during work shift. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 18:51:19 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11285566/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11285601 Employment Specialist at Burrell Behavioral Health Employer: Burrell Behavioral Health \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n Job Title: Employment SpecialistLocation: Independence, MODepartment: Supported Living & Employment ServicesEmployment Type: Full TimeShift: Monday-Friday (flexible CST)  Job Summary:Are you looking to make a positive impact in the lives of others? Do you want to work in a supportive and dynamic environment where you can grow your skills and advance your career? Join our team as an Employment Specialist in the Independence, Missouri area! Ignite your career aspirations and realize your full potential with our Employment Specialists — a dedicated team of experienced professionals committed to opening doors, expanding horizons, and accelerating your climb upwards on the ladder of success. Armed with insider knowledge, expansive networks, and an arsenal of proven techniques, our Employment Specialists serve as your trusted advisors, champions, and confidants throughout each stage of your professional journey.  Position Perks & Benefits:Top-notch training - initial, ongoing, comprehensive, and supportiveCareer mobility - advancement opportunities/promoting from withinWelcoming, warm, supportive - a work culture & environment that promotes your well-being, values you as human being, and encourages your health and happiness Key Responsibilities:Needs Assessment: Conduct thorough assessments to gauge clients' vocational abilities, limitations, interests, and aspirations, subsequently mapping out tailored career paths aligning with their strengths, weaknesses, and objectives.Labor Market Research: Scour job boards, classified ads, company websites, trade publications, industry reports, and economic forecasts to uncover promising leads, emerging trends, and shifting demands within the workforce.Job Development: Proactively generate employment opportunities by cold-calling businesses, attending networking events, distributing flyers, posting advertisements, and soliciting referrals from satisfied customers.Application Assistance: Support clients in completing paperwork, composing CVs, drafting cover letters, filling out forms, preparing résumés, updating LinkedIn profiles, and recording reference lists.Interview Coaching: Stage mock trials simulating real-world scenarios, refining answers to frequently asked questions, analyzing body language, practicing small talk, and eliminating nervous habits obstructing optimal performance.Follow-Up Protocols: Escort clients to interviews, debrief afterwards, supply thank-you cards, send follow-up emails, request feedback, and maintain open channels of communication until final decisions materialize.Placement Services: Mediate introductions, negotiate salary negotiations, coordinate orientation sessions, outline expectations, define job descriptions, allocate resources, assign mentors, and establish probation periods easing transitions.Accommodation Advocacy: Petition employers for reasonable accommodations absolving clients from performing tasks exceeding their functional limitations, thus averting undue burden, discrimination, and litigation risks.Longitudinal Support: Monitor clients' progression, troubleshoot difficulties, reinforce soft skills, celebrate milestones, and maintain constant vigilance over deteriorating circumstances warranting swift intervention. Education and/or Experience Qualifications:A high school diploma or equivalent certificate is required;An associates or bachelor's degree in an applicable field from an accredited institution is preferred.At least one year of experience providing employment services is preferred. Additional Qualifications:A valid driver's license and a reliable vehicle.Strong communication and interpersonal skills.Ability to work independently and as part of a team.Flexibility and adaptability in a fast-paced environment.Compassion, empathy, and a genuine desire to help others. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 18:58:50 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11285601/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11110549 Land Acquisitioner at D.R. Horton, Inc. Employer: D.R. Horton, Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n D.R. Horton, Inc., the largest homebuilder in the U.S., was founded in 1978 and is a publicly traded company on the New York Stock Exchange. It is engaged in the construction and sale of high quality homes designed principally for the entry-level and first time move-up markets. The Company also provides mortgage financing and title services for homebuyers through its mortgage and title subsidiaries. Please visit our website at www.drhorton.com for more information.D.R. Horton, Inc. is currently looking for an Land Acquisitioner for their Operations Department. The right candidate will acquire undeveloped land or finished lots for development.  Work with property owners, brokers, land developers, city officials and others to secure land. Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following. Other duties may be assigned.Coordinate, Secure and Organize Land Acquisition LeadsReceive and provide initial response plan for all new leads from outside sourcesPerform Title and municipal research and initial “cold call” inquiry for potential land leadsProvide initial meeting with seller and/or seller’s representativeProvide all pertinent property description information, seller demands, terms, conditions and contact information to managementPrepare letters of intentMaintain close relationships with land developers, brokers and land ownersUnderwrite and analyze the financial aspects of each development opportunityCommunicate regularly with city officialsNegotiate purchase contracts with sellersConduct all business in a professional and ethical manner to serve customers and increase the goodwill and profit of the companyAble to travel overnight QualificationsEducation and/or ExperienceFifth year college or university program certificateFour to six years related experience and/or trainingProficiency with MS Office and email Preferred QualificationsStrong communication skillsAbility to multi-task and attention to detail Come join a winning team with a Fortune 500 company! We are growing fast and are looking for enthusiastic attitudes and team players to join our success. We offer an excellent benefits package including:Medical, Vision and Dental401(K)Employee Stock Purchase PlanFlex Spending AccountsLife InsuranceVacation, Sick, Personal Time and Company Holidays Build YOUR future with D.R. Horton, America’s Builder. #WeBuildPeopleToo Mon, 8 Jun 2026 18:12:55 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11110549/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11284315 Analyst, Business Services M&A at Lincoln International Employer: Lincoln International \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n Lincoln International, Inc. (NYSE: LCLN) is a trusted investment banking advisor to business owners and senior executives of leading private equity firms and their portfolio companies and to public and privately held companies. Our services include mergers and acquisitions advisory, private funds and capital markets advisory, and valuations and fairness opinions. The global enterprise is comprised of a tightly integrated team of more than 1,400 professionals in more than 30 offices in 14 countries, offering an unobstructed perspective on the global private capital markets, backed by superb execution and a deep commitment to client success. With extensive industry knowledge and relationships, timely market intelligence and strategic insights, we forge deep, productive client relationships that endure for decades. Connect with us to learn more at www.lincolninternational.com. At Lincoln International, we know that the success of our global organization is a direct outcome of the strength of our people. We encourage diversity of thought and create talent density by attracting, retaining and engaging high performers from all demographics, backgrounds and perspectives. We value diversity, equity and inclusion as a catalyst to foster innovation and creative problem solving, access the best candidates and adapt to a highly dynamic, competitive environment. We know that employing a diverse team and valuing the unique perspectives of our people allows us to better understand and serve the needs of our clients.Lincoln International is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. We encourage you to read more about our commitment to diversity and Environmental, Social & Governance (ESG) efforts.Duties & Responsibilities:Lincoln International is seeking an Analyst to join our rapidly growing Business Services, M&A practice in Richmond, VA.  Successful candidates have strong cognitive and interpersonal abilities, want to develop their professional and personal skills, and are motivated by the prospect of building a leading M&A advisory firm. The Analyst position at Lincoln International provides an excellent opportunity to work in a demanding, yet supportive, team-oriented environment. In addition to mastering the financial analysis and research skills typical for the position, an Analyst at Lincoln International learns about and becomes involved in a transaction from start to finish. The Analyst serves as the analytical anchor for his/her deal team and is responsible for preparing, completing, and ensuring the accuracy of all financial modeling and analysis. The Analyst is expected to interpret the results of his/her financial analysis, pose questions, and draw conclusions. In addition, the Analyst plays a critical role in the preparation of client presentations and is responsible for:Preparing marketing materials for sell-side and buy-side M&A assignmentsIdentifying potential acquirers / targetsConducting industry and company-specific researchEnsuring the accuracy and quality of all presentation materialsSupporting the due diligence processInteracting with clients on a regular basisAttending client meetingsSupporting the marketing activities of the firm as they relate to an industry or engagementThe firm offers a unique, flexible culture that rewards initiative and allows an Analyst to develop as quickly as capable. The following factors differentiate the Analyst program at Lincoln International:Responsibilities are limited only by ability rather than by a formal job descriptionHigh levels of exposure to senior professionals within the firmUnparalleled client interactionOpportunity to remain with Lincoln International and be promoted to Associate and beyondOpportunity to contribute to Lincoln International’s global growth and work overseasQualifications:The Analyst position at Lincoln International is extremely challenging, offers an excellent learning experience and provides a solid foundation upon which an individual can build a future business career. Interested candidates should meet the following requirements:Successful Analysts are assertive and self-motivated, can manage multiple tasks and deadlines in a fast-paced environment and are detail-orientedStrong writing, verbal communication, and computer skills (Excel, PowerPoint, Word)Bachelor's degree required2-3 years of experience in sell-side M&A requiredREQUIRED: Minimum GPA of 3.5Additional Information:Lincoln International is not currently hiring individuals for this position who now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status.Click here to view Lincoln International's Candidate Privacy Notices.Lincoln International is a trade name for Lincoln International, Inc. and its subsidiaries and affiliates, which include the following licensed entities: (i) Lincoln International LLC and MarshBerry Capital, LLC (United States), SEC-registered broker-dealers and a members of FINRA (www.finra.org) and SIPC (www.sipc.org) (investment banking services) and (ii) Lincoln International LLP (FRN 474606) and IMAS Corporate Finance LLP (FRN 553889) (United Kingdom), authorized and regulated by the U.K. Financial Conduct Authority. No entity affiliated with Lincoln International, LP provides banking or securities brokerage services, nor is any such affiliate subject to FINMA supervision in Switzerland or similar regulatory authorities regarding such activities in other jurisdictions. Retail clients are NOT the intended recipients of our communications or services and should not act upon this communication.© 2026 Lincoln International LLC. All Rights Reserved.110 North Wacker Drive | 51st Floor | Chicago | Illinois | 60606 | United States. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 15:13:39 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11284315/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11110524 Budget Coordinator at D.R. Horton, Inc. Employer: D.R. Horton, Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n D.R. Horton, Inc., the largest homebuilder in the U.S., was founded in 1978 and is a publicly traded company on the New York Stock Exchange. It is engaged in the construction and sale of high quality homes designed principally for the entry-level and first time move-up markets. The Company also provides mortgage financing and title services for homebuyers through its mortgage and title subsidiaries.  Please visit our website at www.drhorton.com for more information.D.R. Horton, Inc. is currently looking for a Budget Coordinator for their Main Office Department. The right candidate will be responsible for coordinating budgets and purchase orders. Essential Duties and ResponsibilitiesCreate a structured cost budget for each home based on basic bids, contract pricing and upgraded item processingRun each home with options and item numbers in different cost codes to create report of overall profit for production of each jobUse report for true cost of goods to ensure PMI is high and resources are high quality QualificationsEducation and/or ExperienceAssociate's degree (A. A.) or equivalent from two-year College or technical school; or one to two years related experience and/or training; or equivalent combination of education and experience. Come join a winning team with a Fortune 500 company! We are growing fast and are looking for enthusiastic attitudes and team players to join our success. We offer an excellent benefits package including:Medical, Dental and Vision401(K)Employee Stock Purchase PlanFlex Spending AccountsLife & Disability InsuranceVacation, Sick, Personal Time and Company HolidaysMultiple Voluntary and Company provided Benefits Build YOUR future with D.R. Horton, America’s Builder. #WeBuildPeopleToo Mon, 8 Jun 2026 18:26:09 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11110524/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11285498 Teacher Aide/Assistant (Early Childhood Education) at Educare of Omaha, Inc. Employer: Educare of Omaha, Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n GENERAL DESCRIPTION Educare of Omaha, Inc. is a collaborative partnership between the Early Head Start/Head Start, Omaha Public Schools and the Buffett Early Childhood Fund. Comprised of the two Educare Omaha Schools (Kellom and Indian Hill) and the three Early Learning Centers (Skinner, Gateway and Kennedy), the mission of Educare of Omaha, Inc. is to promote school readiness by enhancing the social and cognitive development of children ages 0 to 5 years through the provision of evidence-based education, health, nutritional, social, family engagement and other services to enrolled children and their families.    The Teacher Aide is responsible for assisting the Lead Teacher and Associate Teacher in the planning, implementation and coordination of a comprehensive education program. Under the supervision of the Lead Teacher and the Associate Teacher, the Teacher Aide ensures the education program is developmentally appropriate and meets children’s individual needs as well as program standards of Educare of Omaha, Inc. and the Nebraska Department of Education. Schedule: This position is full-time, 40 hours per week, Monday-Friday. There is a variation of schedules available with the hours falling between 7:00am-5:30pm.  DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIESChild Development  Provide opportunities for children to develop positive self-images and experience success.Assist in the development and the implementation of an individualized educational plan for each child.Contribute information for child and family staffing.Provide information to the Lead Teacher, Associate Teacher, MTS/Coach, and other service providers that will assist in the education of a child.Assist the child and family as child transitions from the infant and toddler program to the preschool program and from the preschool program to kindergarten.Foster positive relationships with all children in the classroom.Classroom Management Assist in developing and maintaining an attractive and stimulating learning environment and assist in encouraging a child’s independence and self-selection of activities.Ensure that all children are always under appropriate supervision and guidance.Maintain a clean, safe, and healthy classroom environment.Utilize Positive Behavior Support strategies.Assist with the timely completion of necessary paperwork, including developmental assessments, lesson plans, newsletters, incident reports, etc.Participate in reflective supervision.Curriculum  Assist the Lead Teacher and Associate Teacher in planning and implementing developmentally appropriate classroom activities that will enhance (1) language and literacy development, (2) cognition and general knowledge, (3) approaches toward learning, (4) physical well-being and motor development, and (5) social and emotional development of each child.Assist in the process of interpreting and analyzing assessment results by collecting data that Lead Teachers and Associate Teachers will utilize to plan individual and classroom experiences as well as contributing to the collection of progress of children so that Lead Teachers and Associate Teachers can intentionally share this information with families.Assist in developing lesson plans with goals, objectives, activities, and outcomes for children and implement them intentionally.Assist in creating documentation panels on a regular basis to make the learning that the children are experiencing visible to parents and visitors.Write anecdotal observations for the development of individualized plans for children and for measuring and evaluating child progress.Parent Involvement  Encourage parent participation in program activities and in implementing education activities for their children at home and in the community.Communicate with parents (informal conversations, newsletters, personal notes) regarding his/her child’s involvement in classroom activities and progress towards learning goals.As assigned by the Lead Teacher and Associate Teacher, communicate with parents regularly about their child’s progress  EDUCATION/QUALIFICATIONSHigh School Diploma or equivalent required.CDA is required, and if not possessed or current must be obtained in the first 12 months of employment.Two years early childhood experience in a group setting preferred.Must be able to pass a background check that meets compliance standards. Educare of Omaha, Inc. is committed to ensuring equal opportunity and non-discrimination in all hiring and employment practices. We are committed to equal treatment for all applicants and employees and will not discriminate based on age, race, color, ancestry, national origin, disability, sex/gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, pregnancy, genetic information, veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. Equal Opportunity Employer Fri, 7 Aug 2026 18:34:00 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11285498/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/10686171 Technical Sales Engineer - Omaha, NE at Logic, Inc. Employer: Logic, Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n                                Technical Sales Engineer - Omaha, NELogic, Inc. is currently seeking applicants for the position of Technical Sales Engineer for our Omaha, NE office. The field of sales engineering is a hybrid of combining the technical and problem-solving skills of an engineer with the relational competencies and desire for customer satisfaction of a salesperson. Our sales engineers utilize their engineering background and knowledge of the solutions offered through Logic, Inc., and consult customers on what products fit the application space.   Responsibilities: As an outside sales engineer, you will be working with manufacturers, utilities, consultants, and systems integrators in the sales and support of hardware and software automation products in our Omaha, NE territory. Logic Inc. offers products for machine and process control, software for industrial applications, and precision motion control.   • Develop new accounts through networking, vendor coordination, and market research • Provide quotations, place orders, submit documents, and provide technical assistance • Prepare and deliver technical demonstrations that provide solutions to fit application needs • Travel within the territory via company car to develop and maintain customer          relationships • Continue learning new technologies, products, and industrial applications Preferred Experience: • Experience with PLCs, VFDs, industrial communications, industrial software, or precision motion is helpful • Degree in automation, mechanical engineering, or electrical engineering • Establish relationships with existing customers in the Omaha, NE area • Must understand industry engineering design concepts and practices • Experience in developing presentations and sales quotes with the ability to explain technical concepts • Excellent interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills • Able to manage time effectively, organize your material, and perform quality work without being micromanaged. What We Offer: • Competitive salary & bonus package • Full benefits package including medical and excellent retirement benefits • Paid holidays and vacation, personal, sick time • Company-provided cell phone, laptop, software, supplies, and company vehicle • Great working environment with a team approach to sales. Who We Are: Logic, Inc. is a regional high-tech distributor that provides solutions and services with control products to aid engineers, system integrators, OEMs, IT, and management professionals in process manufacturing industries. Our corporate headquarters is in Olathe, Kansas, with sales offices in Wichita, KS, St. Louis, MO, Springfield, MO, Des Moines, IA, and Omaha, NE.  Visit us online. Send in your resume today to resumes@logic-control.com. Tue, 27 Jan 2026 17:48:32 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/10686171/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11284717 Entry-Level Sales - Account Executive at Goosehead Insurance Employer: Goosehead Insurance \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n About GooseheadSince 2003, Goosehead Insurance has been disrupting the insurance industry by giving clients the power of choice, utilizing a smarter marketing approach, and delivering world-class service. This is all powered by our focus on hiring and retaining extraordinary people. Our clients trust us with their most valuable possessions, so we’re more than just a bit selective when it comes to hiring new team members. In 2012, we began franchising our business model. This role is for one of our successful franchise partners at the Taxman, Agency in Denver, CO. Job SummaryThe team is responsible for new business revenue generation monthly and works to achieve these on an individual and team level. Account Executives are equipped with extensive training in Salesforce, sales process management, business development and more. Principal Duties and ResponsibilitiesThe primary responsibility of an Account Executive is to build a book of business through:Prospecting and establishing referral partner relationships with professionals from the real estate and mortgage industry.Work with clients to understand their insurance needs, analyze options with a large carrier portfolio, and provide a custom solution to mitigate household risk. Compensation SummaryThe first year’s earnings potential ranges from $53,000 - $90,000, varying based on performance. Our compensation package slightly varies by agency but offers uncapped new business commissions and renewal commissions year-over-year. Renewal commissions provide passive earnings and can exponentially increase your annualized income. Additionally, top performers can qualify for an annual President’s Club trip. Experience and EducationPassing the state licensing exam, once hiredLegally authorized to work in the United States Required Skills and AbilitiesExceptional written and verbal communicationExperience in a fast-paced work environmentB2B or B2C sales experience or related college majorCompetitive attitudeNetworking abilitiesEntrepreneurial spiritProblem-solving mentalitySelf-motivated, hands on, self-starter mindset that can do the workStrong time managementStrong attention to detail and organization Benefits SummaryHigh quality voluntary health, vision, dental insurance programsPaid holidays, vacation, and sick leaveBenefit offerings vary per agency* This job posting is for an opportunity at a Goosehead Insurance agency independently owned and operated by a local franchised Agency Owner. If you choose to apply for this position, you understand and acknowledge that your application and any information included with it will be submitted to the Agency Owner. If you are hired for this position, you also understand and acknowledge that the Agency Owner’s franchised business will be your employer, not Goosehead Insurance Agency, LLC, and that the Agency Owner is solely responsible for all decisions related to your employment, including hiring, firing, discipline, compensation, scheduling, and supervision. To learn more about our job opportunities, apply here. We look forward to speaking with you! Fri, 7 Aug 2026 16:27:35 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11284717/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11286125 Community Outreach Coordinator at Oaklight Environmental Consulting Employer: Oaklight Environmental Consulting \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n Community Outreach CoordinatorOaklight is seeking a detail oriented Community Outreach Coordinator to support our project teams across stakeholder outreach, meeting and event logistics, and communications. This role is a great fit for someone who thrives on staying organized across multiple priorities, enjoys working directly with clients and community stakeholders, and takes pride in producing clean, accurate written materials.You'll coordinate schedules and logistics across active projects, prepare meeting materials and documentation, support stakeholder research and outreach, help plan and staff in person and virtual events, and draft or edit communications ranging from fact sheets to presentations. You'll also play a key role in keeping our records, files, and databases organized and accurate.We're looking for someone who is a strong communicator, comfortable representing Oaklight professionally in public settings, and confident managing detail heavy work without losing sight of the bigger picture.Why join Oaklight?If you're looking for a role where every day looks the same, this probably isn't it. At Oaklight, you'll support projects across multiple states, work directly with experienced professionals, and gain exposure to everything from stakeholder outreach and public meetings to project planning, communications, and client support. You’ll be trusted with real responsibility from day one.Why you?You're organized, dependable, and detail-oriented. You can manage multiple priorities without losing track of the details. You communicate well with a wide range of people, aren't intimidated by new situations, and take pride in doing the job well. Most importantly, you're curious, resourceful, and willing to learn. You know when to ask questions and seek help. You support your teammates and represent Oaklight professionally wherever a project takes you.Key Responsibilities Project Coordination & AdministrationManage assignments across multiple projects, project managers, and project teams.Coordinate project logistics, schedules, meetings, and events.Prepare meeting materials, outreach materials, and project documentation.Draft meeting notes, summaries, and other project documentation.Coordinate with clients, venues, vendors, and project partners as needed tosupport project activities.Enter time and expenses accurately and in a timely manner.Support general office operations and contribute to administrative functions as needed to ensure the efficient execution of projects and business activities.Stakeholder Outreach & ResearchConduct stakeholder, community, and project research.Develop, maintain, and update stakeholder databases and contact lists.Document and track stakeholder communications, inquiries, and responses.Communicate with stakeholders in person, over the phone, and in writing.Meeting & Event SupportAssist with planning, logistics, and staffing for in-person and virtual meetings, open houses, workshops, and community events.Support meeting set-up and breakdown, attendee registration, and event logistics.Provide technical support for virtual meetings using platforms such as Microsoft Teams and Zoom.Represent Oaklight professionally at public meetings and community events.Take accurate notes during meetings and project discussions.Communications & Materials DevelopmentDraft, edit, and proofread fact sheets, newsletters, website content, presentations, correspondence, and other project materials.Assist with the development of PowerPoint presentations and public-facingmaterials.Support website updates, digital engagement activities, and social media content as needed.Review outreach materials and project documents for completeness, consistency, and accuracy.Documentation & Records ManagementSupport project mailings, including database management, mail merges, printing, and distribution.Transcribe comments, sign-in sheets, and other project records.Scan, organize, and maintain digital project files and documentation.Assist with document control and records management activities. Required QualificationsStrong organizational skills and exceptional attention to detail.Strong written and verbal communication skills.Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines simultaneously.Ability to work independently while contributing effectively as part of a team.Professional maturity, sound judgment, and a strong sense of accountability.Ability to communicate professionally with clients, stakeholders, and team members in person, over the phone, and in writing.Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, including Word, Excel, and PowerPoint.Flexibility to occasionally work evenings, weekends, and travel based on project needs.Ability to work in a hybrid environment, including regular attendance at Oaklight's Austin office.Valid driver’s license and reliable transportation.Bonus PointsExperience with public involvement, community engagement, stakeholder outreach, or relationship-building.Experience coordinating meetings, events, open houses, workshops, orcommunity events.Experience maintaining stakeholder databases, contact lists, or project tracking systems.Graphic design experience, including Adobe Creative Suite, Canva, or similar tools.Proficiency in Spanish.Experience developing presentations, newsletters, websites, or other communications materials.Familiarity with survey platforms and digital engagement tools such as SurveyMonkey, Mailchimp, Mentimeter, Microsoft Forms, or Google Forms.Project management or project coordination experience.Ability to find the typo everyone else missed.Education and ExperienceBachelor's degree in communications, public relations, journalism, marketing, planning, environmental studies, political science, or a related field.Compensation & BenefitsWe believe great people deserve competitive compensation, flexibility, and benefits that support life both inside and outside of work. Oaklight offers competitive pay and benefits including, health, retirement planning, paid holidays, paid time off, and flexible work schedule, depending on project and client needsThe anticipated salary range for this position is $50,000-$60,000 annually. Compensation will be commensurate with experience.To apply, please submit a cover letter, resume, and three references to jobs@oaklight.com. You may be asked to provide examples of project work. Oaklight will maintain confidentiality throughout the application and interview process. Oaklight will accept applications for this position on an ongoing, rolling basis and reserves the right to cancel this posting at any time. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 20:16:14 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11286125/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11286610 Commercial Property Manager at Riverway Realty Investment Corporation Employer: Riverway Realty Investment Corporation \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n Commercial Property ManagerLocation: Houston, TXCompany: Riverway PropertiesPosition SummaryRiverway Properties is seeking an experienced, organized, and customer-focused Commercial Property Manager to oversee the daily operations of our growing portfolio of commercial properties. The ideal candidate will be responsible for maintaining strong tenant relationships, maximizing property performance, coordinating maintenance, managing budgets, and ensuring each property is maintained to the highest standards.This is an excellent opportunity for someone who enjoys working in a fast-paced environment and takes pride in delivering exceptional service while protecting and enhancing asset value.Key ResponsibilitiesManage the day-to-day operations of a portfolio of commercial properties.Serve as the primary point of contact for tenants and respond promptly to questions and concerns.Coordinate maintenance, repairs, landscaping, janitorial services, and vendor contracts.Conduct regular property inspections and identify maintenance or safety issues.Manage operating budgets, approve invoices, and monitor expenses.Work with ownership on annual budgets, capital improvement projects, and long-term planning.Oversee lease administration, including renewals, rent escalations, and tenant move-ins/move-outs.Ensure timely rent collections and coordinate with accounting regarding delinquencies.Solicit bids, negotiate vendor contracts, and monitor contractor performance.Ensure compliance with local building codes, safety regulations, insurance requirements, and property standards.Prepare monthly management reports detailing occupancy, financial performance, maintenance activities, and tenant issues.Coordinate with leasing agents regarding available spaces and tenant improvements.Build positive relationships with tenants to promote high retention and satisfaction.QualificationsProficiency with Microsoft Office. QuickBooks is a plus. Knowledge of Tenant billing, commercial leases, CAM reconciliations, budgeting, and property operations.Ability to travel to properties around Houston area, conduct inspections with valid drivers license.Preferred SkillsStrong financial and budgeting experience.Experience managing retail, office, or mixed-use properties.Ability to negotiate vendor contracts and oversee capital improvement projects.Problem-solving mindset with excellent attention to detail.Professional, positive, and team-oriented attitude.Compensation and BenefitsSalary commensurate with experience.Health Benefits and vehicle allowanceAbout Riverway PropertiesRiverway Properties is a Houston-based real estate company committed to delivering exceptional commercial and residential properties through proactive management, quality service, and long-term relationships. We take pride in maintaining attractive, well-managed properties while providing outstanding service to our tenants and ownership. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 22:08:50 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11286610/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11285502 Direct Support Professional- Caregiver (Full & Part Time) at Burrell Behavioral Health Employer: Burrell Behavioral Health \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n Job Description:Job Title: Direct Support Professional (CAREGIVER)Company: Firefly (Supportive Living & Employment Services)Job Location: North KC (includes Platte City, Gladstone and Independence) & South KC (includes Lees Summit, Blue Springs, and Raytown)Employment Type: Full Time & Part time Available: **No experience necessary! We provide free training!****We just need your compassionate, caring heart!**  Job Summary:Are you passionate about making a positive impact in people's lives? Do you want to work in a fulfilling career where you can help others reach their full potential? As a Caregiver (Direct Support Professional), you'll have the opportunity to do just that! If you are compassionate and dedicated to helping others improve their lives, you can look forward to a rewarding career of providing support services to adults with intellectual and developmental disabilities, enriching their lives while making a living!  You will assist clients with daily tasks, promote their independence, and help them achieve their personal goals. Don’t miss out on this rewarding opportunity to make a positive impact on someone's life as well as yours!   As a Caregiver, you will be able to enjoy:Employee Benefits Package - paid time off, health insurance, dental, vision, retirement, life, & more (full-time 30 hours or more)Employee Discounts - Verizon, AT&T, and moreEmployee Assistance Program - counseling, legal aid, and financial guidance at no cost to youMileage Reimbursement - company paid for work functions requiring travelTop-Notch Training - initial, ongoing, comprehensive, and supportiveCareer Advancement Opportunities - promoting from withinWelcoming, Warm, Supportive Work Culture - an environment that promotes your well-being, values you as human being, and encourages your health and happiness  What you’ll get to do as a Caregiver:Help developmentally disabled clients in their homes and communitiesHelp clients to access community resources and participate in social activitiesProvide transportation to clients out into the community for appointments and shoppingTeach clients to live independently, including cooking, cleaning, and managing moneyHelp clients with daily tasks, like personal care and hygieneWrite notes about client progress and achievementsCommunicate the client’s progress with clients, families, and staffUnderstand and follow the client's Individual Support Plan (ISP)Attend meetings and training sessionsPerform other duties as assigned Qualifications:High school diploma or equivalentGood communication and people skillsAbility to work alone and as part of a teamBasic computer skillsReliable transportation and valid driver's license (if applicable)Pass a background check Work Environment:Work mostly in clients' homes and communities, with some travelMay require lifting or moving objects up to 50 poundsWork in various settings, including private homes, public spaces, and outdoorsMust be able to work varying shifts, including weekends Thank you for considering this opportunity to make a positive impact on the lives of adults with intellectual and developmental disabilities! We look forward to hearing from you soon!  Embrace Our Supportive Culture:At Firefly, we foster a culture where our associates are treasured as our greatest asset. We recognize that their fulfillment directly influences the exceptional services we provide. As a valued member of our team, you will be embraced by a supportive environment that encourages your growth and empowers you to harness your strengths through continuous training and professional development opportunities. Position Perks & Benefits:Paid time off: full-time employees receive an attractive time off package to balance your work and personal lifeEmployee benefits package: full-time employees receive health, dental, vision, retirement, life, & moreTop-notch training: initial, ongoing, comprehensive, and supportiveCareer mobility: advancement opportunities/promoting from withinWelcoming, warm, supportive: a work culture & environment that promotes your well-being, values you as human being, and encourages your health and happiness Fri, 7 Aug 2026 18:36:33 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11285502/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11286757 Electrical Design Validation Engineer at Nexthop Employer: Nexthop \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n Nexthop Systems Inc. is seeking an electrical design validation engineer to validate next-generation high-capacity networking systems for emerging AI infrastructures. In this role, you’ll combine technical expertise with innovative problem-solving to plan & execute all the qualifications of cutting-edge system designs that meet the demands of advanced data centers and telecom environments.   What You BringQualifications:Bachelor’s or higher degree in Electrical Engineering.  0-5 years of experience in Electrical design validation for telecom or data center product development.   What You’ll DoDevelop detailed test plans to characterize and validate systems, subassemblies or components as per industry or internal specifications by working closely with HW design (electrical, thermal, power, optics etc.)Support HW bring up, and contract manufacturing NPIE with any electrical qualifications, debugging and test script supportWork closely with the cross-functional teams to co-ordinate test cost, schedule and address cross-functional dependencies e.g. HW allocation, SW readiness.Procure test equipment and resources to complete scheduled tests in a timely mannerAnalyze test results, find product design issues, log bugs using tracking software, report realtime status with adequate details, recommend corrective action, drive resolution and verify fixes Review, edit, and release test reports for the products testedEvaluate technical readiness prior to release to manufacturingLearn and improve test cost, consistency, and efficiency proactively  Technical Skills:  Solid understanding of networking product design & operationStrong knowledge of hardware environmental stress testing through voltage and temperature margin using automated test scripts using PythonExperience with configuring networking products using OS & traffic generator (IXIA, Smartbits etc) to run different types of traffic and protocols to stress critical components, optical modules, interfaces, data and control paths Ability to automate test setup to control devices under test, environmental test chambers, test equipment (traffic generator, scope etc.)  Familiarity with signal & power integrity, reliability and qualityHands-on experience with HW bring up e.g.  I2C, PCIe, SMBUS, SERDES, & SOCWorking knowledge of various optics types OSFP, QSFP etc Hands-On Expertise: Conducting Electrical & Environmental stress tests using automated script and environmental chambersWriting test script to control test equipments Configuring networking products using standalone diagnostic and OSDebugging issues found during testing using high speed scope, & logic analyzerTesting various optical modules &  liquid cool products is a plusSoft Skills:Strong collaboration and communication skills to work effectively across cross-functional teams in a fast-paced environment.  A problem-solving mindset with a focus on delivering results while managing technical risks and tradeoffs.  Ability to adapt and thrive in a dynamic and innovative environment.  Why Join Nexthop Systems?At Nexthop, you’ll have the opportunity to contribute to the evolution of AI infrastructure. Work alongside experts in cutting-edge technologies, contribute to industry-defining projects, and make a tangible impact in the rapidly evolving networking and data center landscape. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 23:32:43 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11286757/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11284851 Marketing Manager at KPER Technologies Inc. Employer: KPER Technologies Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n Location: Irvine, CA (Hybrid)Employment Type: Full-TimeAbout KPERKPER is an automotive technology startup building a peer-to-peer car exchange platform that helps enthusiasts discover, swap, and experience unique vehicles. We're creating a trusted community where members can access everything from sports cars and exotics to daily drivers—all through a seamless digital platform.As we launch, we're looking for a Marketing Manager who can build brand awareness, grow our community, and execute creative campaigns that drive user acquisition.ResponsibilitiesDevelop and execute KPER's overall marketing strategy across digital and offline channels.Plan and manage social media campaigns on Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, Reddit, and other relevant platforms.Create and oversee content calendars, email marketing, and community engagement initiatives.Collaborate with creators, influencers, automotive clubs, and media partners to expand KPER's reach.Manage paid advertising campaigns (Meta, Google, TikTok, etc.) and optimize customer acquisition costs.Analyze campaign performance using analytics tools and provide actionable insights.Coordinate event marketing, including automotive meets, track days, and industry events.Work closely with product, design, and leadership teams to launch new features and promotions.Build and maintain KPER's brand identity and messaging across all channels.QualificationsBachelor's degree in Marketing, Business, Communications, or a related field.3+ years of experience in digital marketing, growth marketing, or brand marketing.Strong understanding of social media trends and performance marketing.Experience with Meta Ads, Google Ads, Google Analytics, and email marketing platforms.Excellent communication and project management skills.Self-starter who thrives in a fast-paced startup environment.Passion for cars, automotive culture, or enthusiast communities is highly preferred.Preferred QualificationsExperience working with startups or technology companies.Experience managing influencer marketing campaigns.Familiarity with SEO, CRM platforms, and marketing automation tools.Basic graphic design or video editing experience is a plus.What You'll GetOpportunity to help build a rapidly growing automotive startup from the ground up.High ownership with direct impact on company growth.Flexible work environment.Competitive salary plus equity opportunities based on experience.Access to automotive events, creator collaborations, and a passionate enthusiast community.If you're passionate about marketing, cars, and building a brand from the ground up, we'd love to hear from you. Join KPER and help redefine how people experience driving. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 16:46:53 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11284851/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11285769 Sales Development Representative at BackStretch Employer: BackStretch \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n Now is the time to join this transportation and logistics company in massive growth!Why apply today?Room to actually grow — Over 60% of new hires say they joined for the growth, and they're not wrong. This company genuinely promotes from within, backs it up with real training, and gives you the tools to move up.Get rewarded for your effort — Competitive base salary plus an uncapped commission structure means your earning potential isn't decided for you. How far you go is largely up to you.Experience isn’t everything, energy matters — You don't need to have done it all before. If you bring the soft skills, the hustle, and a willingness to learn, this is a place that will meet you where you are and help you figure out the rest.A team that moves fast and builds real things — High energy, collaborative environment, and a product that's genuinely leading in the industry. It's the kind of place where you'll actually feel the work matters.Excellent benefits plan — medical, dental, vision plans, 401(k) retirement plan with up to 5% company match, Career and Leadership Development Programs, and the list goes onThe companyBringing together massive carrier capacity, cutting-edge technology, and industry-leading logistics expertise - they are creating more efficient ways for shippers and carriers to move freight across North America, and they're looking for sharp, energetic people to help them do it.The roleThe sales team is expanding, and this Sales Development Representative role exists to drive new business development across a growing customer base. You'll be responsible for identifying, prospecting, and closing new accounts while managing the full lifecycle of those relationships.This is not a passive role. When opportunities move, you move with them. What you'll do on a typical day:Identify and develop new business opportunities through research, trusted sources, and direct outreach to prospectsNegotiate with customers to secure profitable rates, terms, and sustainable relationshipsManage load entry, tracking, reporting, and account activity within internal systemsCoordinate with operations to understand carrier capacity, equipment needs, and logistics requirementsBuild and maintain relationships with customers, ensuring they feel supported and valuedWork collaboratively with teammates to solve problems creatively and close dealsTake ownership of your accounts and work to continuously improve your speed and effectivenessWhat you need to succeedSelf-starter mentality: you're comfortable operating independently while staying connected to the teamStrong communication skills: you'll interact with customers, internal teams, and operational partners with clarity and professionalismProblem-solving ability and resourcefulness: you'll find creative ways to structure deals and overcome obstaclesEmotional intelligence and genuine relationship-building skills: you'll adapt your approach to different personalities and business stylesHunger and drive: success in this role rewards effort and resultsNice to haveExperience in transportation, logistics, brokerage, or supply chainA background in sales, business development, or account managementCold calling or prospecting experienceA track record that demonstrates resilience and determinationThe detailsLocation: The team has recently relocated to a new office in the West End, St. Louis Park Area Compensation: Strong base salary + benefits on day one. Expected average 1st year compensation between 55k to 70k (highest achievers earn more as there is uncapped commissions) Work environment: 5 days a week in-office. Hours are flexible (7 AM–4 PM or 8 AM–5 PM). Your benefits includeComprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans401(k) retirement plan with up to 5% company matchPre-tax accounts for eligible expensesCompany-paid disability and life insuranceEmployee Assistance Program (EAP)Career and Leadership Development ProgramsPaid time off, company holidays, and volunteer daysApply today!  No cover letter required. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 19:29:16 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11285769/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11285549 Shop Foreman Lead Technician at Belfanti Machine Works LLC Employer: Belfanti Machine Works LLC \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n Shop Foreman / Lead Technician — We Are Not Your Father's Machine ShopBelfanti Machine Works — Beaverton, ORWe're a precision CNC and fabrication shop building the next era of American manufacturing — and we're looking for a foreman/technician who's as comfortable dialing in a 5-axis toolpath as they are thinking about robotics, data, and how work actually flows across the floor.This is not a \"run the same part for 20 years\" job. We machine everything from aerospace and defense components to consumer product tooling. We run Haas machining centers (VF-2/VF-4/DM2), a Litz LU-620 5-axis, and we're actively investing in automation. We use modern CAD (Fusion 360, Inventor), digital tool-crib systems we built in-house, and AI-assisted workflows for quoting, planning, and shop-floor management. If you geek out on making a shop smarter, you'll fit right in.What you'll own:Lead the floor — schedule jobs, mentor machinists, and run the shop like it's yours. You set the standard for quality and pace.Value stream engineering — map how work moves from RFQ to shipped part, kill bottlenecks, and drive real Lean/continuous-improvement (not clipboard theater).Robotics & automation — help us spec, deploy, and run automation (bar feeders, pallet systems, cobots, lights-out cells). We're building toward it and want someone hungry to lead it.Technology & AI workflows — work alongside custom software and AI tools we use for quoting, tool management, scheduling, and quality. Your feedback shapes what we build next.Team building — grow and coach a small, sharp crew. We're rolling out a structured onboarding and skills program and want you helping run it.Own the process — CNC setup, first-article inspection, and quality to AS9100/ISO-grade standards.What we're looking for:Fusion 360 CAM experience is a must — you program your own toolpaths in Fusion 360 and know how to structure jobs using container methods (organized setups, folders, and reusable templates) to keep programming clean, consistent, and repeatable.Proven CNC machining experience (5-axis and multi-axis a big plus) — mill and lathe.Real leadership: you've run a floor, led a team, or been the person everyone goes to.  Comfortable with digital/data-driven tools. Bonus if you're already using AI in your workflow.A Lean / value-stream / continuous-improvement mindset — you see waste and can't help but fix it.Interest in (or experience with) robotics and shop automation.Reads blueprints and GD&T cold; holds tight tolerances without drama.U.S. Person status required (we do ITAR-controlled defense work).The details:Pay: $28–$38/hr DOE — with room to grow as you take on operations leadership.Hours: 10 AM–6 PM, plus overtime as needed.Why us: Modern, growing shop that actually invests in technology and its people. Real ownership and a direct line to the owner — no corporate layers. A seat at the table as we build something ambitious.Create. Innovate. Customize. If you want to help build a smarter machine shop instead of just clocking hours at one, reply to this post with your resume and a couple sentences on the coolest thing you've ever made or improved. Fri, 7 Aug 2026 18:44:45 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11285549/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/10275868 Advertising Sales Account Executive at Empower Atlanta Magazine Employer: Empower Atlanta Magazine \n\n Expires: 09/07/2026 \n\n We are searching for an outgoing, self-motivated person with an entrepreneurial mindset for our Advertising Sales Account Executive position. We seek individuals with at least one year of print and/or digital advertising sales experience and a strong background in sales. No base salary. 100% commission. Income is unlimited. .REQUIREMENTS:· Ability to make sales and meet with clients in-person or through the utilization of modern technologies· Enjoy the flexibility to control your schedule and work from a home office· Sales funnel, CRM, and cold call experience· Uncapped commission· Comfortable with commission-only sales opportunities· Strong sales stamina· Not afraid of hearing the word no· A desire to make connections, build relationships and connect others1099 Independent ContractorCommissionNo Base SalaryNo Health Benefits Mon, 8 Sep 2025 22:35:27 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/10275868/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11113949 Trainee/Account Executive - AEC/BIM Services at Neilsoft Inc. Employer: Neilsoft Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/08/2026 \n\n  Title: Trainee/Account Executive - AEC/BIM Services Location: Canton, MichiganExperience: 0–2 Years Neilsoft is a 1550+ people, technology-driven, Engineering Services and Solutions company servicing international customers for over 25+ years in the Architecture, Engineering and Construction (AEC), Manufacturing and Industrial Plant segments. We are headquartered in Pune (India) with international offices in US, Canada, UK, Germany and Japan.  Neilsoft Inc. (a wholly owned subsidiary of Neilsoft Limited) has been supporting North American customers for more than two decades.  As part of our Growth Plans, we are looking to onboard 0-2 years experienced engineering graduates who aspire to build a career in Sales.  After completing structured training, candidates will be assigned to different industry verticals based on their strengths, interests, and performance, ensuring a strong foundation for long‑term career development. Neilsoft’s AEC/BIM Practice addresses needs of the AEC/O industry for A/S/MEPF BIM & Engineering Services, Scan2BIM / Reality capture, real-time Digital Twins, custom BIM automation solutions development, AI/ML-assisted solutions development and custom BIM 4D/5D solutions. We work with leading Architectural firms, MEP Consultants, Trade Contractors, Design-Build firms and Fabricators (Precast, Steel, Modular, Timber) to address the needs of different types of projects including Hospitals, Airports, Corporate campuses, Data Centers, Factories & Industrial Plants, Education & Institutional facilities. To know more about the company please visit www.neilsoft.com  ResponsibilitiesAssist in identifying target accounts, generating leads, and building a qualified prospect funnel.Support business development activities for defined industry verticals and offerings Participate in client interactions, meetings, and presentations alongside senior team members.Learn the complete sales cycle—from prospecting to closure—under the mentorship of a Senior Sales professional.Create a plan to address defined markets & execute on the plan to achieve business/revenue targets Ideal Candidate Profile0-2 years experience, Bachelor’s degree in Civil, Mechanical, Electrical, Architecture, or related Engineering fields (preferred).MBA or business coursework is mandatory.Passionate to build a career in Sales Strong communication skills, curiosity, and willingness to engage with clientsSelf‑driven, organized, and eager to grow in a fast‑paced environmentWillingness to travel, ability to work independently, self-motivated and results-drivenExposure to Salesforce or CRM tools is a plus.      Why Join Us?Be part of a startup‑minded team backed by a global enterprise.Learn directly from senior leadership and experienced Sales professionals.Clear growth path into Sales, Pre‑Sales, or Account Management roles.Exposure to advanced AEC/BIM technologies and global clients. Benefits401(k)Cell phone reimbursementDental insuranceHealth insuranceMileage reimbursementOpportunities for advancementPaid time offTravel reimbursementVision insurance Tue, 9 Jun 2026 17:39:18 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11113949/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11287007 Product Designer at SimplyWise Employer: SimplyWise \n\n Expires: 09/08/2026 \n\n We build mobile apps for small business owners and are looking for a product designer to help build, simplify and improve the UI/UX across our suite. You’ll turn real user behavior into clear, simple product ideas, favoring simplicity, clarity, and speed over polish.We’re an AI-first team looking for a designer excited about how AI is changing the way products get built. You should already be experimenting with and regularly using tools like Claude Code, Figma AI, and other AI design/prototyping tools. You’ll have real ownership, working directly with founders, engineers, and customers to take ideas from insight to shipped product. As part of the interview, we’ll ask you to show us how you use AI in your design process. We care less about specific tools and more about how you experiment and think about what’s newly possible. What You’ll DoDesign product from insight to shipped feature, in close collaboration with engineers and founders.Spend time understanding real user behavior (session recordings, usage data, support tickets, customer conversations).Identify friction, confusion, and unnecessary steps—and simplify them.Design clear, minimal flows that are easy to navigate and easy to understand.Turn complex problems into simple design solutions.Iterate quickly based on real usage and feedback.What We’re Looking ForStrong product instincts and clear design taste.Genuinely excited about AI and already incorporating it into how you design and prototype.Comfort working autonomously in a fast-moving, low-process team.Practical, low-ego, and open to being wrong.Curious about users and how products are actually used.Don’t Apply If You…Need heavy process, specs, or perfect requirements to get started.Optimize for visual flourish and perfection over clarity, usability, and shipping fast.Get attached to your designs or take feedback personally.Prefer narrow ownership over taking a problem from start to finish. Sat, 8 Aug 2026 15:17:30 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11287007/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/10836314 Medical Assistant at Fast Med Urgent Care Employer: Fast Med Urgent Care \n\n Expires: 09/08/2026 \n\n We are seeking a skilled and compassionate Medical Assistant to join our healthcare team. As a Medical Assistant, you will play a crucial role in providing quality patient care and supporting the medical staff. This is an excellent opportunity for individuals who are passionate about healthcare and want to make a positive impact on patients' lives.Duties:- Perform vital signs measurements, including blood pressure, temperature, pulse, and respiration rate- Assist with coding and billing procedures- Administer inhalation treatments as directed by healthcare providers- Assist with X-Ray procedures under the supervision of a licensed radiologist- Provide medical administrative support, including scheduling appointments, managing patient records, and handling insurance documentation- Deliver exceptional patient service by addressing inquiries, providing information, and ensuring patient comfort- Apply knowledge of anatomy to assist healthcare providers during examinations and procedures- Perform basic life support techniques in emergency situations- Administer medications as prescribed by healthcare providers- Provide direct patient care, including wound dressing changes, specimen collection, and assisting with minor surgical procedures Wed, 11 Mar 2026 17:58:17 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/10836314/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11287010 End of Summer Cabin Counselor at Fiver Children's Foundation Employer: Fiver Children's Foundation \n\n Expires: 09/08/2026 \n\n Cabin Counselor Organization: Fiver Children’s Foundation - Camp FiverLocation: Poolville, NYDates of Employment: ASAP - August 21, 2026Compensation: $325 / Week plus housing, mealsTravel Reimbursement based on distance$250 Bonus for finishing Camp Season About the Fiver Children’s Foundation Fiver is not a typical after school program or summer camp. We take a slow and steady approach to building relationships and developing social, emotional and life skills that lead to positive decision-making and outcomes for youth. We are committed to ensuring that all Fiver spaces, communications and interactions are: Inclusive, Warm, Youth-Centered, Honest, and Intentional. Through our one-of-a-kind ten-year commitment, Fiver provides experiences that challenge and builds relationships that nurture so that youth from marginalized communities in New York can create their own positive futures.      Job Description Counselors are responsible for providing supervision, guidance, support and leadership to a group of campers in their cabin. As the camper’s primary caregiver during their two-week stay, counselors must be attentive to the camper’s physical, emotional and social needs. Through our character development program, Fiver teaches campers to be a Friend, an Individual, a Valuable Team Player, an Environmentalist and a Risk Taker. We are looking for outstanding role models to inspire and mentor our children!  Counselors should possess skills in a specific program area (e.g. art, dance, sports, waterfront activities, computers, etc) and be comfortable teaching/assisting in these subject matters during daily activity slots. Counselors work together as a dynamic team; counselors should be fun-loving, kid-friendly, open-minded, patient, flexible, willing to learn, mature and compassionate!  Qualifications At least 19 years old by June 2026One year post high school experience working with children preferred  During their experience at Camp Fiver, Counselors will gain many transferable skills such as leadership, effective communication, time management, strategic thinking, behavior management and youth development best practices. Located in beautiful Upstate New York, Camp Fiver is a four-hour trip from New York City and is 45 minutes southeast of Syracuse. Camp Fiver’s 129-acre property includes a lake, a river, woodlands, a learning center, dining hall, horse barn and more. Counselors live at Camp Fiver for all 4, 12-day sessions (off days will be discussed thoroughly during staff training) including one and a half weeks of training prior to camp.  Click Here to Apply for Camp Fiver 2026! The Fiver Children’s Foundation believes that historically marginalized communities must be centered in the work that we do, and are actively taking steps to make sure our processes and practices promote equity for all, including people of color, people from working-class backgrounds, women, and members of the LGBTQ+ community. We encourage applications from people with these identities or members of other marginalized groups. Sat, 8 Aug 2026 15:27:09 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11287010/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11112528 Assistant Project Engineer at Beaver Excavating Company Employer: Beaver Excavating Company \n\n Expires: 09/08/2026 \n\n Join our growing team as an Assistant Project Engineer and assist the project team in the planning and execution of successful mass excavating and construction projects!This position is continuously open because are always looking for talented Assistant Project Engineers in various locations and departments within our company.Primary Responsibilities Assists in the preparation of work orders, schedules, drawings, field measurements, subcontracts and supplier agreements Attends preconstruction meetings, assisting in preparing a list of action items and proposed solutions Provides support to the Project Manager, Project Superintendent and Contract Administrator in preparing job documents and materialsAnalyzes processes, assists with layout, construction sequencing, cost analysis, measures quantities, supporting field employees, clarifying specifications, as necessary Ensure proper document control, quality assurance documentation and construction project records are kept in accordance with expectationsAssist in monitoring the project site, ensuring that the work is progressing on schedule Develops solid working relationships with all project personnel Any other responsibilities as assignedKnowledge & SkillsAble to read and comprehend contract documents and construction plans Solid general math skills with the ability to complete field calculations MS Office experience Excellent oral and written communications Accuracy and attention to detail Ability to deal effectively and tactfully with customers and employees at all levels Ability to act in a safe manner always High level of motivation, a ‘self-starter’EducationAssociate Degree in Civil Engineering, Construction Management, or related field, or equivalent field experience required Bachelor’s in Civil Engineering, Construction Management, or related field preferredTravel Overnight travel and shift work may be assigned based on business needs.Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to sit; use hands to finger, handle, or feel; reach with hands and arms; and talk or hear. The employee is occasionally required to stand; walk; and stoop, kneel. The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 50 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and ability to adjust focus.Equal Opportunity The Beaver Companies provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibit discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws.This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, and training. Tue, 9 Jun 2026 12:31:16 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11112528/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11375717 Supervisory Logistics Management Specialist at U.S. Department of Health and Human Services Employer: U.S. Department of Health and Human Services \n\n Expires: 09/08/2026 \n\n NOTE: This job will close when we have received 50 applications which may be sooner than the closing date of 09/07/2026.This position is only open to persons eligible for the specific groups listed under \"This job is open to\" section of the announcement, including Federal Employees; CTAP, ICTAP, RPL; Land & Base Mgmt.; veterans; Military spouses; Persons with disabilities; Peace Corps/AmeriCorps, & family of overseas employees, and other special authorities.As a Supervisory Logistics Management Specialist, you will:Planning, directing, and coordinating logistics operations involving warehouse management, inventory control, transportation, and distribution of pharmaceuticals.Developing and maintaining logistics policies, Standard Operating Procedures, and the Quality Management System (QMS).Leading and coordinating interagency logistics operations and emergency response activities with various government agencies.Overseeing the inventory management, transportation, warehouse operations, safety and customer service programs.Please see full job announcement on USAJobs.gov for complete details and how to apply. https://www.usajobs.gov/job/881263700U.S. Citizenship required Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:15:08 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11375717/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11009090 Radiologic Technologist or LMRT at Austin Regional Clinic Employer: Austin Regional Clinic \n\n Expires: 09/08/2026 \n\n ABOUT AUSTIN REGIONAL CLINICAustin Regional Clinic has been voted a top Central Texas employer by our employees for over 15 years!   We are one of central Texas’ largest professional medical groups with 35+ locations and we are continuing to grow. We offer the following benefits to eligible team members: Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts, PTO, 401(k), EAP, Life Insurance, Long Term Disability, Tuition Reimbursement, Child Care Assistance, Health & Fitness, Sick Child Care Assistance, Development and more. For additional information visit https://www.austinregionalclinic.com/careers/ PURPOSEPerforms radiographic exams to assist in a diagnosis of disease and injuries. Works effectively with patients and patients’ families and maintains a cooperative relationship with interdepartmental personnel. Carries out all duties while maintaining compliance and confidentiality and promoting the mission and philosophy of the organization.ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS● Performs diagnostic X-ray procedures, which include positioning patient, adjusting equipment settings to obtain the best density, detail and contrast of the area being imaged and determining proper voltage and exposure.● QC images once taken.● Provides appropriate patient protection following prescribed safety standards.● Notifies supervisor of equipment repair needs.● Maintains compliance with Texas Medical Board and ARRT educational requirements.● Adheres to all company policies, including but not limited to, OSHA, HIPAA, compliance and Code of Conduct.● Regular and dependable attendance.● Follows the core competencies set forth by the Company, which are available for review on ARC SharePoint.● Works holiday shift(s) as required by Company policy. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES● Maintains work area.● Stocks room supplies.● Attends required meetings and in-services.● Performs other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATION Education and Experience LMRT Education: Graduate of a program in Radiologic Technology that meets the requirements for Texas certification of Limited Medical Radiologic Technologist.Radiology Technologist Education:  High school diploma or equivalent.  Satisfactory completion of formal radiologic technology training in an AMA-approved school. Experience: At least one year of related work experience preferred.  Experience in digital radiography preferred (CR and /or DR).  Familiarity with PACS image retrieval and storage.  Experience working with all age groups.  Certificate/LicenseCurrent licensure as a Registered Technologist through the Texas Medical Board.Radiological Technologist must be in good standing with American Registry of Radiological Technologist.Current AHA approved Basic Life Support (BLS) Healthcare Provider Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR) course completion card or within 60 days of hire required. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities● Must possess the knowledge, skills and abilities to perform all diagnostic radiology procedures.● Must be customer oriented in order to provide outstanding services to patients, physicians and co-workers.● Ability to maintain awareness of patient privacy, confidentiality and dignity at all times.● Ability to work in a team environment and/or on their own.● Ability to engage others, listen and adapt response to meet others’ needs.● Ability to align own actions with those of other team members committed to common goals.● Excellent computer and keyboarding skills, including familiarity with Windows.● Excellent verbal and written communication skills.● Ability to manage competing priorities.● Ability to perform job duties in a professional manner at all times.● Ability to understand, recall, and communicate, factual information.● Ability to understand, recall, and apply oral and/or written instructions or other information.● Ability to organize thoughts and ideas into understandable terminology.● Ability to apply common sense in performing job. Thu, 30 Apr 2026 22:05:43 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11009090/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11287320 Account Manager at POSH Cars Employer: POSH Cars \n\n Expires: 09/08/2026 \n\n POSH · Dallas–Fort Worth, TX · Full-time, on-sitePOSH puts people in cars on a subscription instead of a loan. Every month, money moves in from subscribers and out to the partners who own the vehicles, and an Account Manager is accountable for every dollar on both sides being right.This is account management as a discipline, not a desk. You will carry a named book of Fleet Partners and subscribers, and you will know it better than anyone else in the company. No surprises reach your partners. No invoice on your book ages quietly. When the numbers disagree, you find out why before anyone has to ask you.We are looking for people who take that personally.ResponsibilitiesOwn a book of Fleet Partners end to end — every vehicle, every VIN, every dollar owed, every dollar paid.Reconcile partner payments monthly. Find the variance, trace it to its cause, and report it the same week.Own a named book of subscribers. Work it on a published cadence, not on whichever account is loudest.Recover unpaid balances by phone. Leave every call with an amount, a date and a method, or with the reason there isn't one.Build payment plans inside approved parameters and hold subscribers to them.Run swaps, tier changes and upgrades. Keep the subscribers worth keeping.Be the single point of contact your accounts call, and answer before they escalate.Document every conversation, promise and variance in-system the day it happens.Escalate anything that changes what a partner is paid, anything outside your parameters, and anything that sounds like a complaint.Report weekly on what moved, what didn't, and what needs a decision.Basic qualificationsBachelor's degree in any discipline, or equivalent experience.Demonstrated ownership of a customer, account, book, budget or ledger where you were the person answerable for the number.Working fluency with spreadsheets: reconcile two lists and explain the difference.Valid driver's license and a clean driving record.Able to work on-site in Dallas–Fort Worth.Preferred skills and experienceExperience holding direct conversations about money owed — collections, billing, AR, banking, dealership finance, front desk, restaurant close.Experience as the named owner of a client relationship rather than a queue.Track record of catching an error before the customer did.Coursework or work in accounting, finance, operations or analytics.Spanish.Comfort in an environment where the process is written after the work, not before it.Additional requirementsOn-site in Dallas–Fort Worth. This role is in the room and near the fleet.Occasional extended hours at month-end when payment cycles close.Must be able to operate fleet vehicles.Offers are contingent on a background check and a driving-record check. No exceptions.Compensation and benefits$52,000–$65,000 base, depending on demonstrated ownership, plus a quarterly performance component paid on cleared payments recovered and on partner reconciliations completed accurately and on time.POSH is building its collections and partner operations functions this year. The person who does this job well is the internal candidate to lead one of them.Hiring processFive stages, twelve business days from application to offer: application review, a 20-minute phone conversation, a 60-minute on-site working session on real redacted POSH data, two reference calls, and a same-day offer. You will meet the founder at every stage after the first.POSHIT INC is an equal opportunity employer. Sat, 8 Aug 2026 23:34:03 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11287320/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11193604 Client Advisor- Client Services at Louis Vuitton Employer: Louis Vuitton \n\n Expires: 09/08/2026 \n\n About the job At Louis Vuitton, we believe in crafting experiences as exceptional as our products. We are seeking a highly motivated and customer-focused Client Advisor to join our dedicated Client Services team. As a Client Advisor, you will be the voice of Louis Vuitton, responsible for delivering unparalleled service and support to our esteemed clientele across various channels including phone, email, social media, and chat. You will play a crucial role in building lasting client relationships and upholding the Maison's legacy of excellence.Job responsibilitiesAs a Louis Vuitton Client Advisor, Client Services, your key responsibilities will include:Client Engagement: Consistently deliver client-centric responses to a wide range of inquiries, from product availability and sales to shipping updates and after-sales support.Relationship Building: Maintain detailed client profiles and leverage clienteling tools to personalize experiences, tailor recommendations, and build strong relationships based on individual preferences and purchase history.Operational Excellence: Achieve individual objectives for quality, schedule adherence, and other key performance indicators, ensuring efficient use of required systems and maintaining high operational standards.Brand Ambassadorship: Act as a proud ambassador of the Louis Vuitton brand, embodying its values and ethos in every interaction.Commercial Acumen: Identify opportunities to upsell and cross-sell products to meet client needs and exceed sales goals, leveraging your client relationships and product knowledge to achieve sales targets.Continuous Learning: Participate in sales training and development programs to enhance your skills and knowledge, staying up-to-date on all product, company, and department initiatives.ProfileThis is an exceptional opportunity for individuals who are passionate about luxury, possess a strong commercial mindset, and thrive in a fast-paced, client-focused environment. The ideal candidate will have:Experience: 3-5 years of customer service experience, preferably within a luxury retail environment, with demonstrated success in achieving sales targets and building client relationships.Communication Skills: Elevated and sophisticated communication skills, both written and verbal, with the ability to interact effectively with clients and colleagues at all levels. Proficiency in English, French, and/or Spanish is highly desirable.Interpersonal Skills: Exceptional ability to build rapport, de-escalate calls, and maintain composure under pressure.Technical Proficiency: Technically savvy with the ability to use multiple systems simultaneously, including CRM software.Commercial Mindset: Strong commercial acumen with the ability to identify opportunities for upselling and cross-selling products.Organizational Skills: Excellent organization and effective time-management skills, with a proactive, solution-oriented, and detailed approach.Availability: Ability to work Weekends, Evenings, and Holidays as required. The appointed candidate will be offered a starting rate of $20 per hour, a comprehensive benefits package including: medical, dental, vision, short and long-term disability, various paid time off programs, employee discount/perks and two retirement plans both with employer contributions. Thu, 9 Jul 2026 15:38:44 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11193604/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11115781 MRI or CT Technologist at Austin Regional Clinic Employer: Austin Regional Clinic \n\n Expires: 09/08/2026 \n\n Big things are coming - We are expanding our radiology services to include MRI and CT!ABOUT AUSTIN REGIONAL CLINICAustin Regional Clinic has been voted a top Central Texas employer by our employees for over 15 years!   We are one of central Texas’ largest professional medical groups with 35+ locations and we are continuing to grow. We offer the following benefits to eligible team members: Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts, PTO, 401(k), EAP, Life Insurance, Long Term Disability, Tuition Reimbursement, Child Care Assistance, Health & Fitness, Sick Child Care Assistance, Development and more. For additional information visit https://www.austinregionalclinic.com/careers/  PURPOSE Performs magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) procedures at a technical level requiring constant attention to technical detail. Performs a variety of technical procedures that will require independent judgment, with ingenuity and initiative. Recognizes the purpose of this service is to provide high quality magnetic resonance imaging and to prioritize the patient as number one. Works effectively with patients and patients’ families and maintains a cooperative relationship with interdepartmental personnel. Carries out all duties while maintaining compliance and confidentiality and promoting the mission and philosophy of the organization. Performs computed tomography (CT) procedures utilizing imaging equipment while providing quality care to patients of all ages. Requires self motivation to increase the level of understanding and knowledge of the field, disease and new procedures as they evolve. Delivers excellent patient care and adheres to radiation standards and guidelines established by governing agencies to ensure optimal patient safety and customer service. Works effectively with patients and patients’ families and maintains a cooperative relationship with interdepartmental team. Carries out all duties while maintaining compliance and confidentiality and promoting the mission and philosophy of the organization.ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Works effectively with patients and patients’ families and maintains a cooperative relationship with interdepartmental personnel.Notifies supervisor of equipment repair needs.Maintains compliance with Texas Medical Board and ARRT educational requirements.Adheres to all company policies, including but not limited to, OSHA, HIPAA, compliance and Code of Conduct.Regular and dependable attendance.Follows the core competencies set forth by the Company, which are available for review on ARC SharePoint.Works holiday shift(s) as required by Company policy.MRI:Performs high quality MRI procedures, according to exam protocol, in a timely manner. Maintains production and quality of imaging procedures by following established standards and procedures.Performs a variety of technical procedures that will require independent judgment, with ingenuity and initiative.Provides high quality magnetic resonance imaging and prioritizes the patient as number one.Demonstrates a knowledge of the human structure and functions, patient care, positioning, principles of electromagnetic and computer sciences, magnetic protection and specialized techniques.Prepares patient and area for procedure by positioning patient, adjusting immobilization devices, moving equipment into specified position and adjusting equipment controls to set exposure factors.Obtains, verifies and maintains all relevant documentation such as chart, patient history, pregnancy status and shielding precautions taken, consent forms, policies and procedures, etc.Adjusts equipment as needed to produce high quality images.Performs Quality Control of images once taken and evaluates images to make sure they meet the ordering provider’s requirements.Maintains medical imaging records in appropriate system and according to department policies and standards for interpretation in a timely manner.Protects patients and employees by adhering to safety requirements, protocols and techniques.Completes quality scans in a timely manner, effectively organizes and prioritizes workflow to meet urgent demands.Keeps inventory of MRI supplies, stocks room supplies and makes orders for supply restocks as required.CT:Responsible for variety of routine diagnostic CT procedures in accordance with physicians’ orders.Prepares patients for CT exam, explains procedure and ensures technical quality.Provides high quality CT imaging and prioritizes the patient as number one.Obtains, verifies and maintains all relevant documentation such as chart, patient history, pregnancy status, consent forms, policies and procedures, etc.Protects patients and employees by adhering to safety requirements, infection-control, drug and radiation policies, protocols and techniques.Cleans and maintains CT scan equipment.Keeps inventory of CT scan supplies, stocks room supplies and makes orders for supply restocks as required.Promotes individual professional growth and development by meeting requirements for continuing education.OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Maintains work area.Attends required meetings and in-services.Performs other duties as assigned.QUALIFICATIONS Education and Experience Required:  High school diploma or GED.Associate Degree in Radiologic Sciences or Graduate of an AMA-approved school of Radiologic Technology.Completion of courses and training in Magnetic Resonance Technology or Specific Training in Computerized Tomography-GE VCT.One or more years’ experience performing MRI or CT procedures.Skilled in starting IV’s and injection of contrast.Preferred: Three (3) or more years of related work experience. Certificate/License Registered with and must be in good standing with American Registry of Radiological Technologist.Licensed by the Texas Medical Board as a Medical Radiologic Technologist - General License.Registered with the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists (ARRT) with advanced certification in CT, or Registered with the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists (ARRT) or American Registry of Magnetic Resonance Imaging Technologists (ARMRIT) with advanced certification in MRI.Current AHA approved Basic Life Support (BLS) Healthcare Provider Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR) course completion card or within 60 days of hire required. Tue, 9 Jun 2026 22:33:41 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/