t.Performs other duties as assignedMinimum EducationBachelor's degree/equivalent (Equivalency reflected under minimum experience)Minimum Experience (in lieu of bachelor’s degree)Four (4) years of business-to-business sales experience OR two (2) years of the Company's business-to-business sales experience required.Knowledge, Skills and AbilitiesExcellent Communication Skills, Product Knowledge, Solution Building, Time Management, Organization, Self-Motivation, Adaptability, Problem Solving, Business Acumen, History of Relationship Building & Maintaining Strong Client Relationships, Data Analysis & Predictive Analytics for Retention, Experience Leveraging Technology, Drive to Monitor Account Health & Mitigate Risks, & Ensuring Customer Satisfaction and Data Visualization for Success MetricsJob ConditionsModerate overnight travel required.Preferred Qualifications: Customer account management or relationship management experience; Experience onboarding new customers, clients, or accounts; Success growing existing customer relationships or revenue; CRM and account planning experience; Cross-functional collaboration to support customer success. Sponsorship is not available for this position.Pay: $4,331.25 - $8,187.50/monthlyAdditional Details: This is a customer facing role that requires regular in person meetings. Candidates must live within a 50-mile radius of Wallingford, CT or surrounding cities within the territory.Pay Transparency:The compensation listed reflects the pay range or rate of pay reasonably expected for this posted position at the posted location or locations.  If this opportunity includes multiple job levels, the pay information represents the ranges for each level in that job family. Actual pay is determined by several job-related factors permitted by law and relevant to the position, including, but not limited to, experience relative to the job, tenure, market level, pay at the location for this job, performance, schedule, and work assignment. In California, the compensation listed reflects the range or rate of pay reasonably expected for this posted position upon hire.For details on our comprehensive benefits, click here.Federal Express Corporation is an Equal Opportunity Employer including, Vets/Disability.Reasonable accommodations are available for qualified individuals with disabilities throughout the application process. Applicants who require reasonable accommodations in the application or hiring process should contact recruitmentsupport@fedex.com.Applicants have rights under Federal Employment Laws:Know Your RightsPay TransparencyFamily and Medical Leave Act (FMLA)Employee Polygraph Protection ActE-Verify Program Participant: Federal Express Corporation participates in the Department of Homeland Security U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services’ E-Verify program (For U.S. applicants and employees only). Please click below to learn more about the E-Verify program:E-Verify Notice (bilingual)Right to Work Notice (English) / (Spanish) Sun, 2 Aug 2026 16:30:48 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11264518/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11116689 Title: Trainee/Account Executive – Manufacturing Practice at Neilsoft Inc. Employer: Neilsoft Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n Title: Trainee/Account Executive – Manufacturing PracticeLocation: Canton, MichiganExperience: 0–2 Years Neilsoft is a 1550+ people, technology-driven, Engineering Services and Solutions company servicing international customers for over 25+ years in the Architecture, Engineering and Construction (AEC), Manufacturing and Industrial Plant segments. We are headquartered in Pune (India) with international offices in US, Canada, UK, Germany and Japan. Neilsoft Inc. (a wholly owned subsidiary of Neilsoft Limited) has been supporting North American customers for more than two decades.  As part of our Growth Plans, we are looking to onboard 0-2 years experienced engineering graduates who aspire to build a career in Sales.  After completing structured training, candidates will be assigned to different industry verticals based on their strengths, interests, and performance, ensuring a strong foundation for long‑term career development.Neilsoft’s Manufacturing Practice offers engineering & digital services for Clients in the areas of Industrial machinery / equipment & production lines, Manufacturing automation and Digital Factory. We services a variety of industries, namely – Paper & Pulp, Mining, Food & Beverages, Discrete manufacturing, Industrial products, etc.  To know more about the company please visit www.neilsoft.com ResponsibilitiesAssist in identifying target accounts, generating leads, and building a qualified prospect funnel.Support business development activities for defined industry verticals and offerings Participate in client interactions, meetings, and presentations alongside senior team members.Learn the complete sales cycle—from prospecting to closure—under the mentorship of a Senior Sales professional.Create a plan to address defined markets & execute on the plan to achieve business/revenue targets Ideal Candidate Profile0-2 years experience, Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical or Electrical Engineering fields (preferred).MBA or business coursework is mandatory.Passionate to build a career in Sales Strong communication skills, curiosity, and willingness to engage with clientsSelf‑driven, organized, and eager to grow in a fast‑paced environmentWillingness to travel, ability to work independently, self-motivated and results-drivenExposure to Salesforce or CRM tools is a plus. Why Join Us?Be part of a startup‑minded team backed by a global enterprise.Learn directly from senior leadership and experienced Sales professionals.Clear growth path into Sales, Pre‑Sales, or Account Management roles. Benefits401(k)Cell phone reimbursementDental insuranceHealth insuranceMileage reimbursementOpportunities for advancementPaid time offTravel reimbursementVision insurance Wed, 10 Jun 2026 14:57:38 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11116689/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11287516 Field Service Technician at JCL Energy Employer: JCL Energy \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n Job Description: Field Service Technician (entry level) – Substation Power Transformers (Remote, Heavy Travel) JCL Energy is seeking entry level Field Service Technicians to join our team and learn new skills involving the assembly, maintenance, and testing of large, high voltage substation transformers typically found in electric utility and/or industrial electrical grids. Desired candidates will have some experience in mechanical or electrical work, able to work in harsh environments and work productively in a team/crew structure. A 1 or 2 year technical degree in a mechanical, electrical or equivalent program is also desirable as well as a general understanding of how the utility electrical grid works, and the major equipment items involved. As a Field Service Technician, you will learn a variety of technical tasks related to power transformers such as the operation of oil processing equipment; internal core/coil inspections/repairs; LTC testing/maintenance; full scope of electrical testing (SFRA, TTR, WR, PF); bushing, radiator, pump and controls installation/replacement on a wide variety of large power transformers. Key Responsibilities Work & Technical Duties• Compliance with safety rules, regulations per customer and company policies• Be punctual and dependable on assigned projects• Work closely with your assigned crew, taking initiative to learn new tasks• Ability to manage your labor and travel expense reporting as required• Operate company vehicles and equipment responsibly Customer & Business Support• Become knowledgeable on JCL’s full line of capabilities and technical solutions and able to communicate to customers• Support customer satisfaction and business growth through high-quality delivery of our services• Perform other duties as assigned to support the profitability and long-term growth of JCL’s Field Service division.Work Location & Travel Requirements• This is a remote field position with extensive travel across the U.S.• Project schedule will require weekend work and occasional overnight work assignments• No relocation is required, Technicians are dispatched from their home location• Regular travel to JCL sites (Sharon, PA; Houston, TX; Temple, TX; Greenville, SC; Goldsboro, NC ) during onboarding and periodically thereafter.• International travel may be required for OEM training or to support growth in Canada and Mexico. Compensation & Benefits• Hourly rate (overtime eligible), paid bi-weekly in accordance with JCL payroll practices.• Eligible for per diem under JCL’s per diem policy.• Participation in the Service Technician Bonus Program (0–10% of earnings based on individual and team performance).• Benefits include:• JCL Health Insurance (details provided separately)• JCL 401(k) Program (details provided separately)• 2 weeks PTO annually Job Type: Full-time Benefits:• 401(k)• 401(k) matching• Dental insurance• Employee assistance program• Flexible schedule• Health insurance• Health savings account• Life insurance• Paid time off• Vision insurance Sun, 9 Aug 2026 17:19:51 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11287516/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11033113 Photonics Support Engineer I at Thorlabs Employer: Thorlabs \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n Thorlabs is pleased to play a role in advancing science through the components, instruments, and systems we design and manufacture. We believe that science and innovation have great potential to improve the world around us and are committed to advancing photonics (i.e., light-based) technologies that positively impact our customers, employees, and communities. Via educational outreach and more sustainable business practices, we continuously invest in a brighter future. We recognize that each of our employees is a unique individual with the ability to contribute to our success and seek to find great people who will thrive in our fun, fast-paced culture.The Photonics Support Engineer I is responsible for providing entry level technical support by solving problems, troubleshooting, and working with customers to guide them to the best possible product solutions for their applications and experiments. The position works with several other Photonics Support and Design Engineers to support optics, lasers and light sources, fiber, opto-mechanics, motion control, microscope and other imaging systems, telecom instruments and more. Between onsite lab opportunities, customer interactions, tradeshows and Thorlabs manufacturing entities visits, the position can be exposed to every facet of the photonics industry.Although the location of the position is in Newton, NJ, from time to time it may be required to undertake duties at other Thorlabs locations.• Provide technical support via phone, web chat & e-mail to customers worldwide.• Interface with multiple support teams around the world to implement best practices globally.• Reproduce setups and create technical solutions in the lab.• Demonstrate knowledge and problem-solving abilities in providing technical support to customers who purchase from our extensive product portfolio.• Develop and provide customized solutions, assist in the design of custom products.• Support Marketing and Sales activities by attending Tradeshows and Customer visits.• Participate in managing the development of Thorlabs products by being part of an interactive development forum.• Develop Marketing Materials like test data, white papers, or video for use on our website or through another distribution channel• Develop skill in the use of test equipment to help influence the design of next generation photonics products.• Contribute to training of new team members by sharing your unique skills.Requirements Experience:• Entry level to 3 years of Photonics product and applications support experience. Will accept recent college graduate with bachelor’s degree. Lab experience with optics, mechanics, lasers, and electrical components a plus.Education:• BSc, MSc or PhD degree in Optics, Physics or a related Engineering field or equivalent work experience.Specialized Knowledge and Skills:• Knowledge of Photonics and Laser Technology via work or laboratory experience.• Strong communication proficiency and presentation skills.• Ability to multitask, show attention to details, and to solve multidisciplinary problems under time constraints.• Ability to develop and communicate dept. goals in support of Thorlabs' mission and responds to all interactions in a positive manner.• Eagerness to learn about new technologies, process, and business models.• Work schedule may be staggered times to cover our 8am–8pm hours of operation.• Opportunities to travel to tradeshows, other Thorlabs manufacturing facilities (foreign and domestic), and training events on and off site.The estimated pay range for this role is $ 62,000 - $ 70,000 annually Thorlabs values its diverse environment and is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer.  All qualified individuals will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identify or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age or veteran status. Job descriptions are not intended as and do not create employment contracts.  The organization maintains its status as an at-will employer.  Employees can be terminated for any reason not prohibited by law.Benefits Thorlabs offers a complete benefits package that includes medical, dental and vision insurance, company paid life insurance, a generous PTO package, a 401(k) plan, and tuition reimbursement just to name a few. Fri, 8 May 2026 16:54:18 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11033113/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11033105 Photonic Instrumentation Product Line Manager at Thorlabs Employer: Thorlabs \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n At Thorlabs, we design and manufacture components, instruments, and systems that transform the world by identifying, enabling, and accelerating key photonics (i.e., light-based) technologies. Backed by a dedicated workforce of more than 3,000 employees worldwide, Thorlabs contributes to cutting-edge research and real-world innovation.Whether you're early in your career or bringing years of experience, you’ll find opportunities to grow, take ownership, and make meaningful contributions from day one. We know every employee brings unique talents and perspectives that fuel our success, and we seek driven individuals who are excited to make an impact in a fun, fast-moving culture.The Photonic Instrumentation Product Line Manager (PLM) is a member of the Office of the CTO (OCTO) and is accountable for driving the commercial success and the strategic direction and alignment of Thorlabs' Photonic Instrumentation portfolio. The portfolio encompasses benchtop photonic, electronic, and opto-electronic instruments.  These instruments are used as test and measurement equipment, instrumentation, and control electronics supporting multiple markets including, but not limited to, commercial and university basic research, quantum optics, spectroscopy, and datacom-telecom. The product line will be developed and produced across multiple Business Units (BUs) and legal entities globally. The PLM owns the definition and execution of product roadmaps, go-to-market strategies, and portfolio optimization initiatives.The PLM works closely with engineering, manufacturing, marketing, sales, and executive leadership to identify growth opportunities, strengthen product positioning, and expand both catalog and OEM/custom business.Success in this role depends on the ability to combine technical credibility, commercial insight, and cross-functional leadership to align multiple organizations behind a common product strategy and successfully execute it.Essential Job Functions:Portfolio Ownership & Strategic SteeringOwn and actively steer the Benchtop Instrumentation portfolio across participating BUs, ensuring alignment with corporate strategy and market requirements.Define, prioritize, and drive and govern roadmap execution, including new product development, product lifecycle management, and rationalization of underperforming offerings.Maintain a comprehensive understanding of market segmentation, competitive positioning, and Thorlabs’ relative strengths.Market Intelligence & Growth LeadershipLead market analysis efforts to identify trends, adjacencies, and whitespace opportunities, translating insights into actionable portfolio decisions.Drive initiatives to increase market share and wallet share within key accounts in close collaboration with Sales and Applications teams.Originate and lead strategic OEM and custom solution opportunities, coordinating efforts between customers and internal engineering/manufacturing teams.Cross-Functional Alignment & ExecutionAct as the central decision-making and coordination point across BUs for the assigned portfolio, ensuring alignment on priorities, timelines, and resource allocation.Partner with Marketing and Tech Marketing to define and enforce high-quality, consistent digital content, specifications, and application positioning.Shape and guide a coherent tradeshow and business development strategy for the portfolio.NPI Governance & DeliveryPlay a leading role in the New Product Introduction (NPI) process, including concept approval, prioritization, and design validation.Hold teams accountable to agreed development timelines, milestones, and deliverables.Ensure that new product introductions are aligned with portfolio strategy and commercial objectives.Performance Management & AccountabilityDefine, monitor, and report on key portfolio KPIs, including:New product introduction timelinesR&D investment allocation and effectivenessRevenue growth and gross margin performanceTake corrective actions where performance deviates from plan, including reprioritization of projects and resource reallocation.Requirements Experience:8+ years of experience in photonics, opto-electrical, or optical instrumentation, or a related high-technology industry.Demonstrated experience in product management, product line management, systems engineering, applications engineering, business development, or a comparable cross-functional leadership role.Strong understanding of photonic instrumentation markets, particularly research instrumentation, test & measurement, and quantum/AMO laboratory environments.Experience with sales, marketing, use or integration of both photonic and electronic test equipment, familiarity with automation and/or system integration preferred.Experience working with cross-functional teams spanning engineering, manufacturing, sales, marketing, and operations.Demonstrated ability to influence and lead without direct organizational authority.Proven ability to build consensus across multiple organizations while maintaining focus on business objectives.Strong decision-making skills with the ability to balance competing priorities.High degree of ownership, initiative, and accountability.Ability to think strategically while maintaining attention to execution and operational detail. Education:Bachelor's degree in physics, Electrical Engineering, Optical Engineering, or a related technical discipline. An advanced degree (M.S. or Ph.D.) is preferred Specialized Knowledge and skills:·Strong commercial acumen with the ability to balance customer needs, technical capabilities, and financial objectives.·Familiarity with benchtop instrument UI/UX and remote-control hardware interfaces and APIs based on hands-on experience·Understanding of photonic and/or electronic measurement tools and techniques, hands-on experience with low-noise, high-speed, or complex measurements preferred·Excellent understanding of product lifecycle management, portfolio optimization, and New Product Introduction (NPI) processes.·Ability to translate market opportunities into actionable product strategies and development priorities.·Strong analytical skills with experience using market, competitive, and financial data to support decision-making.·Outstanding written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to communicate effectively with customers, senior management, and technical teams.·Comfortable presenting to customers, executive leadership, and at industry conferences. Be willing to travel domestically and internationally around 20% of their time. Direct Reports: None The estimated pay range for this role is $110,000 - $ 150,000 annually Thorlabs values its diverse environment and is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer.  All qualified individuals will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identify or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age or veteran status. Job descriptions are not intended as and do not create employment contracts.  The organization maintains its status as an at-will employer.  Employees can be terminated for any reason not prohibited by law.Benefits Thorlabs offers a complete benefits package that includes medical, dental and vision insurance, company paid life insurance, a generous PTO package, a 401(k) plan, and tuition reimbursement just to name a few. Fri, 8 May 2026 16:58:13 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11033105/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11351821 Network Security Lead (INFOSEC) at U.S. General Services Administration (GSA) Employer: U.S. General Services Administration (GSA) \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n SummaryAs a Network Security Lead (INFOSEC), you will manage the Network Security Program and provide ongoing security operation support. The Security Operations & Engineering Division is responsible for providing real-time operational security through SOC and enterprise network security capabilities.  DutiesAs a Network Security Lead (INFOSEC) you will perform the following duties:Incorporating modern network infrastructure capabilities (i.e., Secure Access Service Edge (SASE), Software-Defined Wide Area Networks (SD-WAN), Software-Defined Perimeter (SDP), Software-Defined Networks (SDN), etc.).Working with a team to analyze the customer current network architecture in conjunction with Zero Trust assessment findings to recommend future-state network architecture design for the agency.Providing assistance in implementing system security requirements for both internal and external networks, as well as multi-cloud environments.Providing support and guidance in constructing, designing, integrating, and configuring cybersecurity and network monitoring.Providing expert advice to the Director of Division. Representing the Division and OCIO in meetings with other GSA entities; and GSA in meetings with representatives of industry, other agencies, public organizations, etc., to resolve problems, develop joint policies/standards; analyze, select and implement IT security products/services/solutions; and exchanges information regarding areas of technical expertise. Wed, 26 Aug 2026 19:08:32 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11351821/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11117305 Business Development Representative at Rise Alliance Employer: Rise Alliance \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n If you’re eager to make a real impact, have guaranteed professional growth alongside a supportive team, and help business owners succeed, Rise Alliance offers the perfect environment to advance your career. About Rise AllianceRise Alliance is a dynamic and fast-growing small business based in the heart of Manhattan. Our mission is to empower businesses by removing the burden of financial management , so they can focus on growth and success. Through customized financial solutions — including Strategic Business Consulting, Debt Restructuring, and connections to a robust network of Capital Partners — we've helped thousands of businesses overcome complex financial challenges with innovative, straightforward strategies. Why Join Rise Alliance?At Rise Alliance, career growth and earning potential are limitless. We foster a high-energy, results-driven culture where passionate professionals thrive.Fast-paced, collaborative, and supportive teamOpportunities for professional development, learning, and advancementRewards high-performing work that makes a direct impact on communities & business success  About The RoleBusiness Development Representatives connect real people to real solutions. You will be handpicked by leadership and trusted with a list of warm leads and nurture the relationships from initial call to closing. You will connect with business owners nationwide, understand their unique challenges , and share our innovative financial solution service to help them overcome debt and achieve long-term success . You will be responsible for building and nurturing client relationships, meeting daily and monthly performance goals , and maximizing opportunities within your assigned portfolio. Joining the Rise team as a Business Development Representative provides you with the opportunity to learn from industry experts about our one-of-a-kind debt resolution services. Our senior team will train you on our offerings and how they relate to our robust client-base, with the expectation of proactive warm lead outreach where you are able to clearly explain Rise debt resolution services as they fit each prospective client’s needs. Key ResponsibilitiesManage full sale cycle pipeline, following up on warms leads to closingServe as a trusted advisor, offering empathetic, consultative guidance tailored to each client’s needs with empathy, professionalism, and transparencyDevelop and maintain strong relationships with prospective clients and warm leadsAchieve daily metrics and monthly targets to drive personal and team successCollaborate with internal teams to deliver seamless service and supportUphold the company’s ethical and client-focused standards in all interactions What You BringA hunger for success, positive attitude, and eagerness to learn and growExcitement to join a dynamic, in-person team full-timeDriven by both personal and team successStrong active listening skills and an empathetic, consultative approachExcellent communication and interpersonal management skillsAbility to thrive in a fast-paced, high-energy environmentSelf-starter mentality with a track record of personal and professional achievementExperience with CRM systems is a plusBachelor’s or Associate Degree preferredFluency in English, Bilingual Fluency in Spanish/Mandarin is a plus Compensation and Benefits:Compensation:$60,000-70,000 + Uncapped Commission (OTE $110,000-$120,000) BenefitsComprehensive Benefits Package:Unlimited Paid Time Off (PTO)Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance401(k) PlanWeekly Forkable lunch stipendGym Membership ContributionWeekly and Quarterly company-sponsored social events ScheduleMonday to Friday10:00 AM - 7:00 PMJunior (new grad, <1 year experience): 10 AM - 6 PM In-person at our Midtown Manhattan office Join Us at Rise AllianceIf you are passionate about supporting business owners, enjoy working in a dynamic environment, and are excited about opportunities for growth, we want to hear from you!Rise Alliance is an equal employment opportunity employer. We will not discriminate against applicants with regard to any legally-recognized basis including, but not limited to: veteran status, race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, marital status, sexual orientation, and physical or mental disabilities.Ready to build something extraordinary with us? Apply today! Wed, 10 Jun 2026 16:43:54 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11117305/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11287741 Marine Officer Positions at Officer Selection Team - United States Marine Corps Employer: Officer Selection Team - United States Marine Corps \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n THE CHALLENGE: LEAD FROM THE FRONT ON THE GROUND AND IN THE AIRThe Marine Air-Ground Task Force (MAGTF) represents the world's premier combined-arms expeditionary force. Whether executing rapid ship-to-shore maneuvers, securing forward operating positions, or coordinating complex air-support networks, Marine Officers bring decisive victory to every front.As a Marine Officer in a Ground or Aviation Support role, you are entrusted with two profound responsibilities: accomplishing your mission and ensuring the welfare of the Marines you lead. We are seeking elite, physically resilient, and mentally sharp college students and graduates ready to command combat elements and lead highly technical support teams. PART I: GROUND COMBAT ELEMENT (GCE) SPECIALTIESGround combat arms represent the bedrock of the Marine Corps. Marine Ground Officers organize and lead units to gain decisive advantages through maneuver, direct and indirect fire, and superior tactical intelligence.03: Infantry Officer: The tip of the spear. Plan, direct, and assist in the deployment and tactical employment of rifle and reconnaissance platoons. Infantry Officers are responsible for the discipline, morale, tactical execution, and welfare of up to 40 Marines.02: Ground Intelligence Officer: Analyze, evaluate, and estimate tactical battlefields. Formulate, coordinate, and execute reconnaissance, counterintelligence, and fire support operations to guide commander decisions.04: Logistics Officer: Keep the MAGTF moving. Plan, coordinate, and supervise tactical logistics across supply, vehicle maintenance, heavy-equipment transportation, and general engineering services from ship to shore.06: Communications Officer: The backbone of Command and Control. Supervise and coordinate the planning, installation, operation, and security of advanced data, telecommunications, satellite, radio, and computer systems on the battlefield.08: Field Artillery Officer: Direct the tactical employment of artillery batteries. Coordinate devastating indirect fires using mortars, cannons, rockets, and naval surface fire support.13: Combat Engineer Officer: Command engineer units to shape the physical battlespace. Duties include constructing expedient roads and forward airfields, managing heavy equipment, placing obstacles, and executing breaching operations.18: Tank Officer: Recommend and execute tactical maneuvers for armored tank units, directing firepower and heavy armor to dominate ground engagements.58: Military Police Officer: Function as tactical supervisors, coordinators, and administrators of law enforcement, security operations, and maneuver support. PART II: AVIATION COMBAT ELEMENT (ACE) SUPPORT SPECIALTIESMarine Aviation cannot dominate the skies without the officers who control the airspace and sustain the aircraft. These critical, non-pilot roles ensure operational readiness and battlespace control.60: Aircraft Maintenance Officer: Supervise and coordinate highly technical aircraft maintenance, diagnostics, and repair activities. Master complex Navy-sponsored maintenance programs to ensure combat aircraft are mission-ready.66: Aviation Supply Officer: Command high-velocity supply chains, multi-million dollar budgets, inventory management, and aviation-specific logistics within Marine Aircraft Wings (MAWs) and Marine Aviation Logistics Squadrons (MALS).72: Aviation Ground Support & Control Roles: Air Defense Officer: Coordinate and command air defense operations and missile defense platforms to protect MAGTF assets.Air Support Control / Air Traffic Control Officer: Direct tactical air support operations, manage complex airfields, and control airspace in expeditionary environments.Aviation Intelligence Officer (AIO): Act as the squadron commander’s primary source for threat weapon systems, electronic warfare tactics, and target imagery. THE BENEFITS OF A MARINE CORPS COMMISSIONEarning the title of a Marine Officer provides exceptional benefits, career variety, and financial security designed to invest in you and your family's future.1. Financial Security & RanksCompetitive Pay & Allowances: Receive regular pay raises, regular cost-of-living increases, and tax-free allowances for housing (BAH) and food (BAS).Thrift Savings Plan (TSP) & Retirement: High-matching retirement savings plans and attractive pension benefits after 20 years of service.Annual Uniform Allowance: Annual funding to purchase and maintain your service and utility uniforms.2. Advanced Education & Career GrowthTuition Assistance Program (TAP): Covers 100 percent of tuition costs for part-time coursework (up to $225 per credit and/or $4,500 per academic year).Advanced Degree Program (ADP): Attend graduate school full-time to pursue a Master's degree at accredited civilian universities while receiving full Marine Officer pay and allowances.Special Education Program (SEP): Fully funded postgraduate opportunities in fields like engineering, computer science, communications, and management.Fellowships: Elite opportunities to work directly with DARPA, Capitol Hill, the White House, or top-tier academic institutions like Tufts University.3. Tangible Quality-of-Life Benefits30 Days Paid Vacation: Earn 30 days of paid leave or vacation each year from day one.Zero-Cost Healthcare: Complete medical and dental coverage for officers and their families.VA Home Loans: Eligibility for Veterans Administration Guaranteed Loans for home purchases.On-Base Perks & Recreation: Low-cost or free access to gyms, pools, campgrounds, boat rentals, golf courses, private beaches, and base exchange shopping.All-Marine Sports: Opportunity to try out and compete on elite, base-supported teams (boxing, soccer, rugby, track, golf) with potential paths to the Olympics. THE TRAINING PATHWAY: FORGING LEADERSThe pipeline to becoming a Ground or Aviation Support Officer is rigorous and highly structured, ensuring you possess the mental, physical, and ethical skills to lead under pressure:Commissioning Programs (PLC or OCC):Platoon Leaders Class (PLC): For college freshmen, sophomores, and juniors. Complete training over summer sessions with zero academic year obligations. Receive stipends and pay during summers.Officer Candidate Course (OCC): For college seniors and graduates. A single, intensive 10-week course in Quantico, VA.Officer Candidates School (OCS) (Quantico, VA): Prove your physical stamina, academic capability, and ethical character under the guiding motto Ductus Exemplo (\"Lead by Example\").The Basic School (TBS) (Quantico, VA - 6 Months): Newly commissioned Second Lieutenants undergo 28 weeks of comprehensive field training, marksmanship, and platoon tactics. TBS reinforces the core concept that \"Every Marine Officer is a combat leader first.\"MOS Selection & Specialty Schools: Near the halfway mark of TBS, officers indicate their preferences and are assigned to their respective Ground or Aviation Support specialty school (lasting from 6 weeks to 18 months depending on complexity). ELIGIBILITY & SELECTION CRITERIAEducation: Must be a U.S. citizen currently enrolled in or graduated from an accredited college or university (minimum \"C\" grade point average).Physical Standards: Must pass the Marine Corps Physical Fitness Test (PFT). Minimum OCS induction standards:Males: 8 pull-ups, timed plank (1:03), and a 3-mile run in 24:00.Females: 1 pull-up, timed plank (1:03), and a 3-mile run in 27:00.Note: Highly competitive selection requires scores far exceeding these minimums.Moral & Medical Fitness: Must pass a comprehensive physical examination and background/moral screening. HOW TO APPLYThe journey begins with an interview. Contact your local Officer Selection Officer (OSO) to undergo screening, complete physical evaluations, and secure your slot for OCS.Contact the Officer Selections Officer, Captain Brandon T. Jackson at brandon.jackson@usmc.marines.mil Mon, 10 Aug 2026 02:16:14 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11287741/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11121104 Superintendent at D.R. Horton, Inc. Employer: D.R. Horton, Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n D.R. Horton, Inc., the largest homebuilder in the U.S., was founded in 1978 and is a publicly traded company on the New York Stock Exchange. It is engaged in the construction and sale of high quality homes designed principally for the entry-level and first time move-up markets. The Company also provides mortgage financing and title services for homebuyers through its mortgage and title subsidiaries. Please visit our website at www.drhorton.com for more information.D.R. Horton, Inc.is currently looking for a Superintendent. The right candidate's primary responsibility is to manage all functions of the job site as it relates to home construction while providing excellent customer service. The Superintendent manages the construction of multiple homes from permit to closing by scheduling and supervising job site subcontractors, homeowner walk-throughs, and inspections while maintaining company construction and safety standards. Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following. Other duties may be assigned.Manage the construction schedule and ensure the highest quality product is delivered on time and within budgetSchedule all involved subcontractors for each phase of construction and evaluate the quality and efficiency of their work to ensure work complies with local, state and federal building code requirements and company standards of workmanshipComplete each home site on schedule from planning through occupancy, ensuring all contract obligations are satisfiedInspect and determine subcontractor’s workmanship and product quality is completed on time and within defined scope of work.  Halt any work that is not satisfactory or noncompliant with plans, specifications, or applicable codeAuthorize payment of subcontractors when all standards are met and upon thorough inspection of work completed and for materials receivedManage the customer experience throughout the entire construction process.  Recognize and enforce quality standards through daily inspection of homes under construction.  Conduct homeowner orientation and walks, provide regular communications regarding progress and address concernsMonitor community cleanliness and ensure the community and worksite is clean, orderly and visually appealing during constructionManage the post-close process for warranty.  Assess warranty requests, determine course of action, schedule subcontractors, and manage quality assuranceFollow up with homeowners to ensure concerns are addressed in a timely and professional mannerMaintain a current working knowledge of all applicable building codesWork closely with the sales, customer warranty, and management team to ensure open communication on all matters; develop a strong environment conducive to proactive resolution of issues and strong commitment to producing a quality productConducts all business in a professional and ethical manner to serve customers and increase the goodwill and profit of the companyAbility to work additional hours as necessary to meet business needs QualificationsEducation and/or ExperienceHigh school diploma or general education degree (GED)Two to four years related experienceAbility to manage and complete the “13 Milestones of Construction” specified in JDEMust have a vehicle capable of carrying supplies, valid driver’s license and be willing to drive among designated communities in daytime and nighttimeAbility to read and interpret construction documents, drawings, specifications, scopes of work and knowledge of all phases of new homes constructionGeneral knowledge of municipal permitting, regulations and building codesAbility to converse with customers, all levels of management and personnelSuperb interpersonal, verbal and written communication skillsDemonstrated commitment to customer satisfactionAbility to control cost overruns and manage a budgetAbility to utilize DRH Construction applications on a smart phone, tablet, or laptopAbility to apply common sense understanding to carry out instructions furnished in written, oral form or via DRH Construction applicationsProficiency with MS Office and emailAbility to stand and walk for 4 hours straight or up to a full 8-hour day; sit for extended periods; kneel and bend at the waist; climb, balance and stoop, crouch or crawl; walk up and down stairs; walk on unlevel terrain; use hands and fingers to handle or feel; reach with hands and arms; talk and hear.  Ability to lift and/or move up to 50 pounds.  Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, color vision and peripheral visionRegular exposure to outside weather conditions, moving mechanical parts, high precarious places and risk of electrical shockThe noise level is generally loud Preferred QualificationsBachelor’s degree from a four-year college a plusWork effectively in a high pressure and high production environment Come join a winning team with a Fortune 500 company! We are growing fast and are looking for enthusiastic attitudes and team players to join our success. We offer an excellent benefits package including:Medical, Dental and Vision401(K)Employee Stock Purchase PlanFlex Spending AccountsLife & Disability InsuranceVacation, Sick, Personal Time and Company HolidaysMultiple Voluntary and Company provided Benefits Build YOUR future with D.R. Horton, America’s Builder. #WeBuildPeopleToo Thu, 11 Jun 2026 18:32:09 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11121104/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11287737 Marine Judge Advocate at Officer Selection Team - United States Marine Corps Employer: Officer Selection Team - United States Marine Corps \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n The Marine Corps is interested in hiring 1Ls, 2Ls and 3Ls for the summer of 2027 and full time thereafter. Once admitted to practice, this summer internship will develop into a guaranteed full-time offer, contingent upon graduating law school and being admitted to the bar. To be clear, the Marine Corps will guarantee qualified applicants a full-time job following law school, as a 1L, 2L, or 3L.After successfully completing a summer contract, Marine Corps Judge Advocates prove themselves in the same training pipeline as every Officer in the Corps. You will attend Marine Corps Officer Candidates School (OCS) over the summer for 10 weeks in Quantico, VA as an Officer Candidate. Upon completion of OCS this summer, you will earn the title of Marine Officer. You’ll then return to law school (whether that is 2L or 3L year), complete your JD, apply for admission to the state bar, then enter active duty as a Judge Advocate with the Marine Corps. During law school, you will accrue time in service (seniority), which will translate into higher pay and accelerated eligibility to draw pension benefits.Marine Judge Advocates will immediately carry a robust caseload and will quickly be first chair on felony level trials in federal court. During your first tour, you’ll serve in many of the following roles: prosecutor, defense attorney, victim’s legal counsel, and legal assistance attorney. You’ll have the unique opportunity to practice law across diverse legal portfolios, gain criminal litigation experience from the start, and lead a team. The work of Judge Advocates may also involve advising commanding officers, overseeing criminal/administrative investigations, and practicing in other areas of law, including but not limited to: civil litigation, law of armed conflict, maritime law, tort claims, labor law, environmental law, operational law, cyber law, and international law.Very few lawyers in the private sector get exposure to such a variety and high-level experience immediately upon graduation from law school. Even fewer earn the right to do so as an officer in the United States Marine Corps. Marines possess critical character traits, a team-building mindset, and are not driven by billable hours, marketing, or profit. Marine Corps Judge Advocates have an accelerated promotion timeline and competitive compensation, receiving a salary above equivalent entry-level state and federal legal positions.The Marine Corps is offering you a chance to practice law in its purest form free of the distractions inherent in civilian practice: you don’t need to advertise and win clients, there is no minimum billable hour requirement, you don’t even need to bill your time. Unlike working in a state’s attorney’s office or as a public defender, the Marine Corps will start you off on a team of prosecutors or defense attorneys working on felony and misdemeanor cases.MARINE JUDGE ADVOCATE DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIESA Marine Judge Advocate serves in a wide range of legal roles that directly support Marines, commanders, and military operations. Their duties are diverse and often rotate throughout their career to build broad legal expertise:Military Justice: Immediately serve as a first chair attorney as either trial counsel (prosecutor), defense counsel, or victims’ legal counsel in courts-martial, handling felony-level cases involving criminal investigations, trial litigation, and post-trial actions.Command Legal Advisor: Advise commanders on legal issues affecting daily operations, including military justice, administrative separations, investigations, rules of engagement, and the lawful use of force.Operational & International Law: Provide legal guidance during training, deployments, and combat operations on the law of armed conflict, targeting, detainee operations, and international agreements.Administrative & Civil Law: Handle matters such as misconduct processing, adverse fitness reports, line-of-duty investigations, ethics reviews, and claims involving government liability or property damage.Victims’ Legal Counsel (VLC): Represent and advise victims of sexual assault and other crimes, ensuring their rights are protected throughout the military justice process.Legal Assistance: Provide personal legal services to Marines and their families, including wills, powers of attorney, consumer law issues, family law guidance, and landlord-tenant disputes.Training & Education: Conduct legal training for Marines and commanders on military law, ethics, and operational legal considerations to ensure lawful and effective decision-making.PIPELINE OF A MARINE JUDGE ADVOCATEA Marine Judge Advocate’s pipeline begins with Officer Candidates School (OCS), a physically and mentally demanding program designed to evaluate leadership, endurance, and character, rather than teach law or tactics. Candidates are assessed on their ability to lead under stress, maintain discipline, and embody Marine Corps values.After commissioning, officers attend The Basic School (TBS) in Quantico, Virginia, a six-month course where all Marine officers—regardless of specialty—are trained as provisional rifle platoon commanders. At TBS, Judge Advocates learn infantry tactics, weapons employment, land navigation, and small-unit leadership to ensure they can lead Marines and understand the operational environment.Following TBS, Marine Judge Advocates attend the Naval Justice School (Naval School of Law) in Newport, Rhode Island, where they complete the Basic Lawyer Course, receiving intensive instruction in military justice, operational law, administrative law, and ethics before reporting to their first fleet assignment.MARINE JUDGE ADVOCATE CONSTRUCTIVE SERVICE CREDITThis is an accelerated promotion offered to Marine Judge Advocates providing significant professional and financial benefits by recognizing their advanced education and immediate responsibilities as licensed attorneys. Judge Advocates are typically promoted to Captain (O-3) within their first year of commissioning, resulting in increased pay, allowances, and leadership authority at a faster rate. This accelerated timeline also enhances career progression by allowing Judge Advocates to assume greater legal and advisory roles sooner, gain more senior-level experience earlier in their careers, and remain competitive for future assignments and leadership opportunities within the Marine Corps.HEALTH CAREActive-duty military qualify for free health care called Tricare Premium. This plan requires no monthly payments, no co-pays, no annual fees, and no premiums. Your dependents automatically receive tri-care premium by virtue of you being active duty. When you or a family member experiences a health incident, Tri-care will provide 100% coverage of those medical fees which is rare amongst other American health-care plans in 2026. This means none of your direct compensation must go into healthcare, a factor most folks in the civilian world must consider when planning their yearly expenses, but not active-duty personnel.OTHER BENEFITSUp to $110,000 in additional compensation (Judge Advocate Continuation Pay)Post 9/11 GI Bill for you or your dependents’ education expenses30 days paid vacation per yearFederal holidays off401K retirement with employer matchSecret Security ClearanceIf you are interested in applying for this summer or beyond, now is the time to reach out. Contact the Marine Corps Officer Selection Officer, Captain Brandon Jackson, by email at brandon.jackson@marines.usmc.mil. Mon, 10 Aug 2026 02:03:54 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11287737/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11334193 Business Analyst at Evergy Employer: Evergy \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n SUMMARY OF JOB RESPONSIBILITIES AND REQUIREMENTS JOB TITLE:            Business AnalystREQUSITION:        ACC002BDEPARTMENT:      Power and Revenue Accounting - Topeka General Office or 801 CharlotteLOCATION:            Topeka, KS                              Kansas City, MOPAY RANGE:         Business Analyst I: $54,400 - $68,000                              Business Analyst II: $66,600 - $83,200                              Scheduled Work Hours:   Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m.  Summary of Primary Duties and Responsibilities:Responsible for detailed analysis of generation, interchange, and load meter data submitted to regional Power Pools for use in preparation of transmission and market system revenues and expenses on a monthly basis on behalf of Evergy and external counterparties. In addition, the position will collaborate and coordinate system enhancements and upgrades, support business initiatives, be responsible to meet the on-going needs of management, and comply with all regulatory and external reporting requirements and deadlines. Document business system requirements for the Transmission System.Oversee system implementations and assist with preparation of related testing materials.Develop business processes, policies, design specifications, and testing activities for new business systems.Coordinate maintenance and support of systems with new and/or changing business requirements.Troubleshoot system problems and coordinate resolution of problems.Improve division efficiency through focus on innovation, process improvements, and leverage of data analysis tools and concepts.Identify, analyze, and interpret trends or patterns in complex Transmission System data. Maintain and enhance working relationships throughout organization by providing clear, concise, accurate and responsive information in a timely manner, and foster an environment of teamwork and quality customer service.General knowledge of the SPP OATT (Open Access Transmission Tariff) and NITS/NOA.Analytical and critical thinking skills in order to solve complex meter and transmission settlement problems.Oversee PowerBI analytics environment including design, implementation, and maintenance of Workspace and App reports/dashboards.Ability to communicate technical settlement concepts to other work groups and external counterparties.Ability to manage multiple tasks and juggle priorities to meet deadlines. Education and Experience Requirements:Bachelor’s degree with an emphasis in Accounting, Finance, IT or Business-related field preferred.Experience in the regulated utility industry, preferred.Requires advanced proficiency with spreadsheets. Experience with SQL and relational databases is preferred.Must possess effective oral and written communication skills, the ability to work in a “team” environment. Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities Required:A strong understanding of energy markets and meter data, as it relates to transmission settlements is required. Be able to apply analytical thinking, creative problem solving and sound reasoning and logic. Demonstrate exceptional interpersonal and communication skills. Must have the ability to handle multiple tasks and respond quickly and accurately, with a strong attention to detail. Must be proficient in the use of Microsoft office, have strong Excel skills and proficiency with SharePoint Online. Experience in PowerBI analytics tool preferred. Licenses, Certificates, Bonding and/or Testing Required:Must have a valid driver’s license. Working Conditions:Normal office working conditions.  Must have a satisfactory work record including good attendance. Evergy has a clear mission – To empower a better future. Evergy chooses to live this mission by valuing People First. We know to accomplish becoming the most innovative and reliable energy company, we need a team with a variety of backgrounds, perspectives and skills. So, our goal is to be a diverse workforce that is representative of the communities we serve. We are committed to celebrating diversity and building a team where everyone – regardless of race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status – has a voice and can bring their best every day. We know that the more diverse and inclusive we are, the better we will be. Evergy is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. Disclaimer: The above information has been designed to indicate the general nature and level of work performed by employees within this classification. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications required of employees assigned to this job. Fri, 21 Aug 2026 15:28:13 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11334193/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11121230 Assistant Superintendent at D.R. Horton, Inc. Employer: D.R. Horton, Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n D.R. Horton, Inc., the largest homebuilder in the U.S., was founded in 1978 and is a publicly traded company on the New York Stock Exchange. It is engaged in the construction and sale of high quality homes designed principally for the entry-level and first time move-up markets. The Company also provides mortgage financing and title services for homebuyers through its mortgage and title subsidiaries. Please visit our website at www.drhorton.com for more information.D.R. Horton, Inc. is currently looking for a Assistant Superintendent. The right candidate will assists the Superintendent with the management of the community job site as it relates to home construction while providing excellent customer service.  This includes but is not limited to assisting in scheduling and supervising job site subcontractors, maintaining quality standards, cost management, homeowner walk-throughs, inspections, community maintenance and upkeep, and enforcing safety standards. Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following. Other duties may be assigned.Inspect each home daily to assure the quality of workmanship, ensure all work is in accordance with plans and specifications, determine the status as it compares to the production scheduleSchedule and walk all inspections with inspectorsWalk each completed home before the homeowner walk-through and closing sign-off to ensure the home is complete, clean, and meets standards of quality.  Note outstanding homeowner walk-through items and schedule repairsConduct homeowner orientation and any additional walks ensuring homeowner satisfactionAid Superintendent to ensure subcontractors are managed and continually evaluated on quality, safety, scheduling and cost control measuresEnforce the site safety program and ensure subcontractor compliance with company standards and all applicable safety codes and regulationsEnforce DR Horton cleanliness standards – Ensure communities and jobsites are free of trash & waste materials.Assist Superintendent in managing construction materials to help prevent damage, waste, & theftSupport the construction schedule and ensure the highest quality product is delivered on time and within budgetProvide a superior level of customer service during all phases of constructionDevelop and maintain positive relations with subcontractors and homeownersDevelop knowledge in building codes, construction materials, methodologies, terminology and construction schedulingIn absence of Superintendent, ensure all schedules, policies, and guidelines are maintainedConducts all business in a professional and ethical manner to serve customers and increase the goodwill and profit of the companyAbility to work overtimeAbility to work additional hours as necessary to meet business needs QualificationsEducation and/or ExperienceHigh school diploma or general education degree (GED)Six months to 2 years of related experienceMust have valid driver’s license and be willing to drive among construction sites in daytime and nighttimeStrong verbal and written communication skillsCommitment to customer satisfactionAbility to read plans and other construction documentsRequire minimum supervision and ability to create a systematic approach in carrying out assignmentsAbility to converse with customers, all levels of management and personnelAbility to utilize DRH Construction applications on a smart phone, tablet, or laptopProficiency with MS Office and emailAbility to lift and/or move up to 50 pounds Preferred QualificationsBachelor’s degree from a four-year college preferredAbility to work effectively in high pressure situations Come join a winning team with a Fortune 500 company! We are growing fast and are looking for enthusiastic attitudes and team players to join our success. We offer an excellent benefits package including:Medical, Dental and Vision401(K)Employee Stock Purchase PlanFlex Spending AccountsLife & Disability InsuranceVacation, Sick, Personal Time and Company HolidaysMultiple Voluntary and Company provided Benefits Build YOUR future with D.R. Horton, America’s Builder. #WeBuildPeopleToo Thu, 11 Jun 2026 18:55:42 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11121230/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11287735 Marine Aviation Officer at Officer Selection Team - United States Marine Corps Employer: Officer Selection Team - United States Marine Corps \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n THE CALL TO LEAD: OWN THE AIR, TAKE THE GROUNDThere is no better integration of air, ground, and logistics support assets into one unit than the Marine Air-Ground Task Force (MAGTF). In the Marine Corps, aviation missions are won by seizing and controlling the ground—and as a Marine Officer, this mission is under your command.Marine Aviation is unique in its ability to operate globally from amphibious platforms, forward operating bases, forward expeditionary land bases, or any combination thereof. We are seeking elite, determined college students and graduates who possess the character, physical stamina, and mental sharpness to lead Marines and pilot the world's most advanced combat aircraft. CORE AVIATION CAREER PATHS (MOS TYPES)As a Marine Aviation Officer, you can pursue diverse technical and leadership trajectories within the Aviation Combat Element (ACE):·       75XX: Pilot (Naval Aviator): Operate rotary-wing, tilt-rotor, or fixed-wing aircraft to deliver combat power and support to the MAGTF commander. Specialized platforms include: ·       Jets: F-35 Lightning II (5th Generation Multi-role Fighter), F/A-18 Hornet·       Helicopters: AH-1Z Viper, UH-1Y Venom, CH-53E/K Super Stallion/King Stallion·       Tilt-Rotor: MV-22 Osprey·       Multiengine: KC-130 HerculesTHE SIX ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF MARINE AVIATIONEvery mission you fly or support serves to deliver battlespace dominance through these six core capabilities:1.      Air Support: Delivering close air support to Marines fighting on the ground.2.      Assault Support: Providing tactical mobility, rapid insertion of ground units, and logistics.3.      Antiair Warfare: Gaining and maintaining air superiority over the battlefield.4.      Electronic Warfare: Exploiting, disrupting, and dominating the electromagnetic spectrum.5.      Aircraft and Missile Control: Directing, coordinating, and controlling air defense and tactical flights.6.      Aerial Reconnaissance: Collecting visual, electronic, and multisensor intelligence. THE BENEFITS OF MARINE CORPS AVIATIONA commission as a Marine Officer offers tangible and intangible rewards far exceeding civilian compensation, providing absolute financial security, advanced education, and a lifetime legacy of leadership.1. Financial Security & Compensation·       Competitive Base Pay & Allowances: Receive regular pay raises, regular cost-of-living increases, and tax-free allowances for housing (BAH) and food (BAS).·       Aviation Incentive Pay: Pilots receive specialized flight pay on top of standard military base salary, scaling with years of aviation service.·       Annual Uniform Allowance: Funding provided annually to maintain professional dress and utility uniforms.·       Retirement & Investment: Full eligibility for the Thrift Savings Plan (TSP) and attractive military retirement benefits.2. Tangible Quality-of-Life Benefits·       30 Days Paid Vacation: Receive 30 days of paid leave or vacation per year from day one.·       Comprehensive Healthcare: Complete medical and dental coverage for officers and their families at zero cost.·       Tax-Free Shopping: Access to the Marine Corps Base Exchange (MCX) and Base Commissary for tax-free goods and groceries.·       VA Home Loans: Eligibility for Veterans Administration Guaranteed Loans to purchase a home.·       Recreational Perks: Access to low-cost or free base recreational facilities, including gyms, swimming pools, private beaches, campgrounds, marinas, boat rentals, and rod and gun clubs.3. Fully Funded Higher Education & Career Growth·       Tuition Assistance Program (TAP): Covers 100 percent of tuition costs for part-time graduate or undergraduate coursework, up to $225 per credit and/or $4,500 per year.·       Advanced Degree Program (ADP): Attend graduate school full-time to earn a Master's degree while receiving regular Marine Officer pay and allowances.·       Special Education Program (SEP): Pursue advanced technical degrees in engineering, computer science, communications, and management at accredited institutions with full benefits.·       Fellowships: Opportunities to participate in elite fellowship programs (e.g., DARPA, White House Fellows, congressional staff, Tufts University Fletcher School).4. Travel, Global Adventure & Esprit de Corps·       Worldwide Deployment: Serve aboard Navy ships, operate from foreign bases, and experience diverse global cultures.·       Adventure Activities: Take advantage of base-sponsored adventure training, including rock climbing, parachuting, scuba diving, snow skiing, and deep-sea fishing.·       All-Marine Sports: Opportunities to compete on elite All-Marine sports teams (rugby, soccer, boxing, track, golf) with paths to interservice or Olympic competition. THE TRAINING PATHWAY: FROM CANDIDATE TO WINGSNo one is born a Marine Aviator; you are forged through the most demanding aviation training pipeline in the world:7.      Officer Selection & Commissioning (PLC / OCC):·       Platoon Leaders Class (PLC): For college freshmen, sophomores, and juniors. Complete training during summer breaks with no academic year obligations. Receive semester stipends and E-5 pay while at training.·       Officer Candidate Course (OCC): For college seniors and graduates. A single intensive 10-week program in Quantico, VA.8.      Officer Candidates School (OCS) (Quantico, VA): Evaluated on leadership, academics, and physical fitness under the motto Ductus Exemplo (\"Lead by Example\").9.      The Basic School (TBS) (Quantico, VA - 6 months): Master the skills of a provisional rifle platoon commander, ensuring every Marine Officer is a combat leader first.10.  Aviation Preflight Indoctrination (API) (Pensacola, FL - 6 weeks): Rigorous ground school covering aerodynamics, navigation, engine systems, land/water survival, and flight physiology.11.  Primary Flight Training (Pensacola, FL / Corpus Christi, TX - 5 months): Take the controls of the T-6B Texan turboprop trainer, learning basic flight instruments, aerobatics, and formation flying.12.  Platform Selection & Advanced Flight Training: Based on performance and the needs of the Marine Corps, candidates are assigned to their final platforms:·       Fixed-Wing Pipeline: Learn advanced jet tactics at NAS Meridian, MS (10 months) before transitioning to F-35s or F/A-18s.·       Helicopter/Tilt-Rotor Pipeline: Train at NAS Whiting Field, FL (6 months) in rotary-wing/tilt-rotor flight before transitioning to AH-1Z, UH-1Y, CH-53, or MV-22 platforms.13.  Fleet Replacement Squadron (FRS) & Fleet Assignment: Spend 6–8 months mastering your specific combat aircraft before joining an operational squadron deployed worldwide. ELIGIBILITY & SELECTION CRITERIA·       Education: Must be a U.S. citizen currently enrolled in or graduated from an accredited college or university, maintaining a GPA of \"C\" or better.·       Aptitude: Achieve qualifying scores on the Aviation Selection Test Battery (ASTB). You must also have an ACT of 22, an SAT of 100 (math and critical reading combined), or ASVAB of 74.·       Physical Fitness: Maintain exceptional physical standards. Candidates must pass the Marine Corps Physical Fitness Test (PFT) with these OCS entry minimums:·       Males: 8 pull-ups, a timed plank (minimum 1:03), and a 3-mile run in under 24:00.·       Females: 1 pull-up, a timed plank (minimum 1:03), and a 3-mile run in under 27:00.·       Note: Stronger competitive scores (such as a 235+ overall PFT score) are highly recommended for selection.·       Medical & Moral Screening: Must pass a comprehensive military aviation flight physical and background screening. HOW TO APPLYEarning a commission as a Marine Officer starts with a conversation. Contact your local Officer Selection Officer (OSO) to begin the screening process, schedule your physical and ASTB tests, and secure your slot in the Platoon Leaders Class or Officer Candidate Course.Contact the Officer Selections Officer, Captain Brandon T. Jackson at brandon.jackson@usmc.marines.mil Mon, 10 Aug 2026 01:57:35 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11287735/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11121241 Assistant Superintendent at D.R. Horton, Inc. Employer: D.R. Horton, Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n D.R. Horton, Inc., the largest homebuilder in the U.S., was founded in 1978 and is a publicly traded company on the New York Stock Exchange. It is engaged in the construction and sale of high quality homes designed principally for the entry-level and first time move-up markets. The Company also provides mortgage financing and title services for homebuyers through its mortgage and title subsidiaries. Please visit our website at www.drhorton.com for more information.D.R. Horton, Inc. is currently looking for a Assistant Superintendent. The right candidate will assists the Superintendent with the management of the community job site as it relates to home construction while providing excellent customer service.  This includes but is not limited to assisting in scheduling and supervising job site subcontractors, maintaining quality standards, cost management, homeowner walk-throughs, inspections, community maintenance and upkeep, and enforcing safety standards. Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following. Other duties may be assigned.Inspect each home daily to assure the quality of workmanship, ensure all work is in accordance with plans and specifications, determine the status as it compares to the production scheduleSchedule and walk all inspections with inspectorsWalk each completed home before the homeowner walk-through and closing sign-off to ensure the home is complete, clean, and meets standards of quality.  Note outstanding homeowner walk-through items and schedule repairsConduct homeowner orientation and any additional walks ensuring homeowner satisfactionAid Superintendent to ensure subcontractors are managed and continually evaluated on quality, safety, scheduling and cost control measuresEnforce the site safety program and ensure subcontractor compliance with company standards and all applicable safety codes and regulationsEnforce DR Horton cleanliness standards – Ensure communities and jobsites are free of trash & waste materials.Assist Superintendent in managing construction materials to help prevent damage, waste, & theftSupport the construction schedule and ensure the highest quality product is delivered on time and within budgetProvide a superior level of customer service during all phases of constructionDevelop and maintain positive relations with subcontractors and homeownersDevelop knowledge in building codes, construction materials, methodologies, terminology and construction schedulingIn absence of Superintendent, ensure all schedules, policies, and guidelines are maintainedConducts all business in a professional and ethical manner to serve customers and increase the goodwill and profit of the companyAbility to work overtimeAbility to work additional hours as necessary to meet business needs QualificationsEducation and/or ExperienceHigh school diploma or general education degree (GED)Six months to 2 years of related experienceMust have valid driver’s license and be willing to drive among construction sites in daytime and nighttimeStrong verbal and written communication skillsCommitment to customer satisfactionAbility to read plans and other construction documentsRequire minimum supervision and ability to create a systematic approach in carrying out assignmentsAbility to converse with customers, all levels of management and personnelAbility to utilize DRH Construction applications on a smart phone, tablet, or laptopProficiency with MS Office and emailAbility to lift and/or move up to 50 pounds Preferred QualificationsBachelor’s degree from a four-year college preferredAbility to work effectively in high pressure situations Come join a winning team with a Fortune 500 company! We are growing fast and are looking for enthusiastic attitudes and team players to join our success. We offer an excellent benefits package including:Medical, Dental and Vision401(K)Employee Stock Purchase PlanFlex Spending AccountsLife & Disability InsuranceVacation, Sick, Personal Time and Company HolidaysMultiple Voluntary and Company provided Benefits Build YOUR future with D.R. Horton, America’s Builder. #WeBuildPeopleToo Thu, 11 Jun 2026 19:05:36 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11121241/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11287409 Professional Softwares Sales (SaaS)- Highly Compensated, 100% Commission-Uncapped, 1099 at Mecherath, LLC Employer: Mecherath, LLC \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n THIS IS A 1099 LONG TERM, 100% Commission Highly Compensated-Uncapped Sales, Remote Position***Please read the entire job description; if this is not you, please save both of us time; it is ok if we are not the right fit for each other.***Additionally, this is NOT a ghost position and WE DO NOT USE AI. Each resume is personally reviewed and considered.***If you don't have any sales experience, are coming from a completely different field, I want you to explain why you are interested in this role. Hiring@Mecherath.com, or most likely based on experience with Handshake, we will move on.You are one of the following:1. A recent or soon-to-be college graduate interested in higher-income SaaS sales2. Experienced Account Manager/Development Representative/BDR who is ready for sales3. Experienced top producer, a self-driven sales executive looking to leverage your earning skills and build a long-term career.You have to be the person who understands and will follow up with each contact every other day, or you won't get the sale; it is a process.You must have the ability to build relationships and trust in the first 5 minutes, understand sales is a process, and know how to close!Qualified leads are provided. Your role is to sell. (not train or support; we have people)You must have outstanding follow-up and organizational skills. You are a self-starter with exceptional phone skills who doesn't have the word no in your vocabulary. You have proven you can work successfully without supervision by setting your hours and work commitments.You are a highly motivated consultant, mentor, and trusted advisor, which requires strong questioning and listening skills. You have successfully identified, connected with, and sold to business owners, presidents, and CEOs in a sales cycle.You are a fast learner who loves hands-off professional support with exceptional training, continual support, mentoring, coaching, and accountability. A plus, but not necessary, is personal and professional experience within the construction industry, business management tools, architecture, trades, and project controls. You have consistently achieved selling success in the B2B environment, earning more than $80K a year with a heavily commissioned comp plan. We'll help you get going, but you can't wait to get paid what your skills are worth! Must be a US legal resident.Responsibilities:Cold call 60-80 calls per day and follow up each call with a template emailThis is a 40 hour per week positionClose Deals and earn commissions; uncapped earning potential sales, with quarterly and year-end bonusesPrioritize and target prospects by the potential for revenue, cost to sell, and the probability of success. Use our CRM in Mecherath and keep records updated.Continually upgrade product knowledge and acquire enhanced selling skills.Your only role is to sell—training and support handled by other professionals within our company. Followup is wise to acquire additional leads.You set your hours and work remotely but must excel at the commitment.You understand this is not a position where you will make money in your first month, but the goal and possible high-level income are worth the effort.Qualifications:Recent college grad or experienced sales professionalProfessional cold-calling experience, excellent follow-up, and organizational skillsConsultative selling skills: we provide a solution, not a productSolution-based selling (we will provide training to improve your skills)Responsible, accountable, and looking to growYou are seeking a career, not looking for a jobAbsolute honesty and integrity. It's not just a saying; we live by it throughout the company.Required to live and legally reside in the US.Mecherath Benefits:You are seeking a career, not looking for a job.Absolute honesty and integrity are who you are and the company you want to work for.An excellent training program and support with ongoing sales meetings,Unlimited Earning Potential (no caps)Independence: Set your hours, but have to work-40 hours per week.Understand that 100% commission is where your highest earning potential is realized.Work with a company that understands and practices professional leadership. We train you well, support you, and let you work independently.Long-term with room to advance Sun, 9 Aug 2026 09:45:43 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11287409/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11121111 Superintendent at D.R. Horton, Inc. Employer: D.R. Horton, Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n D.R. Horton, Inc., the largest homebuilder in the U.S., was founded in 1978 and is a publicly traded company on the New York Stock Exchange. It is engaged in the construction and sale of high quality homes designed principally for the entry-level and first time move-up markets. The Company also provides mortgage financing and title services for homebuyers through its mortgage and title subsidiaries. Please visit our website at www.drhorton.com for more information.D.R. Horton, Inc.is currently looking for a Superintendent. The right candidate's primary responsibility is to manage all functions of the job site as it relates to home construction while providing excellent customer service. The Superintendent manages the construction of multiple homes from permit to closing by scheduling and supervising job site subcontractors, homeowner walk-throughs, and inspections while maintaining company construction and safety standards. Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following. Other duties may be assigned.Manage the construction schedule and ensure the highest quality product is delivered on time and within budgetSchedule all involved subcontractors for each phase of construction and evaluate the quality and efficiency of their work to ensure work complies with local, state and federal building code requirements and company standards of workmanshipComplete each home site on schedule from planning through occupancy, ensuring all contract obligations are satisfiedInspect and determine subcontractor’s workmanship and product quality is completed on time and within defined scope of work.  Halt any work that is not satisfactory or noncompliant with plans, specifications, or applicable codeAuthorize payment of subcontractors when all standards are met and upon thorough inspection of work completed and for materials receivedManage the customer experience throughout the entire construction process.  Recognize and enforce quality standards through daily inspection of homes under construction.  Conduct homeowner orientation and walks, provide regular communications regarding progress and address concernsMonitor community cleanliness and ensure the community and worksite is clean, orderly and visually appealing during constructionManage the post-close process for warranty.  Assess warranty requests, determine course of action, schedule subcontractors, and manage quality assuranceFollow up with homeowners to ensure concerns are addressed in a timely and professional mannerMaintain a current working knowledge of all applicable building codesWork closely with the sales, customer warranty, and management team to ensure open communication on all matters; develop a strong environment conducive to proactive resolution of issues and strong commitment to producing a quality productConducts all business in a professional and ethical manner to serve customers and increase the goodwill and profit of the companyAbility to work additional hours as necessary to meet business needs QualificationsEducation and/or ExperienceHigh school diploma or general education degree (GED)Two to four years related experienceAbility to manage and complete the “13 Milestones of Construction” specified in JDEMust have a vehicle capable of carrying supplies, valid driver’s license and be willing to drive among designated communities in daytime and nighttimeAbility to read and interpret construction documents, drawings, specifications, scopes of work and knowledge of all phases of new homes constructionGeneral knowledge of municipal permitting, regulations and building codesAbility to converse with customers, all levels of management and personnelSuperb interpersonal, verbal and written communication skillsDemonstrated commitment to customer satisfactionAbility to control cost overruns and manage a budgetAbility to utilize DRH Construction applications on a smart phone, tablet, or laptopAbility to apply common sense understanding to carry out instructions furnished in written, oral form or via DRH Construction applicationsProficiency with MS Office and emailAbility to stand and walk for 4 hours straight or up to a full 8-hour day; sit for extended periods; kneel and bend at the waist; climb, balance and stoop, crouch or crawl; walk up and down stairs; walk on unlevel terrain; use hands and fingers to handle or feel; reach with hands and arms; talk and hear.  Ability to lift and/or move up to 50 pounds.  Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, color vision and peripheral visionRegular exposure to outside weather conditions, moving mechanical parts, high precarious places and risk of electrical shockThe noise level is generally loud Preferred QualificationsBachelor’s degree from a four-year college a plusWork effectively in a high pressure and high production environment Come join a winning team with a Fortune 500 company! We are growing fast and are looking for enthusiastic attitudes and team players to join our success. We offer an excellent benefits package including:Medical, Dental and Vision401(K)Employee Stock Purchase PlanFlex Spending AccountsLife & Disability InsuranceVacation, Sick, Personal Time and Company HolidaysMultiple Voluntary and Company provided Benefits Build YOUR future with D.R. Horton, America’s Builder. #WeBuildPeopleToo Thu, 11 Jun 2026 18:25:39 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11121111/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11288732 Staff Accountant at Dahm, Knapp & Associates, PC Employer: Dahm, Knapp & Associates, PC \n\n Expires: 09/09/2026 \n\n Company DescriptionDahm, Knapp & Associates, PC is dedicated to creating opportunities for our clients by delivering exceptional assurance, tax, advisory, and other financial services. Driven by a commitment to excellence and backed by over 40 years of industry expertise, we take pride in exceeding expectations and building long-term client relationships. O