    "https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11334143/share_preview": {
      "title": "Venture and Program Support Intern",
      "description": "Venture and Program Support Intern | UTEP Woody L. Hunt College of Business Dean's Office | Handshake Home Learn More Help You are viewing a preview of this job. Log in or register to view more details about this job. Venture and Program Support Intern UTEP Woody L. Hunt College of Business Dean's Office Tweet Email Partnership Overview This internship is a joint initiative between Pioneers 21 and the Woody L. Hunt College of Business's HUNT G.O. Foundry for Entrepreneurship at The University of Texas at El Paso (UTEP). The position is hosted and supervised day-to-day at Pioneers 21, with the G.O. Foundry co-sponsoring 50% of the intern's wages as part of its commitment to giving UTEP students hands-on experience in the regional startup ecosystem. Position Details Position Title: Venture & Program Support Intern Host Organization: Pioneers 21 Co-Sponsor: HUNT G.O. Foundry for Entrepreneurship, UTEP Woody L. Hunt College of Business Location: El Paso, TX — In-person Schedule: 20 hours/week, Part-Time Term: Fall 2026: September 7 – December 18, 2026 Compensation: $20/hr — 50% Pioneers 21 / 50% G.O. Foundry Reports To: Laura Butler, Executive Director, Pioneers 21 About Pioneers 21 Pioneers 21 is a nonprofit innovation hub and business incubator dedicated to inspiring and incubating businesses and entrepreneurs through mentorship, training, and connection. Since 2011, Pioneers 21 has helped innovators transform ideas into growing companies through access to experienced mentors, educational programming, strategic partnerships, and pathways to capital — including initiatives such as EDGE, Manufacturing EDGE, CapitalEdge, and the P21 Venture Mentoring Service (licensed by MIT). About the HUNT G.O. Foundry The G.O. Foundry for Entrepreneurship is UTEP's home for experiential entrepreneurship education, connecting students to real venture-building experience through speaker series, workshops, and partnerships across the U.S.-Mexico border region. This internship is part of the Foundry's effort to place students directly inside the regional startup ecosystem. Position Summary The Intern will support Pioneers 21's accelerator programs and venture-support initiatives — working directly with founders, mentors, and internal teams to execute programs, track venture progress, and improve operational systems. The role blends administrative and operational support with direct exposure to startup ecosystems, venture development, and innovation operations. Primary Responsibilities Program & Venture Support Assist with planning, coordination, and delivery of accelerator programs, workshops, and special events Support participant registration, onboarding, scheduling, and communications Coordinate logistics for speakers, mentors, instructors, and community partners Track venture progress, milestones, and outcomes across programs Assist with pitch preparation, business model refinement, and market research Maintain attendance records, participant files, and program documentation Funding Research & Administrative Support Research grant, sponsorship, and funding opportunities aligned with organizational priorities Maintain funding calendars, deadlines, and opportunity trackers Assist in gathering information and supporting documents for grant proposals and reports Marketing & Ecosystem Engagement Assist with marketing accelerator programs, workshops, and events Create and schedule social media content and email communications Support outreach efforts with entrepreneurs, community partners, and stakeholders Operations & Technology Maintain internal documentation, databases, and CRM records Contribute to projects involving AI tools, digital enablement, and process improvement Support day-to-day office operations and special projects Qualifications Required Juniors and Seniors currently enrolled as undergraduate business majors at UTEP Valid U.S. work authorization Strong organizational, research, and written/verbal communication skills Ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment Proficiency with Microsoft Office / Google Workspace Preferred Coursework or experience in business, entrepreneurship, marketing, or a related field Familiarity with startups, venture capital, or small business development Experience with AI tools, CRM systems, project management platforms, or Canva Bilingual (English/Spanish) Learning Outcomes Practical experience supporting real ventures and founders Direct exposure to venture mentoring, startup operations, and innovation programs Development of professional skills in research, analysis, funding, and execution Mentorship from experienced operators and Borderland ecosystem leaders Submit your application Please submit your application by August 31st through the link below: Pioneers 21 × UTEP G.O. Foundry We'll conduct interviews during the first week of September to match a start date of September 7th, 2026."
    },
    "https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11289597/share_preview": {
      "title": "Campus Marketing & Community Intern — End of Summer/Fall",
      "description": "Campus Marketing & Community Intern — End of Summer/Fall | MTR Beauty Collective, LLC. | Handshake Home Learn More Help You are viewing a preview of this job. Log in or register to view more details about this job. Campus Marketing & Community Intern — End of Summer/Fall MTR Beauty Collective, LLC. Tweet Email MTR Beauty Collective is building the next generation of beauty brands. We acquire beauty brands with strong heritage, exceptional products, and untapped potential, then work across brand, marketing, creative, digital, retail, and operations to reimagine them for today's consumer. Our first major acquisition is Deborah Lippmann, which we have relaunched as LIPPMANN. We're building on more than 25 years of expertise while introducing the brand to a new generation of consumers. And we're just getting started. As MTR Beauty Collective grows, our goal is to acquire, develop, and scale additional beauty businesses. This internship is an opportunity to join a small, entrepreneurial team and get firsthand experience building a beauty brand from the inside. About LIPPMANN LIPPMANN is the original care-first nail brand, since 1999. We believe healthy nails are beautiful nails, and we create the ritual that gets you there. Built on Deborah Lippmann's decades of expertise as a celebrity manicurist, LIPPMANN combines professional performance with a care-first approach to nail health. The brand is built around three core pillars: Care Without Compromise Beautiful color should never come at the expense of nail health. Every LIPPMANN formula is thoughtfully developed to deliver professional performance while supporting stronger, healthier nails through cleaner, treatment-driven ingredients. Built on Expertise For more than 25 years, Deborah Lippmann has helped redefine what nail care can be through professional expertise, cleaner formulations, treatment-driven innovation, and a care-first philosophy. Capsule Colors We create colors with longevity, not urgency. Every shade is thoughtfully developed to become a lasting part of your beauty wardrobe: timeless, wearable, and beautifully performed. The Role We're looking for a creative, socially connected college senior who can help us introduce LIPPMANN to the next generation of consumers. You'll serve as a bridge between our team and college culture, helping us understand what's resonating with your generation, identify the right people and communities to connect with, and develop creative ways to get students genuinely excited about the brand. This is not an internship where you'll spend the semester watching from the sidelines. We want your perspective, and your ideas. What You'll Work On Campus Outreach & Partnerships Identify and connect with Greek life, student organizations, clubs, campus publications, events, creators, and other communities where LIPPMANN could naturally show up. Community & Ambassador Building Help identify students, creators, campus ambassadors, and brand advocates who could introduce LIPPMANN to their communities. Events & Activations Brainstorm and help execute sampling, gifting, campus events, partnerships, pop-ups, and other creative ways for students to experience the brand. Gen Z Consumer Insights Help us understand what your peers are buying, watching, sharing, talking about, and responding to, and what brands are getting it right or wrong. Social & Content Contribute ideas for TikTok, Instagram, UGC, creator partnerships, trends, and social-first campaigns. Outreach & Communication Help develop thoughtful outreach to campus organizations, creators, potential ambassadors, partners, and other contacts. Brand Building Participate in conversations about how we position, market, and grow LIPPMANN with a younger consumer. You'll also have exposure to the broader work happening at MTR Beauty Collective , giving you a firsthand look at how beauty brands are acquired, repositioned, marketed, and scaled. Who We're Looking For We're especially interested in a current college senior who is: Highly connected to campus life and naturally knows what's happening around them Active in Greek life, student organizations, clubs, athletics, campus media, events, or other student communities Interested in beauty, fashion, wellness, lifestyle, marketing, entrepreneurship, or consumer brands Deeply familiar with TikTok, Instagram, creators, and internet culture Able to recognize what makes people their age genuinely care about a brand A strong writer and natural communicator Comfortable reaching out to new people and building relationships Organized and self-motivated enough to thrive in a remote role Creative, curious, and willing to bring ideas to the table Excited by an entrepreneurial environment where things move quickly and your work has a visible impact Previous beauty-industry experience is not required. We're much more interested in your instincts, initiative, understanding of your peers, and ability to turn an idea into something real. More Than an Internship We're intentionally looking for a senior because we'd love for this role to become something more. MTR Beauty Collective is growing beyond LIPPMANN, and we're interested in finding talented people who want to grow alongside us. You'll have the opportunity to work directly with a small team, take ownership of meaningful projects, and learn how emerging and established beauty businesses are built. For the right person, this internship could lead to continued work during the school year and consideration for a full-time position with MTR Beauty Collective after graduation, with the opportunity to help us grow LIPPMANN and future brands in our portfolio. We're not simply looking for someone to complete an internship. We're hoping to find someone we want to keep"
    },
    "https://wheatoncollege.edu/news/eye-opening-internships/": {
      "title": "Wheaton News",
      "description": "Eye-opening internships - Wheaton College Massachusetts Skip to main content Skip to main content Navigation menu Alumni Athletics Giving Parents & Families insideWheaton Visit Get Info Apply Give Now Academics Academics Academic Calendar Accreditation Academic Advising College Catalog Departments Faculty Directory Global Education Library Life and Career Design Institute Programs Projects & Initiatives Provost Summer Session The Wheaton Curriculum Winter Session Admission Admission Admitted Students Applying to Wheaton Scholarships Information for Counselors International Students Meet the Admission Staff Picture #WheatonMA Transfer Students Tuition & Fees Visiting Wheaton Campus Life Campus Life Athletics and Recreation Clubs & Organizations Dean of Students First Year Resources Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Marshall Center Safety on Campus Wheaton Orientation Programs About Wheaton About Wheaton Campus & Community Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging History & Traditions Honor Code Mission and Vision Offices & Services Outcomes & Impact President & College Leadership Sustainability Facts and Figures The Wheaton Edge Working at Wheaton Search What can we help you find? type keywords here Search Visit Wheaton Learn about how and when you can visit our campus Request Info Receive announcements and materials based upon your academic interests. Apply Now Ready to apply? Check out our requirements and deadlines. × Visit Get Info Apply Give Now Wheaton News Back to all news articles Eye-opening internships August 26, 2026 Experiential Student Justing Zhirzhan ’27 meets with a coworker at the Massachusetts State Lottery during his internship in the marketing department. (Photo by Keith Nordstrom) Wheaton-funded internships helped students apply classroom learning, build professional skills and make valuable connections. “Wheaton opened my eyes to explore more things,” Justin Zhirzhan ’27 said. “If you come in with an open mind, faculty and staff will help you find your path.” Zhirzhan and more than 100 other Wheaton College students gained professional experience during the summer through college-funded internships with businesses, nonprofits, government agencies and sports organizations across the country. The opportunities reflected students’ wide-ranging interests and career goals. Some worked in professional and collegiate sports, including internships with Rhode Island’s professional soccer team and Cape Cod Baseball League organizations. Others explored careers in law and public service from district courts to health care. Here are a few of their stories: Brown Health Pain Clinic – Ashley Almeida ’27, nursing Charles M. Schulz Museum and Research Center – Sid Chapin ’27, European history and visual art Boston Children’s Hospital – Maggie Cizmar ’28, psychology Office of Maryann Lehmann, DDS – Thomas Corridon ’28, biology Maple Hill Disc Golf Course – Aud Dodge ’27, marketing and neuroscience Massachusetts State Lottery – Justin Zhirzhan ’27, business and management Wheaton offers students the opportunity to access funding for an unpaid internship before their junior or senior year through the Life and Career Design Institute . The support ensures that students can pursue meaningful opportunities, including positions that might otherwise be financially out of reach. The experience also gives students an opportunity to test possible career paths, learn from professionals in their fields and return to campus with new skills, knowledge and confidence. Contact Troy Watkins watkins_troy@wheatoncollege.edu Related Links From economics to dentistry Aug 26, 2026 Marketing the Lottery Aug 26, 2026 Related Topics Experiential Student Scroll to Top Wheaton College - Massachusetts 26 E. Main Street Norton, MA 02766 508-286-8200 Arts Directions Map News Blog Magazine Academic Calendar Events Calendar Bookstore Emergency Information Working at Wheaton Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Facebook LinkedIN Instagram TikTok YouTube © 2026 Wheaton College (MA) Accessibility Consumer Disclosures Contact Wheaton Policies Privacy Policy Title IX Website Feedback"
    }
  },
